msgstr ""

#: answer/f971efd1-b0a5-4bc5-829d-148ef9362d37/advice
msgid "Information about resources for human assays is available on the [RDMkit Toxicology page – human assays](https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/toxicology_data#data-from-human-assays---existing-data-and-vocabularies), for animal assays on the [RDMkit Toxicology page – animal assays](https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/toxicology_data#data-from-animal-assays---existing-data-and-vocabularies), and for ecotoxicology on the [RDMkit Toxicology page – ecotoxicology](https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/toxicology_data#ecotoxicology-data---existing-data)."
msgstr ""

#: reference/e5762c40-7b10-4915-89f8-c71180049f13/label
msgid "RDMkit on Toxicology"
msgstr "RDMkit 中的毒理學"

#: question/17464e0f-f477-4a45-a556-687a97b0e826/title
msgid "Will you need existing data from Agricultural Sciences?"
msgstr ""

#: question/b19eab58-3b7f-4b66-b6f2-7e9c2c3c3e27/title
msgid "Will you need existing data from Social Sciences?"
msgstr ""

#: question/849cb43b-8622-4da0-9ef3-ae845dfe58f1/title
msgid "Will you need existing data from Humanities?"
msgstr ""

#: question/efc80cc8-8318-4f8c-acb7-dc1c60e491c1/title
msgid "Is there any pre-existing data?"
msgstr "是否有可用的既有資料？"

#: question/efc80cc8-8318-4f8c-acb7-dc1c60e491c1/text
msgid "Are there any data sets available in the world that are relevant to your planned research?"
msgstr "世界上是否存在任何與您計畫中的研究相關的可用資料集？"

#: answer/72cdbc99-2707-4817-ac40-435a03e5e837/advice
msgid "It is possible that you have overlooked existing data! This question is not only about data sets that are similar to what you want to determine yourself, but also reference data or data that should be mined from the existing literature. Further, it is very likely that you will refer to related data, e.g. other databases where you usually \"quickly look something up\", but that could maybe be properly integrated, especially if you need to do such lookups multiple times."
msgstr "也許還有一些既有資料尚未納入考量。這個問題不只是在問是否有與您想自行產生的資料相似的資料集，也包括參考資料，或是可從既有文獻中擷取的資料。此外，您也可能會用到相關資料，例如平常會「快速查一下」的其他資料庫；如果這類查詢會反覆進行，也許可以考慮將這些資料更妥善地整合進研究流程。"

#: question/fcc51962-08df-4f4c-85ad-6bb932107010/title
msgid "What existing openly available standard reference data did you consider re-using?"
msgstr "您考慮再次使用哪些公開可取得的既有標準參考資料？"

#: question/fcc51962-08df-4f4c-85ad-6bb932107010/text
msgid "Much of todays data is used in comparison with reference data. You may be comparing your own data with a \"standard set\" which is maintained as a collection by someone else. Or you could be determining differences to a standard (for example in bioinformatics, a genome is often compared with a reference genome to identify genomic variants). If you use reference data, there are several specific issues that you should consider. What are the reference data sets that you will use?"
msgstr "現今許多資料都會與參考資料進行比較。您可能會將自己的資料與他人維護的「標準資料集」進行比較；也可能會判定資料相對於某項標準的差異（例如在生物資訊學中，常會將基因組與參考基因組比較，以辨識基因組變異）。如果您使用參考資料，有幾項特定議題需要考量。您將使用哪些參考資料集？"

#: question/3b769dce-a88f-4339-a0f3-641d0ba22932/title
msgid "Reference data set"
msgstr "參考資料集"

#: question/3b769dce-a88f-4339-a0f3-641d0ba22932/text
msgid "Provide the name of the dataset."
msgstr "請提供資料集名稱。"

#: question/7801fe70-a2ac-432b-9470-e326646c249f/title
msgid "Provide PID for this reference data set"
msgstr "請提供此參考資料集的持續識別碼 (PID)"

#: question/7801fe70-a2ac-432b-9470-e326646c249f/text
msgid "Specify a persistent identifier (e.g., a DOI) or a URL for the dataset. If possible, refer exactly to the version that you are using."
msgstr "請指定此參考資料集的持續識別碼 (PID)，例如數位物件識別碼 (DOI)，或提供網址。若可行，請精確指向您使用的版本。"

#: question/58401091-2d48-4231-983a-c972d11d9f6e/title
msgid "Will you be using this reference data set?"
msgstr "您是否會使用此參考資料集？"

#: question/d45ad247-19d4-4919-9a6c-094f696168b6/title
msgid "Why did you decide not to use this reference data set?"
msgstr "為什麼決定不使用此參考資料集？"

#: answer/ebfabb9b-c63b-493e-86a7-9335f29f4006/label
#: answer/c03a5e73-a56d-4737-9f3c-f064b51495c8/label
msgid "It misses data we need"
msgstr "缺少我們需要的資料"

#: answer/d961bef5-234d-49c2-9025-ff3f26e3dc8b/label
#: answer/2d28fbe5-3984-42be-a29e-38a7a72103a3/label
msgid "It misses required aspects"
msgstr "資料缺少必要內容"

#: answer/e2709f59-e656-4264-bf56-47d1a78d40b3/label
#: answer/f3e1e0fc-4ae0-436a-9c6b-5001eb69191b/label
msgid "It is not of sufficient quality"
msgstr "資料品質不夠好"

#: answer/a5515ccb-d529-41dd-b5f5-50b242cf67cf/label
#: answer/88ae749b-9736-46b7-b6af-24e77f3ba481/label
msgid "Its conditions of use do not allow us to use it"
msgstr "其使用條件不允許我們使用"

#: answer/b79d5eac-28be-4b6d-8d71-b7cbf43c27bf/label
#: answer/5c244adb-3a88-402f-aaf7-afac0480f39e/label
msgid "There is another reason"
msgstr "另有其他原因"

#: question/fa591173-c9e5-426f-8bee-6e6082108169/title
msgid "Please specify the reason why you will not be using this reference data"
msgstr "請具體說明您將不使用此參考資料的原因"

#: question/0d9fc7c6-f1eb-4b18-9e38-7e46c28aacb4/title
msgid "Name and contact details of the owner of this data"
msgstr "此資料擁有者的姓名與聯絡資訊"

#: question/aee03da5-b399-4274-8db4-fac82c6210d3/title
msgid "What are the conditions of use for this database or dataset?"
msgstr "此資料庫或資料集有哪些使用條件？"

#: question/aee03da5-b399-4274-8db4-fac82c6210d3/text
#: question/69999c2c-2710-480e-b8ac-8a8fc6f582e5/text
msgid ""
"Although there is no world-wide rule for the application of copyright on data sets (copyright only applies to things that require a so-called \"creative step\"), it is wise to check for an explicit permission to use a data set and not to assume that data can be used freely just because you can access it. \n"
"Note that copyright laws explicitly *forbid* the use of a copyrighted work, *except* if you get permission. Such a permission is called a \"licence\". So: if you can not find a licence, you have to assume you can not use the data."
msgstr ""
"儘管在資料集著作權的適用上並沒有全球一致的規範（著作權僅適用於需要所謂「創作性步驟」的內容），但在使用前，確認資料集是否有明確的使用授權仍是明智之舉，不應因為資料可以被取用，就假設可以自由使用。\n"
"請注意，著作權法明確*禁止*使用受著作權保護的作品，*除非*您已取得許可。這類許可稱為「授權條款」。因此，如果您找不到授權條款，就必須假定您不能使用該資料。"

#: answer/de5d31e0-dadb-422b-bd88-34f006f11d60/label
#: answer/cb713607-cd09-41b5-bd6a-bd403e584be6/label
msgid "They are freely available for any use (public domain or CC0)"
msgstr "這些資料可供任何用途自由使用，例如公眾領域或 CC0"

#: answer/180bb426-9ebe-4210-b307-eaeb1be12c0e/label
#: answer/a278ac17-732d-4fa7-a194-683da6013401/label
msgid "They are freely available with obligation to quote the source (e.g. CC-BY)"
msgstr "這些資料可自由使用，但必須標明來源，例如 CC-BY"

#: answer/85dcd5ee-002b-4db7-a0de-241a4b2f0688/label
#: answer/97dc091d-8103-4119-87a2-c46a277ea303/label
msgid "They are available under some restrictions, which we will follow in our project"
msgstr "這些資料可在某些限制下使用，而我們會在計畫中遵守這些限制"

#: question/dce3e924-717a-4b50-bdac-1b247e9ac18a/title
#: question/283abe36-207b-42c3-8d8e-ec9343d6f6fd/title
#: question/30426255-b153-4f3e-bf20-f13573160a64/title
msgid "What conditions?"
msgstr "哪些條件？"

#: question/dce3e924-717a-4b50-bdac-1b247e9ac18a/text
#: question/283abe36-207b-42c3-8d8e-ec9343d6f6fd/text
msgid "Please describe the conditions."
msgstr "請說明相關條件。"

#: reference/720e0101-8b99-438b-a6e5-8ae9386c7b0c/label
#: reference/81667fbe-dd42-4b28-a956-66a31f064e38/label
msgid "Wikipedia on Copyright"
msgstr "Wikipedia 的著作權頁面"

#: question/7b8c75c0-8d5c-4fde-9898-ded8b91f7f1f/title
#: question/588e3c1f-e9fd-411f-954e-f7a9b1cff1de/title
msgid "Can you use the data in a format that is available?"
msgstr "您是否能使用目前可取得的資料格式？"

#: question/7b8c75c0-8d5c-4fde-9898-ded8b91f7f1f/text
msgid "Do you know the data format of the reference data? Is this suitable for your work? Does it need to be converted?"
msgstr "您是否清楚參考資料的資料格式？該格式是否適合您的作業？是否需要轉檔？"

#: answer/2c2a9b84-b140-4e17-8026-56d5372064d0/label
#: answer/4831f187-8660-4641-9a32-a6f4f569614f/label
msgid "I can directly use it"
msgstr "可以直接使用"

#: answer/9de86d7b-9c60-47d6-8cb1-bfca13d6f619/label
#: answer/3da33836-eff3-4166-898b-3c2c3d3989a8/label
msgid "I need to convert it before using"
msgstr "使用前需要轉換格式"

#: question/10b6548c-21cd-44c8-a8de-47415e7b012e/title
msgid "Is the reference database or dataset versioned?"
msgstr "參考資料庫或資料集是否有版本控制？"

#: question/10b6548c-21cd-44c8-a8de-47415e7b012e/text
msgid "Many reference datasets and databases evolve over time. If the reference data changes, this may affect your results. If different versions of a reference data exist, you need to establish your \"version policy\"."
msgstr "許多參考資料集和資料庫會隨時間演變。如果參考資料有所變動，可能會影響您的研究結果。如果參考資料有不同版本，您需要訂定自己的「版本政策」。"

#: question/f00a28fb-ac77-4110-b285-c73c8bc62630/title
msgid "Which version will you use?"
msgstr "您將使用哪個版本？"

#: question/f00a28fb-ac77-4110-b285-c73c8bc62630/text
msgid "If there are different versions available, you have to decide with all project partners together which version you will be using. Probably you will go for the latest release as of the date of the start of your research project. However, if you have other data from older projects that need to be merged, you may need to consider using the same release you used for a previous project."
msgstr "如果有不同版本可供選擇，您需要與所有計畫合作夥伴共同決定要使用哪個版本。一般而言，您可能會選擇研究計畫開始日期當時可取得的最新釋出版本。不過，如果您需要合併較早計畫的資料，可能需要考慮沿用先前計畫所使用的同一版本。"

#: question/481d0157-6d89-4f68-9f3b-cf1b05f8f15d/title
msgid "Will you change version if it updates?"
msgstr "如果參考資料更新，您是否會改用新版？"

#: question/481d0157-6d89-4f68-9f3b-cf1b05f8f15d/text
msgid "If the reference changes while you are working on your research project, you need to decide whether you will follow these changes. Most likely that will mean that you have to do some analyses again, so you will need to make sure enough resources are available to do so. You can decide to stay with the version that you started with; this can have the disadvantage that you will not benefit from added information or added consistency."
msgstr "如果參考資料在您進行研究計畫期間發生變更，您需要決定是否要跟進這些變更。這很可能表示您必須重新進行部分分析，因此需要確認有足夠的資源可供執行。您也可以選擇繼續使用計畫開始時採用的版本；但這麼做的缺點是，您將無法受益於後續新增的資訊或提升的一致性。"

#: answer/a4f6a1da-536b-43fa-9637-71e33327fa08/label
msgid "Will stay with the old version"
msgstr "會繼續使用舊版"

#: question/deb9d6b3-4f11-4aa8-b016-52d1612c002a/title
msgid "How will the old version be available?"
msgstr "如何確保舊版參考資料仍可供使用？"

#: question/deb9d6b3-4f11-4aa8-b016-52d1612c002a/text
msgid "Since you want to keep using the old version of the reference data, how will it be available to you?"
msgstr "既然您想沿用舊版參考資料，請說明您將如何確保該版本仍可供您使用？"

#: answer/bbef3d6c-7a90-4d5e-8d72-1fea083f6410/label
msgid "I will need it only at the beginning"
msgstr "我只會在一開始需要該版本"

#: answer/e6ddd126-0878-4831-9450-8c5f3e9126dd/label
msgid "I will use a downloaded version"
msgstr "我會使用已下載的版本"

#: answer/07f06e60-9d5b-46b9-832a-75b881c4a9cb/label
#: answer/b4d8d8b8-3c8e-4b41-87a4-dbd01e7b7ad9/label
msgid "The provider keeps old versions around"
msgstr "資料提供者會保留舊版本"

#: answer/069a0976-498c-4a47-b42f-33c6a1e40126/label
msgid "New analyses will be done with the new version"
msgstr "新的分析將使用新版本執行"

#: answer/dc8dbe60-43e8-4ed4-ab11-13bb74aea820/label
msgid "All analyses will be redone with the new version"
msgstr "所有分析都將以新版本重新執行"

#: question/12762d00-f02a-40f7-b175-c7e4c92f5f54/title
msgid "How will you make sure the same reference data will be available to reproduce your results?"
msgstr "您將如何確保同一份參考資料可供他人取用，以重現您的研究結果？"

#: question/12762d00-f02a-40f7-b175-c7e4c92f5f54/text
msgid "Will the reference data in the version you use be available to others?"
msgstr "您所使用版本的參考資料是否可供他人取用？"

#: answer/9832a3a5-e24d-4db1-b48f-4d171c1402ae/label
msgid "I will keep a copy and make it available with my results"
msgstr "我會保留一份副本，並在發表研究結果時一併提供"

#: answer/aee14c30-46a4-4a8f-8918-acc98a31043e/label
msgid "It will be available both from the provider and together with my data"
msgstr "該參考資料可由資料提供者取得，也會隨本研究資料一併提供"

#: question/bf02f456-0a60-4b50-ae86-5cd56d430b2e/title
msgid "What will you use this reference data set for?"
msgstr "您會將此參考資料集用於什麼目的？"

#: reference/37fcb07e-a791-40ef-934b-33dedece5b0c/description
msgid "Creating reference data"
msgstr "建立參考資料"

#: question/be872000-cb98-442f-999c-ca3ef58dcfe8/title
msgid "What existing non-reference data sets did you consider re-using?"
msgstr "您考慮過再次使用哪些既有的非參考資料集？"

#: question/be872000-cb98-442f-999c-ca3ef58dcfe8/text
msgid "Even if you will be producing your own data, you often will also be relying on existing data sets (e.g. from your own earlier projects). You may need to integrate your new data with an existing data set or retrieve additional information from related data bases. Will you be doing such things?"
msgstr "即便您將自行產製資料，通常仍會依賴既有資料集（例如源自您先前自己的計畫）。您可能需要將新資料與既有資料集進行整合，或是從相關資料庫中取得額外資訊。您是否會進行這類操作？"

#: question/682da8d1-c109-4f62-8cf1-dadd8908af77/title
msgid "Non-reference data set"
msgstr "非參考資料集"

#: question/682da8d1-c109-4f62-8cf1-dadd8908af77/text
msgid "Give a name for the data set."
msgstr "請為資料集命名。"

#: question/5f73797c-268a-4862-b48b-75719ff47709/title
msgid "Provide PID for this non-reference data set"
msgstr "請提供此非參考資料集的持續識別碼 (PID)"

#: question/5f73797c-268a-4862-b48b-75719ff47709/text
msgid "Specify a persistent identifier (e.g., a DOI) or a URL for the dataset. If the data set is versioned, try to refer to the exact version you will use."
msgstr "請指定此非參考資料集的持續識別碼 (PID)，例如數位物件識別碼 (DOI)，或提供網址。如果此資料集有版本控制，請盡量精確指向您將使用的版本。"

#: question/f5e129dc-d59d-4352-a5ed-25efe1d83811/title
msgid "Will you be using this non-reference data set?"
msgstr "您是否會使用此非參考資料集？"

#: question/4e0141ae-bec4-492e-98f4-b79a32c7e946/title
msgid "Why did you decide not to use this non-reference data set?"
msgstr "為什麼決定不使用此非參考資料集？"

#: question/584c3be2-8735-4b37-bbac-1976e1b1c266/title
msgid "Please specify the reason why you will not be using this non-reference data set"
msgstr "請具體說明您將不使用此非參考資料集的原因"

#: question/b141a560-a823-48a7-9ed2-933eee397ae2/title
msgid "Name and contact details for the rightsholder of this data"
msgstr "此資料權利人的姓名與聯絡資訊"

#: question/69999c2c-2710-480e-b8ac-8a8fc6f582e5/title
msgid "What are the conditions of use for this data set?"
msgstr "此資料集有哪些使用條件？"

#: question/39e0cc7c-17fe-4991-88d8-1280c3fe7923/title
msgid "Will the rightsholder of this dataset work with you on this study?"
msgstr "此資料集的權利人是否會與您共同進行這項研究？"

#: question/f59d2d89-fe27-4a8a-b3e6-2782bcc2fb97/title
msgid "Do you need to request access to the data?"
msgstr ""

#: answer/08b6593f-60a2-498a-9c20-eeb55568f8c1/label
msgid "We are rightsholders"
msgstr "我們就是權利人"

#: question/50864250-7dad-421a-9f6c-303114fe6e6c/title
msgid "Does the data set include personal data?"
msgstr "該資料集是否包含個人資料？"

#: question/c2da0410-ede1-4b0a-a750-09e6e6bd38cf/title
msgid "What is the legal basis for processing the data under the GDPR?"
msgstr "根據 GDPR，處理此資料的法律依據是什麼？"

#: question/c2da0410-ede1-4b0a-a750-09e6e6bd38cf/text
msgid ""
"[Article 6](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-6-gdpr/) (1) lists under what conditions the processing is considered lawful. Of these, **Consent** or **Public** interest are relevant when it comes to research. You should determine what legal basis (or bases) you have for processing the personal data in your project. \n"
"\n"
"Traditionally, *consent* has been the basis for processing personal data for research, but under the GDPR there cannot be an imbalance between the processor and the data subject for it to be considered to be freely given. In some countries the use of *consent* as the legal basis for processing by universities for research purposes is therefore not recommended. In those cases, public interest should probably be your legal basis. Note that if your legal basis for processing is consent, [a number of requirements](https://gdpr-info.eu/issues/consent/) exists for the consent to be considered valid under the GDPR. Consents given before the GDPR might not live up to this. \n"
"\n"
"Also note that even if *public interest* is the legal basis, other laws and research ethics standards might still require you to have consent from the subjects for performing the research."
msgstr ""
"[第 6 條](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-6-gdpr/) 第 1 項列出處理行為在何種條件下可視為合法。其中，與研究相關的通常是「**同意**」或「**公共利益**」。您應判斷在您的計畫中，處理個人資料適用哪一項或哪些法律依據。\n"
"\n"
"過去，研究處理個人資料時，通常以「*同意*」作為法律依據；但依 GDPR，若資料處理者與資料主體之間存在權力不對等，就難以認定該同意是自由給予。因此，在某些國家，不建議大學以「*同意*」作為研究目的處理個人資料的法律依據。在這類情況下，較可能適合的法律依據是公共利益。若您以同意作為處理依據，請注意，同意必須符合[若干要求](https://gdpr-info.eu/issues/consent/)，才會被 GDPR 視為有效；GDPR 生效前取得的同意，不一定符合這些要求。\n"
"\n"
"也請注意，即使法律依據是「*公共利益*」，其他法律或研究倫理標準仍可能要求您取得受試者的同意，才能進行研究。"

#: answer/597d2547-4e97-4045-8605-3b5249f2b412/label
#: answer/c732f0b9-2f66-47f4-902f-724a44cdfd4b/label
msgid "Public interest"
msgstr "公共利益"

#: answer/eb17ff9a-c57e-4fd4-b3bd-89edb31c6568/label
msgid "Consent given by the research subject"
msgstr "受試者所給予的知情同意"

#: answer/eb17ff9a-c57e-4fd4-b3bd-89edb31c6568/advice
msgid "Traditionally, *consent* has been the basis for processing personal data for research, but under the GDPR there cannot be an imbalance between the processor and the data subject for it to be considered to be freely given. In some countries the use of *consent* as the legal basis for processing by universities for research purposes is therefore not recommended. In those cases, public interest should probably be your legal basis. Note that if your legal basis for processing is consent, [a number of requirements](https://gdpr-info.eu/issues/consent/) exists for the consent to be considered valid under the GDPR. Consents given before the GDPR might not live up to this. "
msgstr "過去，研究處理個人資料時，通常以「*同意*」作為法律依據；但依 GDPR，若資料處理者與資料主體之間存在權力不對等，就難以認定該同意是自由給予。因此，在某些國家，不建議大學以「*同意*」作為研究目的處理個人資料的法律依據。在這類情況下，較可能適合的法律依據是公共利益。若您以同意作為處理依據，請注意，同意必須符合[若干要求](https://gdpr-info.eu/issues/consent/)，才會被 GDPR 視為有效；GDPR 生效前取得的同意，不一定符合這些要求。 "

#: question/28e7c4f7-7ade-42b2-a68e-63ab4f67b960/title
msgid "Does the consent cover your data reuse?"
msgstr "受試者的同意是否涵蓋資料再次使用？"

#: question/28e7c4f7-7ade-42b2-a68e-63ab4f67b960/text
msgid "If the data that you will re-use is coupled to people, the informed consent that was originally obtained from those people may not be covering your current research. In that case re-consent may be necessary."
msgstr "如果您將再次使用的資料可連結至個人，則原先向這些人取得的知情同意可能不涵蓋您目前的研究。在這種情況下，可能需要重新取得知情同意。"

#: answer/15071f5e-c120-4a10-b0e8-054dea4dbf04/label
msgid "The existing consent covers our reuse"
msgstr "既有同意的範圍已涵蓋我們對資料的再次使用"

#: answer/5374139c-f125-4d04-bce2-3ef6d4b34a2a/label
msgid "New consent will be needed to cover our usage of the data"
msgstr "需要重新取得同意，才能涵蓋我們對該資料的使用"

#: question/40ea30cc-ea49-4407-8bba-c511a9fb1786/title
msgid "Which?"
msgstr "是哪一項？"

#: question/40ea30cc-ea49-4407-8bba-c511a9fb1786/text
msgid ""
"The following legal bases are unlikely for processing personal data when doing research.\n"
"\n"
"The meaning of the different options are as follows:\n"
"* Legal requirement: we are legally obliged to do this data processing\n"
"* Vital interest: we need to do this to protect the vital interests of the data subject\n"
"* We have a legitimate interest: data subjects all expect us to do this data processing because of who we are"
msgstr ""
"下列法律依據在研究中處理個人資料時通常較不適用。\n"
"\n"
"各選項的意思如下：\n"
"* 法律要求：我們依法有義務進行這項資料處理\n"
"* 重大利益：我們需要進行這項處理，以保護資料主體的重大利益\n"
"* 我們具有合法利益：基於我們的身分，資料主體可合理預期我們會進行這項資料處理"

#: answer/18db88c7-97c9-416e-b1ae-763bf018345e/label
#: answer/f10de3a8-2751-42c7-afaa-92eed4833f8e/label
msgid "Legal requirement"
msgstr "法律要求"

#: answer/8caeb960-7c5e-457c-ae9e-1a2e038a466a/label
#: answer/557a5401-a94a-4a37-af2e-a21829557bfa/label
msgid "Vital interest"
msgstr "重大利益"

#: answer/34bf8a67-6bba-4eab-8264-8d76f97e66c8/label
msgid "We have a legitimate interest"
msgstr "我們具有合法利益"

#: answer/bfb7a92c-5eec-497e-8a0f-ef7b12f353c2/label
msgid "We require the processing to fulfil our contract with the data subjects"
msgstr "我們需要進行此處理，以履行與資料主體之間的契約"

#: question/c15710f6-1c7f-43a0-97e7-ab70f6b5a115/title
msgid "Is a new approval or extension of any existing approval under research ethics laws needed for re-use of the data?"
msgstr "資料再次使用是否需要依研究倫理法規取得新的核准，或展延既有核准？"

#: question/c15710f6-1c7f-43a0-97e7-ab70f6b5a115/text
msgid "If the data that you will re-use is coupled to people, the ethical approval that was originally obtained may not be covering your current research. In that case an extension of the original approval, or a new approval, may be necessary."
msgstr "如果您將再次使用的資料可連結至個人，則原先取得的倫理審查核准可能不涵蓋您目前的研究。在這種情況下，可能需要申請展延原核准，或重新取得新的核准。"

#: answer/ad44fec7-d244-4bb1-9028-8d6856a06d6b/label
msgid "Not applicable"
msgstr "不適用"

#: answer/284110a8-66b4-4ba5-9e7a-edb77b1f2b3a/label
msgid "The existing ethical approval under research ethics laws covers our reuse"
msgstr "依研究倫理法規取得的既有倫理審查核准，已涵蓋我們對資料的再次使用"

#: answer/12ae8bdc-a6eb-4db9-9a1a-7e6fed7f9ace/label
msgid "An extension of existing ethical approval under research ethics laws will be needed"
msgstr "將會需要依研究倫理相關法規，申請展延既有倫理審查核准"

#: answer/6dd1142d-f76f-4d0b-9c38-999f7d8a229b/label
msgid "New ethical approval under research ethics laws will be needed to cover our usage of the data"
msgstr "需要依研究倫理法規取得新的倫理審查核准，以涵蓋我們對此資料的使用"

#: question/588e3c1f-e9fd-411f-954e-f7a9b1cff1de/text
msgid "Do you know the data format of the data? Is this suitable for your work? Does it need to be converted?"
msgstr "您是否清楚該資料的資料格式？該格式是否適合您的操作？是否需要轉檔？"

#: question/62ddfc73-1680-4bbf-b198-6a7231875fb1/title
msgid "How will you be accessing the data?"
msgstr "您會如何取用資料？"

#: answer/423f7c77-c3bd-4ece-a9f6-ad9e3d0428a1/label
msgid "Already have a copy"
msgstr "已有一份副本"

#: answer/4e183e8d-d4bd-442a-a663-d3accf4f9217/label
msgid "Will download or get a copy"
msgstr "將下載或取得副本"

#: answer/f5e1c4d3-79f7-4950-9b10-6a7738f21978/label
msgid "Will use it online"
msgstr "將在線上使用"

#: question/3b088f38-81bd-46f9-8066-90513740b662/title
msgid "Is the data set fixed, or will it be updated in the future?"
msgstr "資料集是固定不變的，還是未來還會更新？"

#: question/3b088f38-81bd-46f9-8066-90513740b662/text
msgid "Is the data set you will reuse a fixed data set (with a persistent identifier), or is it a data set that is being worked on (by others) and may be updated during your project or after?"
msgstr "您將再次使用的資料集，是一個固定不變的資料集（具有持續識別碼），還是一個仍在由他人持續處理、並可能在您的計畫期間或之後更新的資料集？"

#: answer/aff2edcd-4d18-4311-9a03-3b6b676c9277/label
msgid "It is a fixed data set, this will not influence reproducibility of my results"
msgstr "這是一個固定不變的資料集，因此不會影響研究結果的可重現性"

#: answer/d700715e-4ae0-45ed-a1d3-4d79bb32155f/label
msgid "It may change"
msgstr "可能會變動"

#: answer/d700715e-4ae0-45ed-a1d3-4d79bb32155f/advice
msgid "Make sure a copy of the version of the input data you use will be available with the results"
msgstr "請確保您使用的輸入資料版本副本，會與研究結果一併提供"

#: question/2e7af465-4852-4411-8d8e-7f0ff64d8b25/title
msgid "Can you and will you use the complete existing data set?"
msgstr "您是否能夠且願意使用完整的既有資料集？"

#: question/2e7af465-4852-4411-8d8e-7f0ff64d8b25/text
msgid "If you use any filtering, how will you make sure that your results will be reproducible by yourself and others at a later time?"
msgstr "如果您使用任何篩選方式，您將如何確保您自己以及其他人之後仍能重現您的結果？"

#: answer/2076afb5-3c5c-4f42-8f77-9b78fec76a62/label
msgid "I will use the complete data set"
msgstr "我會使用完整的資料集"

#: answer/f748624d-8d28-4d07-91c7-28b33db1fabd/label
msgid "Any filtering or selection will be well documented"
msgstr "任何篩選與選取的過程都會完整記錄起來"

#: answer/cba7c977-986d-4673-9bbc-fb3f7fed95c6/label
msgid "I will make sure the selected subset will be available together with my results"
msgstr "我會確保所選取的子集會與研究結果一併提供"

#: question/eb711ea8-8ee7-40b1-a56d-1a374fe8b4c2/title
msgid "What will you use this non-reference data set for?"
msgstr "您將把這個非參考資料集用於什麼目的？"

#: question/8cedcf93-7676-4397-b3fc-a81167ff1853/title
msgid "Do you need to harmonise different sources of existing data?"
msgstr ""

#: question/8cedcf93-7676-4397-b3fc-a81167ff1853/text
msgid "If you are combining data from different sources, harmonization may be required. You may need to re-analyse some original data."
msgstr "如果您正在整合來自不同來源的資料，可能需要進行資料調和。您也可能需要重新分析部分原始資料。"

#: question/1d1ac8bb-66c8-4b9e-bfc9-4c26f3598062/title
msgid "Will you be making your harmonisation results available to others?"
msgstr ""

#: question/1d1ac8bb-66c8-4b9e-bfc9-4c26f3598062/text
msgid "By publishing either exactly what you did or (better) make sure that the harmonized data is available for reuse, you may save others the effort."
msgstr "透過公開您實際進行的處理步驟，或更理想的是，確保調和後的資料可供再次使用，您可以為他人節省心力。"

#: question/7e77ee02-ce26-4cd9-b07d-3eea03bc35c9/title
msgid "Will you be using data that needs to be (re-)made computer readable first?"
msgstr "您是否會使用需要先轉為電腦可讀形式的資料？"

#: question/7e77ee02-ce26-4cd9-b07d-3eea03bc35c9/text
msgid "Some old data may need to be recovered, e.g. from tables in scientific papers or may be punch cards."
msgstr "有些舊資料可能需要另外設法復原，例如從科學論文的表格中整理出來，或者資料本身是穿孔卡片。"

#: question/530124a4-c7e9-4821-b26d-32a8ecd0d978/title
msgid "Will you be making the data itself available in computer readable form to others?"
msgstr "您是否會將資料本身以電腦可讀形式提供給他人？"

#: question/530124a4-c7e9-4821-b26d-32a8ecd0d978/text
msgid "It is advisable to make the result of your efforts available in a standard repository. If you answer 'yes' here, do not forget to mention the dataset under the chapter 'giving access to data'."
msgstr "建議將您的處理成果存放於標準的儲存庫中並對外提供。若您在此回答「是」，請別忘了在「提供資料取用權限」章節中提及該資料集。"

#: answer/dce00426-ea06-4aac-979e-ccefb9ba01f9/label
msgid "Yes, through a standard repository"
msgstr "是，透過標準儲存庫提供"

#: answer/790dbcb1-69fb-4aac-bffc-4b7dd8b24aaa/label
msgid "Yes, through other means"
msgstr "是，透過其他方式提供"

#: question/44b0de3f-b580-4dd0-9e9a-24864c8fe9c8/title
msgid "Will you provide machine readable, standardised metadata to others?"
msgstr "您是否會向他人提供機器可讀且標準化的後設資料？"

#: answer/69b0dc80-4b80-4fe6-b162-2a3eff9e133e/advice
msgid "If the data is published in a standard repository, that repository will tell you which metadata standards to use."
msgstr "如果資料發布於標準儲存庫中，該儲存庫會告訴您應使用哪些後設資料標準。"

#: question/f09c417a-3b3d-4dc8-a1a2-93b1c4bcf8fd/title
msgid "Which metadata standards will you use?"
msgstr "您將使用哪些後設資料標準？"

#: question/2e5b1f82-4836-4b49-a0bf-2a2624eeaafb/title
msgid "Metadata Standard"
msgstr "後設資料標準"

#: question/2e5b1f82-4836-4b49-a0bf-2a2624eeaafb/text
#: question/f0ca4f37-ef70-452e-b620-434d52fb5924/text
msgid "You will be presented with suggestions from [FAIRSharing](https://fairsharing.org/), but you also have the option to manually enter the metadata standard that is not listed there."
msgstr "系統會顯示來自 [FAIRSharing](https://fairsharing.org/) 的建議項目，但您也可以手動輸入未列於其中的後設資料標準。"

#: reference/9b5581d7-9226-446a-be68-1754a5cbd6a9/label
msgid "Google dataset search"
msgstr "Google 資料集搜尋"

#: reference/fffcd354-ac6e-4905-b74b-f1a6b180bcff/label
msgid "Datacite Search"
msgstr "搜尋 Datacite"

#: reference/7e8d2692-7da6-4f29-a97c-1cf09e2cbb06/label
msgid "RDMkit on Reusing Data"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料再次使用頁面"

#: reference/5e67414d-d584-47d4-8bdc-ee0a3ec29c68/label
msgid "RDMkit on Existing Data"
msgstr "RDMkit 的既有資料頁面"

#: reference/87c7169d-f8bf-4616-bdb4-d1db922746d3/label
msgid "DMEG on Data Discovery"
msgstr "DMEG (Data Management Expert Guide) 中的資料探索"

#: reference/ba9fdb42-1524-4d68-8aa9-c3ab72b54dc5/label
msgid "DMEG on Access to Data"
msgstr "DMEG (Data Management Expert Guide) 的「取用資料」頁面"

#: chapter/b1df3c74-0b1f-4574-81c4-4cc2d780c1af/title
msgid "Creating and collecting data"
msgstr "建立與蒐集資料"

#: chapter/b1df3c74-0b1f-4574-81c4-4cc2d780c1af/text
msgid ""
"In this chapter we describe all the sources of data: they can e.g. come from instruments or from questionnaires; data can be newly collected as part of the current project, but it can also be pre-existing data that may need proper contracts with the maintainer, some pre-processing, and quality checks. It can also be reference data that is part of curated resources and (public) databases. \n"
"\n"
"For more information see [Collecting in RDMKit](https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/collecting)"
msgstr ""
"本章說明所有的資料來源：資料可能來自儀器或問卷；可能是在目前計畫中新蒐集的資料，也可能是既有資料，需要與維護者訂定適當契約、進行部分前處理與品質檢查。資料也可能是來自經過策展的資源以及（公眾）資料庫中的參考資料。\n"
"\n"
"更多資訊請參閱 [RDMkit 的資料蒐集頁面](https://rdmkit.elixir-europe.org/collecting)"

#: question/0e810343-6026-4992-8ea0-5539cbc77093/title
msgid "Will you be collecting physical samples?"
msgstr "您是否會蒐集實體樣本？"

#: question/0e810343-6026-4992-8ea0-5539cbc77093/text
msgid "Will you be collecting artefacts like specimens, minerals, biological samples?"
msgstr "您是否會蒐集標本、礦物、生物樣本等實體物件？"

#: question/f67a9910-4ea3-4280-b503-386dff3b8305/title
msgid "Do your samples need to be submitted to a public repository?"
msgstr "您的樣本是否需要提交至公開的儲存庫？"

#: question/f67a9910-4ea3-4280-b503-386dff3b8305/text
msgid "In some fields, it is considered good practice to deposit samples to a public repository before deriving any digital data from them."
msgstr "在某些領域中，從樣本產製任何數位資料之前，先將樣本寄存至公開儲存庫，被視為良好實務。"

#: question/cc57d7c0-49db-4546-958f-e9407eaf93ee/title
msgid "Will the samples be stored in a local repository such as a biobank?"
msgstr "樣本是否會存放在本地儲存庫，例如生物樣本庫？"

#: question/da0d28e6-1c6e-44d8-ba47-d834aeca847b/title
msgid "How will the samples be identified?"
msgstr "樣本可以怎樣被識別？"

#: answer/a0ced35d-28f4-4208-b4b1-bb524401939d/label
msgid "Samples will only get an internal code"
msgstr "樣本僅會以內部編碼加以識別"

#: answer/b0544e61-df56-4d21-bd68-f81f83fdc7c4/label
msgid "Samples will receive a universally unique persistent identifier (PID)"
msgstr "樣本將會取得一組全域唯一的持續識別碼 (PID)"

#: question/d488b314-2b5c-4e79-be1e-c5742205d2a5/title
msgid "Where will the physical samples be stored?"
msgstr ""

#: question/9e238002-da35-4f9b-a9b7-8fe3613a3c03/title
msgid "Will you make explicit cross-reference between physical samples and your digital data?"
msgstr "您是否會在實體樣本與數位資料之間建立明確的交叉參照？"

#: question/9e238002-da35-4f9b-a9b7-8fe3613a3c03/text
msgid "Is the identifier of your physical sample present in the metadata for the digital data that associates to it? Will you be able to locate the physical sample if you have the digital data? And how about the reverse?\n"
msgstr "與您的數位資料相對應的後設資料中，是否包含該實體樣本的識別碼？如果您手上有數位資料，是否能夠據此找到對應的實體樣本？反過來也是如此嗎？\n"

#: reference/5c6e0a81-4a69-4542-a667-f3e67d56392e/label
#: reference/bdf3a93e-4413-42ad-8a33-c977e6a0c4f5/label
msgid "RDMkit on Identifiers"
msgstr "RDMkit 的識別碼頁面"

#: question/8c962e6f-17ee-4b22-8ebb-9f06f779e3b3/title
msgid "How will you be collecting and keeping your metadata?"
msgstr "您將如何蒐集並保存後設資料？"

#: question/8c962e6f-17ee-4b22-8ebb-9f06f779e3b3/text
msgid "For the re-usability of your data by yourself or others at a later stage, a lot of information about the data – for example how it was collected and how it can be used – should be stored with the data. Such *data about the data* is called **metadata**, and this set of questions are about this metadata."
msgstr "為了讓您自己或他人日後能再次使用資料，應將資料的相關資訊一併保存，例如資料的蒐集方式及使用方式。這類「*關於資料的資料*」稱為**後設資料** (metadata)，本組問題將探討這些後設資料。"

#: answer/6d18bfff-0f53-469b-934e-9806dda9d4fb/label
#: answer/c05f27a2-30ac-44fd-9ac9-cd6f62b16d0c/label
#: answer/d8ecede2-f952-4b08-8a68-20d97849733f/label
#: answer/5af813b7-cb41-4eb9-afe7-ca364771b74e/label
#: answer/aca843cd-e38e-4174-8ce1-477c2b405fdf/label
#: answer/54e9c073-52ee-4f8d-a1aa-1d279ec0f61d/label
#: answer/0d64d3c6-4312-47a9-92ad-0bc9440d6e45/label
#: answer/f7f2ff16-eee0-42a7-a89a-bd7291cef5fc/label
