#: answer/6d18bfff-0f53-469b-934e-9806dda9d4fb/advice
msgid ""
"There are many kinds of metadata, each serving their own purpose.  Some key metadata that you should consider:\n"
"* There is metadata that helps identify where the data is coming from (e.g. who created it, title). For this the [Dublin Core](https://www.dublincore.org) is often used.\n"
"* There are different ways of adding metadata to make the data \"discoverable\" for other researchers. This requires either keywords or ontology terms describing what is in the data.\n"
"* There is metadata describing how the data can be re-used, such as license information and, for data about people, the extent of their consent for data reuse.\n"
"* There is metadata that makes the data understandable, e.g. linking to the exact processes used to collect them (is a *body temperature* measured under the tongue or in the rectum?) and units (is a temperature given in Celsius or Fahrenheit?). \n"
"* There is metadata describing where the data comes from and what it is useful for. For frequently used data types, there are often very well defined metadata standards, in other cases you may need to think about this yourself.\n"
"For each of these kinds of metadata there are specific standards. There is no single standard that will get you all the metadata needed to make the data as FAIR as possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"後設資料有許多類型，各有不同用途。以下是您應考量的幾類關鍵後設資料：\n"
"* 有些後設資料有助於識別資料來源，例如建立者與標題。這類資訊通常會使用 [Dublin Core](https://www.dublincore.org)。\n"
"* 有些後設資料能讓其他研究人員更容易發現資料。這通常需要使用關鍵字，或使用描述資料內容的知識本體 (ontology)術語。\n"
"* 有些後設資料會描述可以如何再次使用該資料，例如授權條款；若是與人相關的資料，也包括原始同意涵蓋的資料再次使用範圍。\n"
"* 有些後設資料能讓資料更容易理解，例如連結到蒐集資料時使用的確切流程（例如「*體溫*」是在舌下還是直腸量測？），以及度量單位（溫度是攝氏還是華氏？）。\n"
"* 有些後設資料會描述資料來源，以及資料適合用於哪些目的。對於常見資料類型，通常已有定義完善的後設資料標準；其他情況下，您可能需要自行判斷。\n"
"每一類後設資料都有相應的特定標準。沒有任何單一標準能涵蓋所有讓資料盡可能符合 FAIR 原則所需的後設資料。\n"

#: question/1440afd6-d516-44f6-9c02-6abb13900b66/title
msgid "What standard(s) will you use to specify author/title/keyword information?"
msgstr "您將使用哪些標準來指定作者、標題與關鍵字資訊？"

#: question/1440afd6-d516-44f6-9c02-6abb13900b66/text
msgid "There are a few different standards that are often used to give basic information about your dataset. Which ones of these will you be using?"
msgstr "有幾種不同標準常用於提供資料集的基本資訊。您將使用其中哪些標準？"

#: question/da1d96bb-3eb4-41ca-8629-c9e6b34c63c3/title
msgid "What standard will you use to specify author/title/keyword information?"
msgstr ""

#: question/da1d96bb-3eb4-41ca-8629-c9e6b34c63c3/text
#: question/127bc0d5-8de6-4021-9a95-22b97ed3c308/text
msgid "You will be presented with suggestions from [FAIRsharing](https://fairsharing.org/), but you also have the option to manually enter the metadata standard that is not listed there."
msgstr ""

#: question/434b28c1-dbc0-4dd0-bb53-6d6ad51b86f4/title
msgid "Will you be creating a data/variable dictionary?"
msgstr "您是否會建立資料字典或變項定義表？"

#: question/434b28c1-dbc0-4dd0-bb53-6d6ad51b86f4/text
msgid "If anyone wants to see whether they can re-use your data, it must be possible to see what information in contains. For this, a data dictionary can play an important role."
msgstr "若有人想看看是否能再利用您的資料，他們必須能夠了解資料中有什麼資訊。為此，資料字典 (data dictionary) 可以發揮重要作用。"

#: reference/7be357bc-b820-42af-a512-95d68cb78d79/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on creating a data/variable dictionary"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的「建立資料／變項字典」頁面"

#: question/6226d7f2-565f-4991-94b3-c00be6aca20e/title
msgid "Do suitable 'Minimal Metadata About ...' (MIA...) standards exist for your experiments?"
msgstr "是否存在適用於您實驗的「最少後設資料描述 (Minimal Metadata About …, MIA…)」相關標準？"

#: question/6226d7f2-565f-4991-94b3-c00be6aca20e/text
msgid "Many research fields have worked together to define what kind of metadata should really be collected when an experiment of a certain kind is performed and described. That information is described in a Minimal Metadata Standard. Often, these standards describe both what kind of information needs to be collected as well as the format in which it is expected."
msgstr "許多研究領域已共同定義，在執行並描述某類實驗時，實際應蒐集哪些後設資料。這些資訊會以最少後設資料標準描述。這類標準通常同時描述需要蒐集哪些資訊，以及預期使用的格式。"

#: answer/a23664b1-a17c-41fe-855c-db274984b355/advice
msgid "Did you really check a service like fairsharing.org to verify this?"
msgstr "您是否確實查核，像用 fairsharing.org 這樣的服務來加以驗證？"

#: question/44a9d6c0-f96c-47d2-8c7a-902a9c222067/title
msgid "Do you have a good idea of what metadata is needed to make it possible for others to read and interpret your data in the future?"
msgstr "您是否知道需要哪些後設資料，可讓他人在未來能夠讀取並理解您的資料？"

#: question/44a9d6c0-f96c-47d2-8c7a-902a9c222067/text
msgid ""
"Imagine yourself trying to interpret a similar data set from a colleague in a few years. \n"
"Is there any way in which the data could be misinterpreted? Does everyone in the field do things in exactly the same way? And will that still be known in 10 years?\n"
"How can such misinterpretation be avoided?"
msgstr ""
"請想像幾年後，您要嘗試解讀一位同事所產出的類似資料集\n"
"這些資料是否有任何可能被誤解的地方？這個領域中的每個人是否都完全以相同的方式處理事情？而且這些做法在 10 年後仍然眾所周知嗎？\n"
"如何避免這類誤解？"

#: reference/67a39c34-fe6f-415e-93d1-998fc2911748/label
#: reference/2bdad98e-ef5f-4645-9ec7-bf5101e0b4c1/label
#: reference/cab1617b-adf5-46c0-9e55-66348e35961f/label
msgid "FAIRsharing repository of standards"
msgstr "FAIRsharing 的標準登錄頁面"

#: question/e7b6cd51-22a6-4f7a-9ad5-a7234fa436cb/title
msgid "Which \"Minimal Information\" standards will you use?"
msgstr "您將使用哪些「最少資訊」標準？"

#: question/f0ca4f37-ef70-452e-b620-434d52fb5924/title
msgid "Minimal Information Standard"
msgstr "最少資訊標準"

#: question/ed872b74-6bf7-4cba-8f36-4da4509e4a4f/title
msgid "Do you know how and when you will be collecting the necessary metadata?"
msgstr "您是否知道將如何以及何時蒐集必要的後設資料？"

#: question/ed872b74-6bf7-4cba-8f36-4da4509e4a4f/text
msgid "Often it is easiest to make sure you collect the metadata as early as possible."
msgstr "確保盡早蒐集後設資料通常是最容易的做法。"

#: question/15573266-7ddf-4c6b-962e-45691d34cf61/title
msgid "Will you consider re-usability of your data beyond your original purpose?"
msgstr "您是否會考量資料在原始目的之外再次使用的可能性？"

#: question/15573266-7ddf-4c6b-962e-45691d34cf61/text
msgid "Adding more than the strict minimum metadata about your experiment will possibly allow more wide re-use of your data, with associated higher data citation rates. Please note that it is not easy for yourself to see all other ways in which others could be reusing your data."
msgstr "為您的實驗新增超過最低需求的後設資料，有機會讓您的資料被更廣泛地再次使用，並可能提高資料引用率。要預想他人未來可能以哪些方式再次使用您的資料並不容易，因此提供較完整的後設資料尤為重要。"

#: answer/b2ca0d26-7fdd-44f1-b064-bc4cd4c45661/label
msgid "I will only add the metadata that is \"required\" in the standard"
msgstr ""

#: answer/b2ca0d26-7fdd-44f1-b064-bc4cd4c45661/advice
msgid ""
"Please consider adding metadata items that is available to you. This can be helpful for others that may want to re-use your data for a different purpose.\n"
"If you collect your metadata on the fly, it is not a lot of work to keep it."
msgstr ""
"請考慮加入您能蒐集到的後設資料項目。這些資訊可能有助於未來想為其他目的再次使用您資料的人。\n"
"如果您在工作過程中同步蒐集後設資料，保留這些資訊通常不會增加太多工作。"

#: answer/cb765913-50c9-482e-bf10-5f5f91d0e473/label
msgid "Yes, I will add \"optional\" metadata where I can"
msgstr "是，我會在可行時加入選填（非必填）後設資料"

#: question/73bf7531-3490-4c0f-b6a2-a9f4f2bc3e1a/title
msgid "How will you balance the extra efforts with the potential for added reusability?"
msgstr "您會如何在額外投入的工作量，與讓資料更容易再次使用所帶來的潛在效益之間取得平衡？"

#: answer/3002eaed-c31f-4bdd-83ed-49262ae79165/label
msgid "I will see what I can do"
msgstr "我會看看我能做些什麼"

#: answer/7ef32aea-b6a7-4297-92bd-0869a13276ad/label
msgid "I will use preselected additional standard modules of metadata"
msgstr "我會採用預先選定的額外標準後設資料模組"

#: answer/018fc8a0-c51e-48f4-99d5-77e8c9dcf51f/label
msgid "I will collect all metadata I can gather and document the data set beyond minimal standards"
msgstr "我會盡可能蒐集完整的後設資料，並在最低標準之上，加強資料集的記錄"

#: question/c961b59a-b635-4a77-87ba-bc1b449bb012/title
msgid "Do you need to exchange your data with others?"
msgstr "您的資料是否需要與他人交換？"

#: question/ae28a862-5020-44c2-8c78-3abc185b190f/title
msgid "Will a licence be assigned to your datasets?"
msgstr ""

#: question/ae28a862-5020-44c2-8c78-3abc185b190f/text
msgid "It is not always clear to everyone in the project (and outside) what can and can not be done with a data set. It is helpful to associate each data set with a licence as early as possible in the project. A data licence should ideally be as free as possible: any restriction like 'only for non-commercial use' or 'attribution required' may reduce the reusability and thereby the number of citations. If possible, use a computer-readable and computer actionable licence."
msgstr ""

#: answer/0b0e1e89-3b7b-4d9e-95f6-d96397b28c3b/advice
msgid "Please consider adding licenses to all datasets you are collecting as soon as possible."
msgstr "請考慮盡快為您正在蒐集的所有資料集指定授權條款。"

#: question/0551adc9-7faa-4ddc-a07b-08fbde2a247b/title
msgid "Will you store the licences with the data at all time?"
msgstr ""

#: question/0551adc9-7faa-4ddc-a07b-08fbde2a247b/text
msgid "It is very likely that data will be moved and copied. At some point people may lose track of the origins. It can be helpful to have the licenses (of course *as open as possible*) stored in close association with the data."
msgstr "資料很可能會被移動與複製。久而久之，人們可能會無法追蹤其來源。因此將授權條款（當然是*盡可能開放*的授權條款）與資料一併保存，會很有幫助。"

#: reference/6df6b71d-d85d-4ca6-bb8f-7136b7bd73fa/label
#: reference/ae5e819c-7d9f-4f1d-9433-81c20171f86e/label
msgid "RDMkit on Licensing"
msgstr "RDMkit 的授權頁面"

#: reference/ce21ae0b-3efa-4249-941f-b1f3f18b2799/label
msgid "DMEG on Licensing"
msgstr "DMEG 的授權頁面"

#: question/de1b1a0f-58ea-4859-91b0-aa2b52090395/title
msgid "Where do you keep any applicable restrictions on the usage of the data?"
msgstr "資料若有適用的使用限制，您會記錄在哪裡？"

#: answer/5458a4cb-b4b1-400f-bc7e-df45bbeb42af/label
msgid "In a specialised registry or catalogue"
msgstr "在專門的登錄冊或目錄中"

#: answer/ff6ea5fb-c987-4391-bca7-c3c3e7a95964/label
msgid "Closely attached to the data in the data management system"
msgstr "緊密附加於資料管理系統中的資料"

#: answer/eefe3d60-b037-488a-826c-871490357ffc/label
msgid "Stored in the same folder as the data"
msgstr "與資料保存在同一資料夾"

#: answer/0cdaa526-aa38-47d6-aa28-e8eaa8a3b127/label
msgid "In another way"
msgstr "以其他方式保存"

#: question/f9572d3c-c91f-4945-a56b-ccfb32750fe9/title
msgid "How will you store any applicable restrictions?"
msgstr "您會如何保存這些使用限制？"

#: reference/35bcd464-9a68-49f3-8365-677fca660b17/label
#: reference/b2db3b93-3ce7-4c3c-a80e-866671a9103a/label
msgid "Data Use Ontology"
msgstr "資料使用知識本體 (ontology)"

#: question/948b5fd8-c1bd-457d-8f81-ea2fd093f541/title
msgid "How will you be keeping track of the \"provenance\" of the data?"
msgstr "您將如何追蹤資料溯源資訊？"

#: question/948b5fd8-c1bd-457d-8f81-ea2fd093f541/text
msgid ""
"Data analysis is normally done step-by-step.  It is important that for all data the origin and all processing and filtering steps are documented, otherwise results will not be reproducible. \n"
"\n"
"Re-users of the data also need this information to decide whether the data can be used for their purpose.\n"
"\n"
"In computing, systems like Galaxy and (Jupyter) notebooks often automatically keep provenance information."
msgstr ""
"資料分析通常是逐步進行的，因此對所有資料而言，完整記錄其來源，以及所有處理與篩選步驟相當重要；否則，分析結果將無法再製。\n"
"\n"
"資料的再利用者 (re-users) 同樣需要這些資訊，才能判斷資料是否適合他們的使用目的。\n"
"\n"
"在運算環境中，Galaxy 與 (Jupyter) 筆記本等系統往往能自動保留資料溯源資訊 (provenance information)。"

#: answer/7b450ee7-8783-4adc-9955-fd667fac5a56/label
msgid "We use lab notebooks"
msgstr "我們會使用實驗室記錄本"

#: answer/7b450ee7-8783-4adc-9955-fd667fac5a56/advice
msgid "Make sure to make the notes available in electronic form along with your data"
msgstr "請確保將這些筆記以電子形式提供，並與您的資料一併附上"

#: answer/a1e67aee-77dd-486f-ab51-e5a6f39a32cc/label
msgid "We use an electronic lab notebook"
msgstr "我們會使用電子實驗室記錄本"

#: answer/68dc8368-d1fd-4bd5-8677-abc9ac7aa4b4/label
msgid "Our computing workflow system keeps provenance information "
msgstr "我們的運算工作流程系統會保存資料溯源資訊 (provenance information) "

#: answer/ccdb5296-919c-44ac-89df-351fd2e564ae/label
msgid "We use other arrangements"
msgstr "我們會採用其他安排"

