msgstr "W3C Prov 入門指南"

#: question/91a7c75c-6f0e-4bae-b3f3-1890feaae9b2/title
msgid "Will you use a workflow system that automatically keeps track of the steps in the analysis?"
msgstr "您是否會使用能自動追蹤分析步驟的工作流程系統？"

#: question/91a7c75c-6f0e-4bae-b3f3-1890feaae9b2/text
msgid "Some workflow systems automatically keep track of which steps were done in data analysis and what options were selected. This can help document the data for reproducibility."
msgstr "有些工作流程系統會自動追蹤資料分析過程中執行了哪些步驟，以及選用了哪些選項。這有助於記錄資料處理過程，從而提升研究的可重現性。"

#: reference/bb71dd81-e53a-4ee3-ab8e-bdd687329b91/label
msgid "RDMkit on documentation and metadata"
msgstr "RDMkit 的文件與後設資料頁面"

#: reference/91440234-5fb8-4342-909e-39196dfbb143/label
msgid "Metadata Standards Catalogue (RDA)"
msgstr "後設資料標準目錄 (RDA)"

#: reference/692f635c-22a5-48e6-a3af-07ff881c3701/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on FAIR and the notion of Metadata "
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的 FAIR 原則與後設資料概念頁面 "

#: reference/3e04aff9-3f6d-4b04-bc86-058ee0c2c81b/label
msgid "DMEG on Metadata"
msgstr "DMEG 的後設資料頁面"

#: question/2bac9020-99cf-4463-8d34-0b0eb2781cd1/title
msgid "What existing encodings/terminologies/vocabularies/ontologies will you be using?"
msgstr "您將使用哪些既有的編碼方式、術語、詞彙表或知識本體 (ontology)？"

#: question/2bac9020-99cf-4463-8d34-0b0eb2781cd1/text
msgid "If you want to facilitate interoperability of your data with data you get from elsewhere, and facilitate re-use of your own data later, it is handy if you use standard ways to encode certain data. Such standard encodings are sometimes called terminologies or ontologies."
msgstr "如果您希望提升資料與其他來源資料之間的可相互操作性，並促進自身資料日後被再次使用，那麼採用標準方式來編碼某些資料會很有幫助。這類標準化的編碼方式有時稱為術語或知識本體 (ontology)。"

#: question/9a7e42c3-eed2-46da-bf45-52acbf1eb50f/text
msgid "You will be presented with suggestions from [FAIRSharing](https://fairsharing.org/), but you also have the option to manually enter the vocabulary or ontology that is not listed there."
msgstr "系統會顯示來自 [FAIRSharing](https://fairsharing.org/) 的建議項目，但您也可以手動輸入未列出的詞彙表或知識本體 (ontology)。"

#: question/c00627a4-40e3-48c2-b481-a0cff5e00080/title
msgid "If you use a standard that is not in FAIRsharing, please specify its PID or URL"
msgstr "若您使用未收錄於 FAIRsharing 的標準，請提供其持續識別碼 (PID) 或網址"

#: reference/c0f78b3d-af6c-4083-8398-688984178536/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook introduction to terminologies and ontologies"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的術語與知識本體 (ontology) 介紹頁面"

#: reference/5669ca15-3bab-46b5-9b0d-9e1013e6172b/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on selecting terminologies and ontologies"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的術語與知識本體 (ontology) 選擇頁面"

#: reference/06211161-75e4-43b7-8e80-c470fccb2893/label
#: reference/ae26faa3-f8ad-4f5d-8bd3-b3d16c526ceb/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on Selecting an ontology lookup service"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的知識本體 (ontology) 查詢服務選擇指南"

#: question/8e886b55-3287-48e7-b353-daf6ab40f7d8/title
msgid "How will you do file naming and file organisation?"
msgstr ""

#: question/8e886b55-3287-48e7-b353-daf6ab40f7d8/text
msgid "Putting some thoughts into file naming can save a lot of trouble later. "
msgstr "事先思考檔案命名方式，可以省去日後許多麻煩。 "

#: question/d4fe0b55-4aee-4d05-88d4-a3f4cad2cfa9/title
msgid "Did you make appointments in the project on how to name files and folders?"
msgstr "您是否已在計畫中約定檔案與資料夾的命名方式？"

#: question/d4fe0b55-4aee-4d05-88d4-a3f4cad2cfa9/text
msgid "It can help if everyone in the project uses the same naming scheme."
msgstr "如果計畫中的每個人都使用相同的命名規則，將會有所幫助。"

#: question/9ff389f0-2236-48cf-880c-040ea1bb0d2f/title
msgid "How do you name files in the project?"
msgstr "您會怎麼命名計畫中的檔案？"

#: question/9ff389f0-2236-48cf-880c-040ea1bb0d2f/text
msgid "Describe how everyone in the project will be naming files and folders, and what folder structure you will use."
msgstr "請說明計畫中每位成員會如何命名檔案與資料夾，以及您們將採用怎樣的資料夾結構。"

#: question/37d0367b-3b69-4b3e-9303-71e628b1f360/title
msgid "Will you be keeping the relationships between data clear in the file names?"
msgstr "您是否會在檔名中清楚呈現資料之間的關係？"

#: question/37d0367b-3b69-4b3e-9303-71e628b1f360/text
msgid "Advice: Use the same identifiers for sample IDs etc throughout the entire project."
msgstr "建議：在整個計畫中，樣本 ID 等識別碼請始終使用相同的命名方式。"

#: question/7dfd022e-6d6e-4923-a81a-ca1f11024b57/title
msgid "Will all the metadata that is embedded in the file names also be available in the proper metadata?"
msgstr "嵌入檔名中的所有後設資料，是否也會在正式後設資料中提供？"

#: question/7dfd022e-6d6e-4923-a81a-ca1f11024b57/text
msgid ""
"The file names are very useful as metadata for people involved in the project, but to computers they are just identifiers. To prevent accidents with e.g. renamed files metadata information should always also be available elsewhere and not only through the file name.\n"
"\n"
"Also note that if metadata could need to change, embedding it in the file names may require renaming files during the project; and this may have implications for references to those files."
msgstr ""
"檔名對參與計畫的人員而言是很有用的後設資料，但對電腦來說，它們只是識別碼。為避免例如檔案重新命名造成的意外，後設資料應一律也在其他地方提供，而不應只透過檔名提供。\n"
"\n"
"也請注意，如果後設資料可能需要變更，將其嵌入檔名可能會使計畫期間必須重新命名檔案；這也可能影響對這些檔案的參照。"

#: answer/df53b7a2-1b1e-4f5d-99df-b9a7a1da91e9/label
msgid "No, the file names in the project are an essential part of the metadata"
msgstr "不，計畫中的檔案名稱是後設資料中不可或缺的一部分"

#: answer/2f695e7c-0661-4b43-ba55-1a82a2c706ef/label
msgid "Yes, all metadata is also explicitly available elsewhere"
msgstr "是，所有後設資料也會在其他地方明確提供"

#: question/b1f62b06-e69a-41be-8d16-1d73b9b75cd2/title
msgid "Will you be using persistent identifiers to refer to data within the project?"
msgstr "您是否會在計畫中使用持續識別碼來參照資料？"

#: question/b1f62b06-e69a-41be-8d16-1d73b9b75cd2/text
msgid "Especially for large projects, referring to data internally via a persistent identifier system can be helpful as such a system can help to keep track of data that moves to a new location."
msgstr "對於大型計畫而言，透過持續識別碼 (persistent identifier) 系統在內部引用資料特別有幫助，因為此類系統能協助追蹤遷移至新位置的資料。"

#: reference/d9ddb6db-2afd-45c0-8d25-f50208c53aa4/label
msgid "The Handle System"
msgstr "Handle 系統"

#: reference/06ca6750-b48d-42fc-b350-8d98b462b458/label
msgid "Handbook on Persistent Identifiers"
msgstr "持續識別碼手冊"

#: reference/e9091f21-22a1-4f5e-b8e1-6e3e4b2f8dca/label
#: reference/b0f4ce3b-4dcd-467f-92e1-07c4f97004b7/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on creating resolvable identifiers"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的可解析識別碼建立指南"

#: reference/8652cd42-4f7c-4b50-9828-5c7b71034ba6/label
#: reference/4cb74793-c4c8-4013-aeb4-2a60a36396a5/label
msgid "RDMkit on data organisation"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料組織頁面"

#: reference/525e23cd-1c2e-4698-8c23-b5f7671149ca/label
msgid "DMEG on File Naming and Folder Structure"
msgstr "DMEG (Data Management Expert Guide) 中的檔案命名與資料夾結構"

#: question/b08fe063-33f8-4380-b3a9-ba1e586dedf2/title
msgid "What existing data formats/types will you be using?"
msgstr "您將使用哪些既有資料格式或資料類型？"

#: question/b08fe063-33f8-4380-b3a9-ba1e586dedf2/text
msgid ""
"Have you identified types of data that you will use that are used by others too? Some types of data (for example \"images\" or \"tables\") are used by many different projects. For such data, often common standards exist (in our example \"JPG\" and \"CSV\" [comma separated values]) that help to make these data reusable. Are you using such common data formats?\n"
"\n"
"Please make sure you list all the data types that are important for your project. You should make sure also to list the formats used in any data sets that you are re-using."
msgstr ""
"您是否已確認本計畫會使用的常用資料類型？有些資料類型（例如「圖像」或「表格」）會被許多不同計畫使用。這類資料通常已有通用標準格式，例如 JPG 或 CSV（逗號分隔值），有助於提升資料可再次使用的可能性。您是否會使用這類通用資料格式？\n"
"\n"
"請列出本計畫中重要的所有資料類型，也請一併列出您將再次使用的資料集所採用的資料格式。"

#: question/f00cf643-5368-458a-97d4-b463c2000c66/title
msgid "Data format/type"
msgstr "資料格式／類型"

#: question/f00cf643-5368-458a-97d4-b463c2000c66/text
msgid "You will be presented with suggestions from [FAIRSharing](https://fairsharing.org/), but you also have the option to manually enter the data format/type that is not listed there."
msgstr "系統會顯示來自 [FAIRSharing](https://fairsharing.org/) 的建議項目，但您也可以手動輸入未列出的資料格式／類型。"

#: question/ecff019a-d4e6-44c6-a8fe-c84eb15ed8b7/title
msgid "Is this a standard data format widely used by researchers in this field?"
msgstr "這是否是一種在本領域研究人員之間被廣泛使用的標準資料格式？"

#: question/8bd3d76a-4f69-4a1e-82dd-5416739720b3/title
msgid "Why are you using a non-standard format?"
msgstr "您為什麼使用非標準格式？"

#: answer/2da70314-879e-46f5-a1da-2794d71a12d3/label
msgid "There is no standardised format for this data type"
msgstr ""

#: answer/6c26d57b-468c-42ba-a01c-05d1334d0a6e/label
msgid "It is optimised for processing speed and/or volume"
msgstr ""

#: answer/ab19f42e-6204-409e-aa6d-6d87783cce44/label
msgid "Another reason"
msgstr "其他原因"

#: question/ea7420ef-3de3-4ca8-9ff8-ac1cdb0e506f/title
msgid "What other reason do you have for not using a standard file format for this type?"
msgstr "您不使用此類型標準檔案格式的其他原因是什麼？"

#: question/ced5a7c2-4034-4763-a1d5-3cb815cdfddb/title
msgid "Does this data format enable sharing and long term archiving?"
msgstr "此資料格式是否有助於資料分享與長期典藏？"

#: question/ced5a7c2-4034-4763-a1d5-3cb815cdfddb/text
msgid ""
"Complicated (binary) file formats tend to change over time, and software may not stay compatible with older versions. Also, some formats (e.g. DOC, XLS) hamper long term usability by making use of patents or being hampered by restrictive licensing. \n"
"\n"
"Ideally a format should be simple, text only, completely described, not restricted by copyrights, and implemented in different software packages."
msgstr ""
"複雜的（二進位）檔案格式往往會隨時間改變，而操作的軟體也可能無法持續相容於舊版本的檔案格式。此外，某些格式，例如 DOC、XLS 因涉及專利或受限於嚴格的授權條款，會妨礙資料的長期可用性。\n"
"\n"
"理想的檔案格式應具備以下特性：結構簡單、純文字、規格完整公開、不受著作權限制，且可由不同軟體套件支援。"

#: question/bf32374c-b24e-4b03-9898-a753cff56fcf/title
msgid "Will you convert to a file format more suitable for archiving later?"
msgstr "您稍後是否會轉換成更適合典藏的檔案格式？"

#: answer/7d8dc2f5-2699-4fb3-8bf6-e620868a0583/advice
msgid "You may need to reserve time and budget for this"
msgstr "您可能需要為此預留時間與預算"

#: question/ba9e42fc-2bf5-413f-85de-003f981aaf81/title
msgid "What volume of data of this type will you be working with?"
msgstr "您將處理多少此類型資料？"

#: answer/7d3857a2-bb7d-4355-b2ca-bd6beb7cc3ea/label
msgid "So small that it is not a problem"
msgstr "資料量很少，不至於成為問題"

#: answer/c2bc3d0b-a11b-4831-bd2c-5235dbf868b7/label
#: answer/ec502175-376d-4bf3-a055-c4f7d7639103/label
msgid "I can specify the total amount"
msgstr "我可以說明總資料量"

#: question/4ae6452a-4ca6-434c-8453-7e3872e41847/title
msgid "Data volume in Gigabytes"
msgstr "資料量（GB）"

#: question/4ae6452a-4ca6-434c-8453-7e3872e41847/text
#: answer/24dbd191-2d0c-4267-b858-d9063b21a486/advice
msgid "Specify an approximation of the expected data volume"
msgstr "請估算預期的資料量"

#: answer/24dbd191-2d0c-4267-b858-d9063b21a486/label
msgid "I can specify the number of files/subjects and the size of each"
msgstr "我可以具體說明檔案數／受試者數，以及每個單位的資料量"

#: question/448403e9-578b-4155-9017-d4aa9119ea6a/title
msgid "Number of files/subjects"
msgstr "檔案數／受試者數"

#: question/624cfadf-6177-47b7-9ba8-b80b68aef0fd/title
msgid "Rough average size of each file/subject in gigabytes"
msgstr "每個檔案／每位受試者的概略平均資料量（單位：GB）"

#: question/192fc5d3-dc2a-495c-8f24-f59a4c5d95c9/title
msgid "Is this data format completely described?"
msgstr "這種資料格式是否已有完整的描述？"

#: question/192fc5d3-dc2a-495c-8f24-f59a4c5d95c9/text
msgid "Formats like XLS or SQL are very flexible; they can be adapted to many different uses, and this makes them good for interoperability. However, their flexibility also makes that it is not immediately obvious from the file structure how it can be used. The data needs a proper *description* in order for others (or yourself at a later time) to be able to unambiguously understand what it contains."
msgstr "XLS 或 SQL 這類格式相當有彈性；它們可以因應不同用途進行調整，因此有助於資料的可相互操作性。然而，正因為這種彈性，單從檔案結構本身往往無法立即理解資料可以如何被使用。因此，資料必須搭配適當的*描述*，他人（或未來的自己）才能清楚且不產生歧義地理解檔案內容。"

#: answer/14503afc-3fe3-4e28-8f2d-81c065ee7565/advice
msgid "Plan time and budget for either documenting this data or for conversion to a well-described specific format."
msgstr "請規劃時間與預算，用於記錄這些資料，或將其轉換為描述完整的特定格式。"

#: reference/6c37835d-2aa5-4a40-92e7-28c3a8cc6752/label
msgid "DMEG on Fomats and Conversion"
msgstr "DMEG 的格式與轉換頁面"

#: question/5ba53879-eb48-47f2-a73b-f7f7d83bf030/title
#: resourcePage/93b54fa8-a2f2-4f32-b081-1fbe293f0a5e/title
msgid "Will you be using new types of data?"
msgstr "您是否會使用新的資料類型？"

#: question/5ba53879-eb48-47f2-a73b-f7f7d83bf030/text
msgid "Sometimes the type of data you collect can not be stored in a commonly used data format. In such cases you may need to make your own, keeping interoperability as high as possible."
msgstr "有時您所蒐集的資料類型無法以常用的資料格式儲存。在這種情況下，您可能需要自行設計格式，並盡可能維持其可相互操作性。"

#: answer/c470de83-0a9b-4d7d-a2cd-903bfbedc8d1/label
msgid "No, all of my data will fit in common formats"
msgstr "否，我所有資料都適用常見格式"

#: answer/bf76127e-0497-46eb-8b5d-e4cfcb84f622/label
msgid "Yes, I will need to use custom formats for some of my data"
msgstr "是，我需要為部分資料使用自訂格式"

#: question/ae235844-e3b6-461c-8c1d-668148dbf53b/title
msgid "Will you need to add fields in your data format to a data type registry?"
msgstr "您是否需要將資料格式中的欄位加入資料類型登錄冊？"

#: question/ae235844-e3b6-461c-8c1d-668148dbf53b/text
msgid "Even if the data format you are using is unique to your project, the discrete data items should be reused or reusable as much as possible. Data type registries can help with that."
msgstr "即使您使用的資料格式是該計畫所特有的，各個離散資料項目仍應盡可能可再次使用。資料類型登錄冊能對此有所幫助。"

#: answer/48ed91ec-5dbc-497a-9f84-f26daa60c0bd/label
msgid "No, all of my data types are described in a data type registry already"
msgstr "否，我所有資料類型都已在資料類型登錄冊中描述"

#: answer/e4fdba2a-f6e6-4087-99a6-0e00c1bcd5f7/label
msgid "Yes, I will add new types to an existing data type registry"
msgstr "是，我會將新類型加入既有資料類型登錄冊"

#: answer/28c5197f-a3fe-4b96-b0fb-83e271155a95/label
msgid "Yes, I will create my own data type registry"
msgstr "是，我會建立自己的資料類型登錄冊"

#: question/7fe217e0-9af0-422f-a45b-6873f0344bcd/title
msgid "Which data type registries will you use?"
msgstr "您將使用哪些資料類型登錄冊？"

#: question/b211f896-b363-4978-9423-212644ff5d72/title
msgid "Do you need to create vocabularies or ontologies for any of your data items?"
msgstr "您是否需要為任何資料項目建立詞彙表或知識本體 (ontology)？"

#: question/b211f896-b363-4978-9423-212644ff5d72/text
msgid "For good interoperability the use of controlled vocabularies for each discrete data item is advisable. If such vocabularies exist, it is best to reuse those."
msgstr "為了達到良好的可相互操作性，我們建議每一個單獨的資料項目都使用控制詞彙。若已有相關控制詞彙，應優先再次使用。"

#: answer/efe50d9c-4dc2-49c5-ae61-1dc8ff0d7655/label
msgid "No, suitable public controlled vocabularies or ontologies exist for all of my data types"
msgstr "否，所有資料類型都有合適的公開控制詞彙或知識本體 (ontology)可用"

#: answer/668ecd34-4413-4aa9-8921-616325766ec0/label
msgid "Yes, I will make and publish a vocabulary or ontology for some of my data"
msgstr "是，我會為部分資料建立並發布詞彙表或知識本體 (ontology)"

#: question/76cf4d79-dafe-4d89-9958-047ea4b977ee/title
msgid "Will you be mapping your terms to existing vocabularies or ontologies?"
msgstr "您是否會將您的術語對應至既有詞彙表或知識本體 (ontology)？"

#: question/76cf4d79-dafe-4d89-9958-047ea4b977ee/text
msgid "Mapping even part of the terms from your own vocabulary to other existing vocabularies or ontologies can make a real difference for the interoperability of your data."
msgstr "即使只將您自訂詞彙中的部分術語對應至其他既有詞彙表或知識本體 (ontology)，也能大幅提升資料的可相互操作性。"

#: question/a9103296-915a-4bdf-b259-116775d5e676/title
msgid "How will you design your new data format?"
msgstr "您將如何設計新資料格式？"

#: answer/bda912f3-14a7-4242-b293-025f1b19892d/label
msgid "There is a closely related more generic and open format that I can specialise"
msgstr ""

#: answer/b4334e27-3e6c-4215-b4cb-f60eabd9c61e/label
msgid "I will use a Linked Data format"
msgstr "我會採用資料連結 (Linked Data) 格式"

#: answer/974fa3ea-4047-4006-a49c-f7972bf9c961/label
msgid "I will use a completely custom data format"
msgstr "我會使用完全自訂的資料格式"

#: question/caba60b1-57b3-4288-8d3e-aa3542c28027/title
msgid "Will you describe your new data format for others?"
msgstr "您是否會向他人說明新資料格式？"

#: answer/057e84be-3329-4fa2-9cc8-d37f53a44cd0/label
msgid "No, this is not needed"
msgstr "不，這不需要"

#: answer/252757f4-e4ed-4c3f-8c13-b14f55133dfe/label
msgid "Yes, I will register my standards at a data standards registry"
msgstr "是，我會將我的標準登錄至資料標準登錄冊"

#: question/f87c331d-794a-42c8-a910-61a2a9110dab/title
msgid "Will you be acquiring data using measurement equipment?"
msgstr "您是否會使用量測設備取得資料？"

#: question/f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc/title
msgid "Specify what data sets you will acquire using measurement equipment"
msgstr "請列出您將使用量測設備取得的資料集"

#: question/f5fef09d-ade5-4019-b089-f05bd89c34bc/text
#: question/b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa/text
msgid "You can use any name for the data set, make sure that it identifies the data set to yourself."
msgstr "您可以為資料集使用任何名稱，但請確保這個名稱能讓您自己辨識該資料集。"

#: question/a077aec4-83d2-45c2-8d9f-75a391bdee20/title
#: question/d87a239f-9aee-4d6a-a5f6-fa83c73e67e1/title
#: question/b0949d09-d179-4491-9fb4-14b0deb9f862/title
msgid "Data set:"
msgstr "資料集："

#: question/ee59664e-4026-4796-a42a-e8003df6dadf/title
msgid "Who will do the measurements? And where?"
msgstr "誰將進行量測？地點在哪裡？"

#: question/ee59664e-4026-4796-a42a-e8003df6dadf/text
msgid "Are there easily accessible specialized service providers for data capture?"
msgstr "是否有容易取用、且專門提供資料擷取服務的供應商？"

#: answer/44ef09a4-5a78-439d-9fb4-940d3d84bfab/label
msgid "Experts in the project, with our own equipment"
msgstr "計畫內的專家，並使用自有設備"

#: answer/eb0b9a82-0379-47c3-967f-b35b40129af2/label
msgid "Experts in the project, at a specialised infrastructure"
msgstr ""

#: answer/f2784b7e-b0ed-4973-9d68-954c5c24e8bb/label
msgid "External party"
msgstr "外部團體"

#: answer/f2784b7e-b0ed-4973-9d68-954c5c24e8bb/advice
msgid "consider making them partner in the project"
msgstr "可考慮邀請他們成為計畫合作夥伴"

#: question/aa27852a-00f4-44a4-a85c-0e0fd3ac20d1/title
msgid "Has formal ownership of the data been established?"
msgstr "是否已建立資料的正式所有權 (formal ownership)？"

#: answer/786edd0d-ae07-489c-b078-423c18e02043/label
msgid "The party measuring the data owns it"
msgstr "量測資料的一方擁有資料"

#: answer/306f7ef4-97fd-47b0-84de-f192cb94ea3a/label
msgid "The project partners acquire full ownership"
msgstr "計畫合作夥伴取得完整所有權"

#: answer/399245d4-7988-461c-b940-ee813a1c99b1/label
#: answer/8197cf1c-999a-43ae-9e29-bb5d0452052b/label
#: answer/82ef3ee8-461e-4f5b-a66a-2d4aaccbe68b/label
#: answer/17443e43-bc5a-49ce-8197-6997e9cf3d41/label
#: answer/a3286c6a-ce1b-4ff0-8cee-9686d0bd1e72/label
#: answer/620b1090-2a57-4f3c-b336-97c9e95da637/label
msgid "We have made other arrangements"
msgstr "我們已有其他安排"

#: question/f0a474ac-21b5-4b6a-9fd5-b9c3f8882055/title
msgid "Has responsibility for long term safe keeping of the raw data been established? Who will deal with data publication?"
msgstr "是否已確立長期保存原始資料的負責單位或人員？誰會將資料公開發布 (data publication)？"

#: answer/b10cd3bf-ecd6-4fa1-a9c4-d8d974de714c/label
msgid "The measuring party will publish it after a fixed embargo period"
msgstr "量測方會在固定延後開放期限後發布資料"

#: answer/a3393cc1-3393-45ba-ba91-e447bf755eb7/label
msgid "The measuring party will publish it when the project tells them to"
msgstr "量測方會依計畫通知發布資料"

#: answer/350fa8cc-ecc8-40cc-a50e-1d87405970b1/label
msgid "The measuring party will delete the data, the project partners will deal with data publication"
msgstr "量測方會刪除資料，由計畫合作夥伴負責發布資料"

#: question/e33ae210-62fe-4665-b836-e71660325a06/title
msgid "Specify instruments used for data collection"
msgstr ""

#: question/e33ae210-62fe-4665-b836-e71660325a06/text
msgid "Specify what technical instruments you are using to collect the data."
msgstr "請說明您用於蒐集資料的技術儀器。"

#: question/2426addd-293b-4829-b87b-f3dd6b594516/title
msgid "Instrument name"
msgstr "儀器名稱"

#: question/45b61cd4-057a-40ff-873f-5558acf3568c/title
msgid "Instrument description"
msgstr "儀器說明"

#: question/bce52f7f-2256-4afc-9801-2e4da8111470/title
msgid "Is the equipment completely standard and well described?"
msgstr "設備是否完全標準化，且已有完善的說明？"

#: question/bce52f7f-2256-4afc-9801-2e4da8111470/text
msgid "If the technology is very much under development, you may want to come back later to understand exactly how the measurements have been made. Is the measurement equipment and protocol sufficiently standard that you will be able to explain how it is done or refer to a standard explanation?"
msgstr "如果該技術仍處於非常初期的研發階段，您之後可能會需要回頭確認量測究竟是如何進行的。量測設備與協定是否已充分標準化，以致您將來能夠說明其進行方式，或引用一套標準的說明？"

#: answer/cba473be-2489-4387-8877-ce49cf95a304/label
msgid "Very well described and known"
msgstr "已有充分描述且廣為人知"

#: answer/526db9ec-a5a1-4431-9cc3-751fc6625217/label
msgid "Less well described or not completely standard"
msgstr "描述較不完整，或尚未完全標準化"

#: answer/526db9ec-a5a1-4431-9cc3-751fc6625217/advice
msgid "Take pictures of the instruments for documentation, and keep copies of any documentation."
msgstr "請拍攝儀器照片以供文件記錄，並保存任何文件副本。"

#: question/28b99b8e-3a0c-45c5-8d2b-b778a7d43323/title
msgid "Is special care needed to get the raw data ready for processing?"
msgstr "原始資料在進行後續處理前，是否需要特別準備？"

#: question/28b99b8e-3a0c-45c5-8d2b-b778a7d43323/text
msgid "Where does the data come from? And who will need it? Sometimes the raw data is measured somewhere else than where the primary processing is taking place. In such cases the ingestion or transport of the primary data may take special planning. You also need to make sure that data is secure and that data integrity is guaranteed."
msgstr "資料從哪裡來？誰會需要這些資料？有時原始資料的量測地點，與主要處理作業的地點不同。在這些情況下，原始資料的匯入或傳輸可能需要特別規劃。您也需要確保資料安全，並保障資料完整性。"

#: answer/b541e78e-3300-4e7d-ac36-93d7b5ebf031/label
msgid "No, this is all fine"
msgstr "否，目前不需要特別準備"

#: answer/065a500b-53c0-487f-9096-00fd6f7234a6/label
msgid "Yes, lets explore this"
msgstr "是，需要進一步檢視"

#: question/2c5fd209-1ff5-4c34-b6e4-2bf1228e97de/title
msgid "Is the data format established?"
msgstr "資料格式是否已經確立？"

#: question/2c5fd209-1ff5-4c34-b6e4-2bf1228e97de/text
msgid "Has the storage and transport format of the primary data been established between the people responsible for the measurement and the people responsible for the processing?"
msgstr "負責量測的人員與負責處理資料的人員，是否已確定主要資料的儲存與傳輸格式？"

#: question/2e8d6e55-36ea-46eb-a921-65e550bce5dc/title
msgid "How will the raw data be transported?"
msgstr "原始資料會如何傳輸？"

#: answer/489c3813-c010-4197-b54a-41e742aa8f35/label
msgid "No transport is needed, analysis is done where it is obtained"
msgstr "不需傳輸，會在取得原始資料的地點進行分析"

#: answer/8c9c3d59-cd51-4303-9202-519e30998e1a/label
msgid "On physical media"
msgstr "使用實體儲存媒體傳輸"

#: question/31da89a7-4d04-4345-a414-ea1226377df7/title
msgid "Is sufficient writing and reading capacity available for the physical media?"
msgstr "實體儲存媒體的讀寫能力是否足夠？"

#: question/31da89a7-4d04-4345-a414-ea1226377df7/text
msgid "Has time been reserved on any tape/disk reading and writing stations?"
msgstr "是否已預留磁帶或磁碟讀寫設備的使用時間？"

#: answer/be674d81-cadb-470a-acf9-7365175b533d/label
#: answer/44dfd6cb-b3ce-41a4-bca8-9689be8df67c/label
msgid "Yes, has been taken care of"
msgstr "是，已處理"

#: answer/ca02196a-aae3-42aa-b6cb-aeb1b86f752a/label
msgid "Via the network"
msgstr "透過網路傳輸"

#: question/3d942d91-39a2-4d2f-a27a-6fe57deb87ff/title
msgid "Is sufficient network capacity available?"
msgstr "是否有足夠的網路傳輸容量？"

#: question/3d942d91-39a2-4d2f-a27a-6fe57deb87ff/text
msgid "Can the volume of data be accommodated by the standard network connection? Has a special network connection (e.g. light path) that is needed been reserved?"
msgstr "標準網路連線是否足以負荷這筆資料量？是否已預留所需的特殊網路連線（例如專用光路徑）？"

#: reference/5b5a7569-939f-4304-9d79-f71e383d7ad2/label
#: reference/2a84091c-43eb-49c1-b5d8-78b37dcb3cc5/label
msgid "RDMkit on Data Transfer"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料傳輸頁面"

#: question/129f74a4-dc91-4cc7-aee3-b384c8ea30dd/title
msgid "Is data integrity guaranteed during this stage?"
msgstr "此階段是否能確保資料完整性？"

#: question/129f74a4-dc91-4cc7-aee3-b384c8ea30dd/text
msgid "Do you have any means of identifying whether the raw data has been transferred error free and has not been tampered with?"
msgstr "您是否有方法可確認原始資料在傳輸過程中未發生錯誤，且未遭到竄改？"

#: question/0ebd660b-364a-4357-9044-c4dc0293a9ba/title
msgid "Is data security guaranteed during this stage?"
msgstr "此階段是否能確保資料安全？"

#: question/0ebd660b-364a-4357-9044-c4dc0293a9ba/text
msgid "Are the raw data encrypted or otherwise protected from theft or leaks at either site or during transport? You could e.g. use a light path or a virtual private network if you transport the data over the net."
msgstr "原始資料在任一地點或傳輸過程中，是否已加密，或以其他方式防止遭竊或外洩？若透過網路傳輸資料，可使用光路徑或虛擬私人網路等方式。"

#: answer/c30318bd-f2ca-4328-ae27-a14870916543/label
msgid "No, not needed"
msgstr "否，不需要"

#: question/ba38b16d-2154-4372-b445-7854a6e90443/title
msgid "Will you be using quality processes?"
msgstr "您是否會採用品質管控流程？"

#: question/ba38b16d-2154-4372-b445-7854a6e90443/text
msgid "Specify how you guarantee that measurements measure what you think they should measure, and how you establish completeness and correctness of data and metadata."
msgstr "請說明您如何確認量測結果確實符合預期，以及如何檢查資料與後設資料的完整性與正確性。"

#: question/e458d2eb-ba1e-4c4c-8619-5f8f431715b4/title
msgid "Are you calibrating measurements?"
msgstr "您是否會進行量測校準？"

#: question/d5ab8298-9382-455c-8241-f64d3cc54ffe/title
msgid "Are you running repeat samples or are you repeating measurements in order to monitor consistency of the results?"
msgstr "您是否會重複蒐集樣本或進行重複測量，以監測結果的一致性？"

#: question/ecdc6c3f-249a-4d82-822c-649754201981/title
msgid "Are you running standardised data capture or recording?"
msgstr ""

#: question/01b70401-021b-4fe7-9073-570ecb3b320c/title
msgid "Are you doing Data Entry validation?"
msgstr "您是否會進行資料驗證？"

#: question/01b70401-021b-4fe7-9073-570ecb3b320c/text
msgid "Are you checking that data that is entered e.g. in forms is satisfying criteria of reasonability?"
msgstr "您是否有確認輸入的資料（例如表單資料）符合合理性準則？"

#: question/56354f8a-31df-40fc-aeae-67d45af560b5/title
msgid "Are you using data peer review?"
msgstr "您是否會進行資料的同儕評審？"

#: question/56354f8a-31df-40fc-aeae-67d45af560b5/text
msgid "Do you make sure all collected is cross-checked by colleagues?"
msgstr "您是否會確保所有蒐集到的資料都由同儕交叉檢查？"

#: question/e2401b56-5d7e-42c6-bb97-c8bede39b4b0/title
msgid "Are you using controlled vocabularies where possible?"
msgstr "您是否會盡可能使用控制詞彙？"

#: question/e2401b56-5d7e-42c6-bb97-c8bede39b4b0/text
msgid "Controlled vocabularies should be used to limit what can be entered in most text fields. "
msgstr "應使用控制詞彙來限制大多數文字欄位的輸入內容。 "

#: question/839ea5fc-9cc1-497e-91bf-c05b34847a5e/title
msgid "Are you using any other quality processes?"
msgstr "您是否採用其他品質管控流程？"

#: question/e24167a2-14ec-445d-b205-fb6c7e24a7d1/title
msgid "What other quality processes do you use?"
msgstr "您還會採用哪些其他品質管控流程？"

#: question/1b919e1e-a4fe-4be6-a976-862b82aab9b0/title
msgid "Are you measuring samples for which the outcome is known in order to monitor consistency?"
msgstr "您是否會量測結果已知的樣本，以監測結果的一致性？"

#: reference/5414f646-58a7-403d-b269-09526c8a19fa/label
#: reference/148f612f-722b-420f-b1ca-e9ac6a6be8cb/label
msgid "RDMkit on Data Quality"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料品質頁面"

#: question/135aa977-ecc2-4bb8-aa55-2def9d9d6040/title
#: question/c520b63c-cc35-4789-9d98-cc87b59ebcf1/title
msgid "Who else could be interested in using this data?"
msgstr "還有哪些人可能會有興趣使用這些資料？"

#: answer/f5a4d36c-4ce8-4ab6-8e5e-d7a2418c77c7/label
#: answer/e862d2cb-967d-4f3b-b845-403259c79751/label
msgid "Just us"
msgstr "只有我們"

#: answer/515cac06-d101-4af1-95ef-33fd6a2da8b0/label
#: answer/1566d3af-666b-456a-9ace-daee8d690d6e/label
msgid "Other researchers working in the same field of research"
msgstr "在相同研究領域工作的其他研究人員"

#: answer/9270c716-f997-43e1-bc2a-55687e149dbd/label
#: answer/0c630b6f-8aec-4153-818d-90fbb559072f/label
msgid "Researchers working in other fields"
msgstr "在其他領域工作的研究人員"

#: question/1ca28160-8b73-48fe-8b74-18c0f5cb56df/title
#: question/41a1b4ba-8cd5-47fe-a7be-06cccf9a1688/title
msgid "How do you think other researchers can use this data?"
msgstr "您認為其他研究人員可以如何使用這份資料？"

#: question/f038bd46-ee4e-4f53-b7ea-482381c2c855/title
msgid "Do you have any non-equipment data capture?"
msgstr "您是否有不透過儀器設備進行的資料擷取？"

#: question/f038bd46-ee4e-4f53-b7ea-482381c2c855/text
msgid "Does the data you collect contain non-equipment captured data such as questionnaires, case report forms, electronic patient records?"
msgstr "您所蒐集的資料是否包含非由設備取得的資料，例如問卷、個案報告表 (case report forms) 或電子病歷？"

#: question/85079340-7b80-4dc7-86ae-cc5f599ec737/title
msgid "Will you be collecting questionnaires?"
msgstr "您是否會蒐集問卷？"

#: question/36a5ed1e-ecd5-4b86-a719-f1196e376a52/title
msgid "Will you be collecting case report forms?"
msgstr "您是否會蒐集個案報告表？"

#: question/7e456b72-72a1-427d-8e75-9da096bc9806/title
msgid "Will you be collecting data from electronic patient records?"
msgstr "您是否會從電子病歷中蒐集資料？"

#: question/4eb1bd6f-5d10-4b0a-aab1-715facc29cbb/title
msgid "Has access to the electronic patient records been arranged?"
msgstr "是否已安排電子病歷的取用方式？"

#: answer/03f16c20-4299-4511-a893-79da17a16b50/label
#: answer/1c6da256-72d5-45b1-842e-c1458e6d2e21/label
#: answer/4dd69e44-097b-42fc-98a4-4ce379453d46/label
msgid "Not yet"
msgstr "尚未"

#: question/b642c31d-a512-4ca7-8743-a2e0254006fa/title
msgid "Please list all non-equipment data sets you will collect"
msgstr "請列出您將蒐集的所有非由設備取得或記錄的資料集"

#: question/934f6592-a032-4ada-91b2-4448d740d157/text
msgid "Briefly describe the contents of this data set"
msgstr "請簡要描述此資料集的內容"

#: question/4e84a44f-e66b-42f5-bb42-7e6c4bd3b79b/title
msgid "How will the data be captured?"
msgstr "您將如何擷取資料？"

#: answer/407560bc-705a-4885-85d6-4f61fe58eeed/label
msgid "All immediately in digital form"
msgstr "所有資料都會直接以數位形式記錄"

#: answer/374974a6-2c51-4508-aa93-9ef8f1ef65fd/label
msgid "Data will first be on paper"
msgstr "資料最初會以紙本形式記錄"

#: question/32f5bc5c-6bc6-4df0-849f-1619951c5b98/title
msgid "Who will do the data entry?"
msgstr "誰會負責資料輸入？"

#: answer/9d51aae1-ca1b-4267-b0df-d43dc85f5bc6/label
msgid "A specialised team"
msgstr ""

#: answer/9660950a-41d7-4c3b-a6fd-97e58c8fa412/label
msgid "One of the members of the project team"
msgstr "計畫團隊的其中一名成員"

#: question/a205f751-cbb6-4f58-a692-2ba450e1e133/title
msgid "Did you arrange who will make the data digitally available to you?"
msgstr "您是否有安排是誰會負責將資料以數位形式提供給您？"

#: question/36d40d39-894b-4c1a-9e9c-feaddef09df3/title
msgid "Will all data be collected by a single person?"
msgstr "所有資料都會由同一位人員蒐集嗎？"

#: answer/4ea74c15-c1d2-46c1-9bd6-8fe251648a4e/label
msgid "This data will be collected by one person"
msgstr "這些資料會由同一位人員蒐集"

#: answer/d988687b-41e9-4be4-8472-031938d13c37/label
msgid "More people will capture data"
msgstr "資料會由多人蒐集"

#: question/68956a97-6138-4538-9968-e7a925f299cc/title
msgid "Is there a risk of different interpretations? Subjectivity?"
msgstr "資料蒐集過程是否可能有不同解讀或主觀判斷的風險？"

#: answer/2a1261d5-6678-4181-8ab9-b9671546a02a/label
msgid "The data capture is objective"
msgstr "資料擷取過程是客觀的"

#: answer/c4443193-11f5-4a9e-9444-fabf575d9246/label
msgid "There are internal controls to deal with interperation differences"
msgstr "有內部控管機制可處理解讀差異"

#: answer/2dc09f04-0613-45e5-bba9-18ffe4db8a82/label
msgid "We accept the risk of different interpretations"
msgstr "我們接受資料可能有不同解讀的風險"

#: answer/8bf15202-b0dc-4be7-8093-72349c7b65c9/label
msgid "We do validation afterwards"
msgstr "我們會在事後進行驗證"

#: question/ab4b3f39-dfab-45a5-9489-2d46ceacbb73/title
msgid "Is there a data integration tool that can handle and combine all the data types you are dealing with in your project?"
msgstr "是否有資料整合工具可以處理並整合計畫中的所有資料類型？"

#: question/20a9685a-5560-43dc-bb13-73c434f8d666/title
msgid "Can all data be brought into the same format, e.g. RDF?"
msgstr "是否能將所有資料轉換為相同格式，例如資源描述框架 (RDF)？"

#: reference/f57c5313-6ccb-4eb4-b79a-fdbd3c72bc48/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on tools to convert data to RDF"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的「將資料轉換為 RDF 的工具」頁面"

#: question/2e394765-d87d-4c1e-9f90-d8d2a06826e3/title
msgid "What software will you be using to collect all data?"
msgstr "您會使用哪些軟體來彙整所有資料？"

#: answer/ffcb476b-8321-42d6-84fb-8347fcff1011/label
msgid "We will not use a data warehouse"
msgstr "我們不會使用資料倉儲系統"

#: answer/cce63dc5-5ac7-4706-ab5a-4a204ef380e3/label
msgid "TranSMART"
msgstr "TranSMART"

#: answer/aa23e0c5-45ca-4061-9e81-04fc9d56c97c/label
msgid "Software not listed here"
msgstr "此處未列出的軟體"

#: answer/2be7a50f-f044-4649-a163-2197a13e5edc/label
msgid "We will develop our own"
msgstr "我們會自行開發軟體"

#: question/677c07f0-a709-4d77-946f-78735a88c858/title
msgid "Why will you develop your own software?"
msgstr "您為什麼會選擇自行開發軟體？"

#: answer/2bfd3b78-6013-42b3-ba13-51041aac5618/label
msgid "Nothing like this has ever been done before"
msgstr "目前沒有類似的軟體"

#: answer/62028d39-f35d-4b09-ad7a-a0772d45573e/label
msgid "Existing solutions are not suitable"
msgstr "既有解決方案不符合需求"

#: answer/62028d39-f35d-4b09-ad7a-a0772d45573e/advice
msgid "Did you consider collaborating to improve an existing solution?"
msgstr "您是否曾考慮與他人合作，改進既有解決方案？"

#: reference/6c8abc44-e975-4e0e-882d-d231f1c45315/description
msgid "Planning data integration processes"
msgstr "規劃資料整合流程"

#: question/02b3fed1-0b50-4a80-b8b6-a225a1107022/title
msgid "Will you monitor data integrity once it has been collected?"
msgstr "資料蒐集完成後，您是否會監控資料完整性？"

#: question/02b3fed1-0b50-4a80-b8b6-a225a1107022/text
msgid "Working with large amounts of heterogenous data in a larger research group can have implications for the data integrity. How do you make sure every step of the workflow is done with the right version of the data? How do you handle the situation when a mistake is uncovered? Will you be able to redo the strict minimum data handling?"
msgstr "在較大型研究團隊中處理大量類型多樣、格式不一的資料，可能會影響資料完整性。您如何確保工作流程的每個步驟都使用正確版本的資料？若發現錯誤，您會如何處理？您是否能只重做必要範圍內的資料處理？"

#: answer/033e0538-5322-49c8-b537-9375eb86fd90/advice
msgid "If you are working with multiple people on a complex project, it could be causing problems if changes are made to e.g. sample identifiers half-way the project. If there is no central information keeping, not everyone may be aware of important changes, and updates of partially run workflows could be forgotten."
msgstr "若您與多人共同執行複雜計畫，在計畫進行期間變更樣本識別碼等資訊，可能會造成問題。若沒有集中管理資訊的機制，相關人員未必都能掌握這些重要變更，而對於僅部分執行完成的工作流程，其後續更新也可能被忽略。"

#: question/e0759fdc-7ce9-4020-816d-73119f634c7e/title
msgid "Will you be keeping a master list with checksums of certified/correct/canonical/verified data?"
msgstr "您是否會保存一份主清單，列出已認證／正確／標準／已驗證資料的總和檢查碼？"

#: question/e0759fdc-7ce9-4020-816d-73119f634c7e/text
msgid "Data corruption or mistakes can happen with large amounts of files or large files. Keeping a *master list* with data checksums can be helpful to prevent expensive mistakes, because it will help detect early when data files are damaged or mixed up. It can also be helpful to keep the list under version control so that all changes are well documented."
msgstr "在處理大量檔案或較大的檔案時，有可能發生資料毀損或錯誤。建立一份包含資料總和檢查碼 (checksums) 的「*主清單 (master list)*」，有助於及早偵測檔案是否受損或被混用，從而避免代價高昂的錯誤。此外，將此清單納入版本控制，也能確保所有變更能被完整記錄。"

#: reference/b0955b59-a0a1-47ef-9850-348bc9f2d1ee/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on creating checksum files"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的「建立總和檢查碼檔案」頁面"

#: question/acb86509-e93a-4d87-a958-74def0678e10/title
msgid "Will you define a way to detect file or sample swaps, e.g. by measuring something independently?"
msgstr "您是否會訂定方法來偵測檔案或樣本是否被調換，例如透過獨立量測某些項目？"

#: reference/abcc180f-fb2f-4c97-99ce-70d96275bfdf/label
msgid "DMEG on Data Quality"
msgstr "DMEG 的資料品質頁面"

#: reference/4cbf4d06-9b4f-4088-b5e4-ab0813c5d853/label
msgid "DMEG on Data Integrity"
msgstr "DMEG 的資料完整性頁面"

#: question/49c009cb-a38c-4836-9780-8a8b3dd1cbac/title
msgid "Will you collect any data connected to a person, \"personal data\"?"
msgstr "您是否會蒐集任何與個人相關的資料，也就是「個人資料」？"

#: question/49c009cb-a38c-4836-9780-8a8b3dd1cbac/text
msgid ""
"Very many kinds of data are connected to people. If there could be a way for someone, including yourself, to find out who that person is, that is considered personal data.\n"
"\n"
"Simple examples are name, birth day or address; but there are many other data that can be personal: for example a voice recording, a combination of a location and a time (traffic flow), genetic information, or an X-ray of the skull."
msgstr ""
"許多種類的資料都與人相關。只要有方法讓某人（包括您自己）辨識出該個人，就會被視為個人資料。\n"
"\n"
"簡單例子包括姓名、出生日期或地址；但還有許多其他資料也可能屬於個人資料，例如聲音記錄、地點與時間的組合（交通流量）、基因資訊，或頭骨 X 光圖像。"

#: question/c8687abf-ac88-4bef-b1cc-7070bd039a07/title
msgid "General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) considerations"
msgstr "歐盟《個人資料保護規則》(GDPR) 相關考量"

#: question/be4651c9-9a8c-4e10-a158-61b94ca0e139/title
msgid "What legal basis are you using to collect and process the personal data?"
msgstr "您蒐集與處理個人資料時，採用的法律依據是什麼？"

#: question/be4651c9-9a8c-4e10-a158-61b94ca0e139/text
msgid ""
"[Article 6](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-6-gdpr/) (1) lists under what conditions the processing is considered lawful. Of these, **Consent** or **Public** interest are relevant when it comes to research. You should determine what legal basis (or bases) you have for processing the personal data in your project. \n"
"\n"
"Traditionally, *consent* has been the basis for processing personal data for research, but under the GDPR there cannot be an imbalance between the processor and the data subject for it to be considered to be freely given. In some countries the use of *consent* as the legal basis for processing by universities for research purposes is therefore not recommended. In those cases, public interest should probably be your legal basis. Note that if your legal basis for processing is consent, [a number of requirements](https://gdpr-info.eu/issues/consent/) exists for the consent to be considered valid under the GDPR. Consents given before the GDPR might not live up to this. \n"
"\n"
"Also note that even if *public interest* is the legal basis, other laws and research ethics standards might still require you to have consent from the subjects for performing the research.\n"
"\n"
"Please consult with the Data Protection Officer of your organisation on which legal basis to apply to your data.\n"
msgstr ""
"[第 6 條](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-6-gdpr/) 第 1 項說明在何種情況下，個人資料處理可被視為合法。就研究而言，較常見的法律依據包括「**同意**」與「**公共利益**」。請確認您的計畫處理個人資料時，是依據哪一項或哪些法律依據。\n"
"\n"
"過去，研究處理個人資料時，通常以「*同意*」作為法律依據；但依 GDPR，若資料處理者與資料主體之間存在權力不對等，就難以認定該同意是自由給予。因此，在某些國家，不建議大學以「*同意*」作為研究目的處理個人資料的法律依據。在這類情況下，較可能適合的法律依據是公共利益。若您以同意作為處理依據，請注意，同意必須符合[若干要求](https://gdpr-info.eu/issues/consent/)，才會被 GDPR 視為有效；GDPR 生效前取得的同意，不一定符合這些要求。\n"
"\n"
"另外，即使您以「*公共利益*」作為法律依據，其他法律或研究倫理標準仍可能要求您取得受試者同意，才能進行研究。\n"
"\n"
"請諮詢您組織的資料保護官，確認您的資料應適用哪一項法律依據。\n"

#: answer/c732f0b9-2f66-47f4-902f-724a44cdfd4b/advice
msgid "Note that scientific research is not considered public interest in many jurisdictions."
msgstr "請注意，在許多司法管轄區中，科學研究並不被視為公共利益。"

#: answer/73cd2dda-41ba-456b-9a4e-aa34c78f2fcf/label
msgid "We ask the data subjects for their consent"
msgstr "我們會向資料主體取得同意"

#: answer/73cd2dda-41ba-456b-9a4e-aa34c78f2fcf/advice
msgid ""
"Traditionally, *consent* has been the basis for processing personal data for research, but under the GDPR there cannot be an imbalance between the processor and the data subject for it to be considered to be freely given. In some countries the use of *consent* as the legal basis for processing by universities for research purposes is therefore not recommended. In those cases, public interest should probably be your legal basis. Note that if your legal basis for processing is consent, [a number of requirements](https://gdpr-info.eu/issues/consent/) exists for the consent to be considered valid under the GDPR. Consents given before the GDPR might not live up to this. \n"
"\n"
"Note that consent needs to be completely voluntary. If the subject gets any service or good in return for their permission, this is not considered consent. Also note that in European (GDPR) law, a data subject should be able to retract their consent at any moment."
msgstr ""
"過去，研究處理個人資料時，通常以「*同意*」作為法律依據；但依 GDPR，若資料處理者與資料主體之間存在權力不對等，就難以認定該同意是自由給予。因此，在某些國家，不建議大學以「*同意*」作為研究目的處理個人資料的法律依據。在這類情況下，較可能適合的法律依據是公共利益。若您以同意作為處理依據，請注意，同意必須符合[若干要求](https://gdpr-info.eu/issues/consent/)，才會被 GDPR 視為有效；GDPR 生效前取得的同意，不一定符合這些要求。\n"
"\n"
"請注意，同意必須完全出於自願。如果受試者因給予同意而取得任何服務或物品，該同意就不會被視為有效同意。也請注意，依歐盟《個人資料保護規則》 (GDPR)，資料主體應能在任何時候撤回同意。"

#: question/f5e162ee-1077-4ebe-a932-192bc7f67e98/title
msgid "What kind of consent will you be acquiring?"
msgstr "您將取得哪一種同意？"

#: answer/a484287c-fd7f-47ca-8dea-cdb36f48616d/label
msgid "We collect consent for our specific use of the data"
msgstr "我們會為資料的特定使用目的取得同意"

#: answer/08014631-8a8a-4efa-bd58-3766cc40c7ed/label
msgid "We collect consent for our use as well as for reuse of the data"
msgstr "我們會為資料使用與再次使用取得同意"

#: answer/3a77595a-87ae-484d-a9a6-052f312453ee/label
msgid "We will collect consent for our use of the data and for anonymisation; We will anonymise the data afterwards for reuse"
msgstr ""

#: answer/e7e4f219-5edd-468f-b042-b5f88a559c3a/label
msgid "We ask for consent for anonymisation; We will anonymise first and all further processing is on the anonymous data"
msgstr ""

#: question/61d21b4f-332b-4257-a345-bbf51b10d357/title
msgid "Explain how data subjects will be informed"
msgstr ""

#: question/61d21b4f-332b-4257-a345-bbf51b10d357/text
msgid ""
"Explain how data subjects will be informed and how data subject's requests will be handled.\n"
"\n"
"Data subjects must be informed of the purpose, the interest of the study, the type of collected data, and the potential risks to which they will be exposed.\n"
"\n"
"If the processing operation is exempted from the right to information according to the GDPR, provide a justification.\n"
"Mention the relevant document in which the responsibilities regarding the information of data subjects are indicated."
msgstr ""
"請說明將如何告知資料主體 (data subjects) 相關資訊，以及如何處理他們所提出的請求。\n"
"\n"
"資料主體必須被告知研究目的、研究的利益、所蒐集的資料類型，以及他們可能承受的潛在風險。\n"
"\n"
"若該資料處理活動依據歐盟《個人資料保護規則》(GDPR) 可免除告知義務，請提供相關說明。\n"
"並請指出載明資料主體告知責任之相關文件。"

#: question/d0e029ee-aee0-420f-bc6f-ad471410ad42/title
msgid "Will the consent form be available for re-users?"
msgstr "同意書是否會提供給再次使用者？"

#: question/d0e029ee-aee0-420f-bc6f-ad471410ad42/text
msgid ""
"It is important for re-users to know what consent items you asked exactly from participants.\n"
"\n"
"Note that the answers from participants is personal data that requires protection!"
msgstr ""
"對再利用者而言，清楚知道您當初究竟向參與者徵求了哪些具體的同意事項，是非常重要的。\n"
"\n"
"請注意，參與者所提供的回答屬於個人資料，必須受到保護！"

#: question/c6579da8-496a-4468-b567-9fb6ce472bf9/title
msgid "Describe the procedure for obtaining consent from data subjects"
msgstr "請說明向資料主體取得同意的程序"

#: question/c6579da8-496a-4468-b567-9fb6ce472bf9/text
msgid ""
"Where the processing is under consent, appropriate measures should be take to demonstrate how the data subjects have consented.\n"
"Mention the documents where the consent is established (e.g., data information sheet)."
msgstr ""
"若資料處理以同意為法律依據，應採取適當措施，確保日後能證明資料主體已表示同意。\n"
"請註明同意內容記載於哪些文件（例如資料說明書）。"

#: question/361c38f0-ce75-4157-94f1-804e4d7986c2/title
msgid "Describe how data subjects exercise their rights to their data"
msgstr "請說明資料主體如何針對其資料行使權利"

#: question/361c38f0-ce75-4157-94f1-804e4d7986c2/text
msgid "For projects involving data collection from subjects, it must be ensured the subjects can exercise all their rights."
msgstr "凡涉及向受試者蒐集資料的計畫，皆需確保受試者得以完整行使其相關權利。"

#: choice/e63d7501-86b4-40b7-9b2a-43e7c1745ae1/label
msgid "They can access the data during the project"
msgstr ""

#: choice/216661ca-3b33-4541-bfb7-d7578466e137/label
msgid "They can access the data after the project's completion"
msgstr ""

#: choice/f7a1854f-511e-44c8-b1e5-422d26024433/label
msgid "They can ask for the data to be modified after the project's completion (which may include the deletion of the data)"
msgstr ""

#: choice/dd1b03f1-2b1c-41f5-9e15-4eb14d46afcf/label
msgid "They can ask for data access to be modified during the project"
msgstr ""

#: choice/31b7d794-e805-4364-9be8-e33b132f1c0c/label
msgid "They can ask for data access to be modified after the project's completion"
msgstr ""

#: reference/f093edb7-f08c-4742-8b0e-8abe0bf6c34f/label
msgid "GDPR Chapter 3: Rights of the data subject"
msgstr "GDPR 第三章：資料主體權利"

#: answer/2a84c15c-f5ca-4471-b1fe-10f3d1231f24/advice
msgid "These are less likely"
msgstr "這些較不可能適用"

#: question/b307cc44-7896-4383-b9b0-11cf4a58f531/title
msgid "Which other?"
msgstr "是哪一項其他法律依據？"

#: question/b307cc44-7896-4383-b9b0-11cf4a58f531/text
msgid ""
"The following legal bases are unlikely for processing personal data when doing research.\n"
"\n"
"The meaning of the different options are as follows:\n"
"* Fulfil contract: we require the processing in order to fulfil our contract with the data subjects.\n"
"* Legitimate interest: data subjects all expect us to do this data processing because of who we are.\n"
"* Vital interest: we need to do this to protect the vital interests of the data subject.\n"
"* Legal requirement: we are legally obliged to do this data processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"以下法律依據在研究中處理個人資料時通常不太適用。\n"
"\n"
"各選項的意思如下：\n"
"* 履行契約：我們需要進行此處理，才能履行與資料主體之間的契約。\n"
"* 合法利益：基於我們的身分，資料主體會預期我們進行這項資料處理。\n"
"* 重大利益：我們需要進行此處理，以保護資料主體的重大利益。\n"
"* 法律義務：我們依法有義務進行這項資料處理。\n"

#: answer/1dfe0a6d-4281-4d5e-bcaa-5e20fa28a591/label
msgid "Fulfil contract"
msgstr "履行合約"

#: answer/9d5e3104-2b6b-4d95-848e-253ef069d8b3/label
msgid "Legitimate interest"
msgstr "合法利益"

#: question/c7496ece-4535-4f5d-bcf7-7845989906e9/title
msgid "State the purpose of processing the personal data"
msgstr "請說明處理個人資料的目的"

#: question/eccb8305-b78e-4e60-a4ee-094c70003b7a/title
msgid "Who are the data controller(s) of the personal data processed in the project?"
msgstr "本計畫所處理個人資料的資料控管者是誰？"

#: question/eccb8305-b78e-4e60-a4ee-094c70003b7a/text
msgid "[Article 4](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-4-gdpr/) (7): *“**‘controller’** means the natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body which, alone or jointly with others, **determines the purposes** and means of the processing of personal data; […].”* The Controller is typically the university employer of the PI, and the PI should act as a representative of her university employer and is responsible for ensuring that personal data is handled correctly in her projects. For cross-border collaborative projects the controllers of different datasets should be identified. Also, if joint controllership is considered, make sure that all parties understand their obligations, and it is probably good to define the terms for this in an agreement between the parties."
msgstr "[第 4 條](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-4-gdpr/) 第 7 款指出：「***控管者** 係指單獨或與他人共同 **決定個人資料處理之目的** 與方法之自然人或法人、公務機關、局處或其他機構……*」資料控管者通常是計畫主持人任職的大學；計畫主持人應代表其任職大學，並負責確保計畫中的個人資料受到妥善處理。對於跨國多方協作計畫，應釐清各資料集分別由誰擔任資料控管者。此外，若考慮由多方共同擔任資料控管者，請確保各方都了解自身義務；也建議各方以協議明定相關條款。"

#: answer/42a0b857-00e1-4389-bd26-cb5b924ab462/label
msgid "Please  specify the controller(s)"
msgstr "請列出資料控管者"

#: question/6cc336d2-2ae1-4ba7-92bf-00307c48dbdf/title
msgid "Controller"
msgstr "控管者"

#: question/b9619bee-6d69-4111-b1e0-6c3ea50e01f8/title
msgid "Organisation"
msgstr ""

#: question/b9619bee-6d69-4111-b1e0-6c3ea50e01f8/text
msgid "You will be presented with suggestions from [ROR](https://ror.org/), but you also have the option to manually enter the organisation that is not listed there."
msgstr ""

#: question/312ad81e-a274-4523-a6b2-2299e56422b7/title
msgid "Is there more than one controller of the personal data processed in the project?"
msgstr "計畫所處理的個人資料是否有不只一個資料控管者？"

#: answer/57a9a008-d0b0-4716-bf26-13e6eb80dc36/label
msgid "No, there is only one controller"
msgstr "否，只有一個資料控管者"

#: question/bdb07de8-6b54-41ac-b89d-21e089f01597/title
msgid "Will the parties be joint controllers?"
msgstr "各方是否會共同擔任資料控管者？"

#: question/0dda3f9c-7567-47c8-8726-23fdfbe67e33/title
msgid "Has a joint controllership agreement between the parties been established?"
msgstr "各參與方是否已建立共同資料控管者協議 (joint controllership agreement)？"

#: question/9e0fb0fd-0268-4cf3-8dfa-ba0b2a1e8e89/title
msgid "Under what GDPR category does the project data fall?"
msgstr "計畫資料屬於 GDPR 的哪一類？"

#: question/9e0fb0fd-0268-4cf3-8dfa-ba0b2a1e8e89/text
msgid ""
"The GDPR defines (sub)categories for personal data and expects data processors to be aware of and to document the categories of data that they process.\n"
"\n"
"Standard personal data  includes e.g. name, date of birth, address, (online) identifiers, contact info, account/personnel/customer or other ID numbers, appearance.\n"
"\n"
"Special  category data includes: data concerning health, Genetic data, racial or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, political opinions, religious or ideological convictions or trade union membership, criminal convictions and offences"
msgstr ""
"GDPR 定義了個人資料的類別與子類別，並期待資料處理者了解並記錄自己所處理的資料類別。\n"
"\n"
"一般個人資料包括姓名、出生日期、地址、線上識別碼、聯絡資訊、帳號／人員／客戶或其他 ID 編號、外貌等。\n"
"\n"
"特殊類別資料包括：涉及健康之資料、基因資料、種族或人種、性傾向、政治意見、宗教或意識形態信念、工會會員身分、前科與犯罪資料"

#: answer/9d5a52da-221f-4cfb-9727-8564a3a0d15b/label
msgid "Standard personal data"
msgstr "一般個人資料"

#: answer/4c42e36b-f70a-4c2d-b13a-66294bc22459/label
msgid "Special category data (plus optional additional standard personal data)"
msgstr "特殊類別資料，並可視需要加入其他一般個人資料"

#: question/f9118137-437a-47bc-b9de-b2c049eabeae/title
msgid "Which category?"
msgstr "哪一類？"

#: choice/bccae922-5281-48f8-aa9b-f1497acc9106/label
msgid "Data concerning health"
msgstr "涉及健康之資料"

#: choice/039eceea-640e-4e6c-89fb-40965956a2e7/label
msgid "Genetic data"
msgstr "基因資料"

#: choice/be1a9124-d071-46e9-8048-f8a9857fb466/label
msgid "Racial or ethnic origin"
msgstr "種族或人種"

#: choice/2d654094-e4d1-48be-b2ce-6af94e8bfc1d/label
msgid "Sexual orientation"
msgstr "性傾向"

#: choice/5e214079-f16b-4832-ac04-f4c038c48157/label
msgid "Political opinions, religious or ideological convictions or trade union membership"
msgstr "政治意見、宗教或意識形態信念，或工會會員身分"

#: choice/4e4a40fa-cf4d-4de2-8959-fc2d651be3f5/label
msgid "Criminal convictions and offences"
msgstr "前科與犯罪資料"

#: question/de72effc-807a-4081-b842-1e77ecc9c43f/title
msgid "What are the exemptions to the prohibition for processing of special categories of data (such as health and genetic data) under Art. 9 GDPR used?"
msgstr ""

#: question/de72effc-807a-4081-b842-1e77ecc9c43f/text
msgid ""
"Processing of certain categories of personal data is not allowed unless there are exemptions in law to allow this. Among these categories (“sensitive data”) are *“‘[...] data revealing racial or ethnic origin, [...] genetic data, [...] data concerning health’”*. Most types of personal data collected in biomedical research will fall under these categories. [Article 9](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-9-gdpr/) (2) lists a number of exemptions that apply, of which *consent* and *scientific research* are most likely to be relevant for research. Please consult with your Data Protection Officer of your organisation.\n"
"State cohort/dataset for each type of exemption."
msgstr ""

#: question/2418a1b7-6950-4a19-8e58-6c5089c71b53/title
msgid "Select exemption"
msgstr "請選擇例外規定"

#: answer/7c215b23-edb9-4fc7-95d1-010ee53f3853/label
msgid "Scientific research"
msgstr "科學研究"

#: answer/59bc5ee8-71c9-497f-a09a-7b0736c40d74/label
msgid "Consent"
msgstr "同意"

#: question/5fa61693-3750-4fcb-b8c2-ca003ecb5d62/title
msgid "State the exemption"
msgstr "請說明例外規定"

#: question/595978f2-2973-4658-afa0-7efd004d16b4/title
msgid "Exemption"
msgstr "例外規定"

#: question/c6e30ba1-10d6-4f3c-b81a-5f2b362f74cd/title
msgid "Have data processing agreements been (or will they be) established between the data controller(s) and any data processors?"
msgstr "資料控管者與任何資料處理者之間，是否已訂立或將訂立資料處理協議？"

#: question/c6e30ba1-10d6-4f3c-b81a-5f2b362f74cd/text
msgid ""
"Note: A data processing agreement has to contain the obligatory clauses specified in [Art 28.3 of the\n"
"GDPR](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-28-gdpr/). The agreement should also regulate the use of any sub-processors.\n"
"\n"
"[Article 4](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-4-gdpr/) (8): *“**‘processor’** means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body which processes personal data on behalf of the controller.”* Examples of this is if you use a secure computing environment provided by another organisation to do your analysis or to store the data, along with several other scenarios. In the case that you do, there needs to be a legal agreement established between the controller(s) and processor(s) as defined in [Article 28](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-28-gdpr/) (3): *“Processing by a processor shall be governed by a contract or other legal act under Union or Member State law, that is binding on the processor with regard to the controller and that sets out the subject-matter and duration of the processing, the nature and purpose of the processing, the type of personal data and categories of data subjects and the obligations and rights of the controller. […]”* Article 28 also lists the required contents of such an agreement. Your organisation and/or the processor organisation will probably have agreement templates that you can use."
msgstr ""
"注意：資料處理協議必須包含 [GDPR 第 28 條第 3 項](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-28-gdpr/)規定的必要條款。\n"
"協議也應規範任何次級資料處理者的使用。\n"
"\n"
"[第 4 條](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-4-gdpr/)第 8 款將資料處理者定義為：「***處理者** 係指代控管者處理個人資料之自然人或法人、公務機關、局處或其他機構。*」例如，若您使用其他組織提供的安全運算環境進行分析或儲存資料，就可能屬於這種情況；其他情境也可能適用。若屬於這種情況，資料控管者與資料處理者之間需要依[第 28 條](https://gdpr-info.eu/art-28-gdpr/)第 3 項訂立法律協議：「*處理者所為處理應受契約或歐盟法或會員國法之其他立法之拘束，該等規定對於處理者及控管者具有拘束力，並規定處理標的及處理期間、處理之本質與目的、個人資料之類型及資料主體之類別以及控管者之義務及權利……*」第 28 條也列出此類協議的必要內容。您的組織及／或資料處理者所屬組織，很可能已有可供使用的協議範本。"

#: answer/aa88e146-e460-4611-898d-3f015df27780/label
msgid "Not relevant"
msgstr "不適用"

#: answer/e722d0dc-7a57-4634-8250-7c177664765a/label
msgid "Not yet, but they will be established before processing starts"
msgstr "尚未，但會在處理開始前訂立"

#: question/a21efb45-5238-4e9a-a00c-28d3d88d801b/title
msgid "List processors and agreements established"
msgstr "請列出資料處理者及已訂立的協議"

