#: question/a30f5047-33c1-45a7-8b3f-b1b90c364fc9/title
msgid "What technical and procedural safeguards have been established for processing the data?"
msgstr "已為資料處理建立哪些技術與程序保護措施？"

#: question/a30f5047-33c1-45a7-8b3f-b1b90c364fc9/text
msgid "To ensure that the personal data that you process in the project is protected at an appropriate level, you should apply technical and procedural safeguards to ensure that the rights of the data subjects are not violated. Examples of such measures include, but are not limited to, pseudonymisation and encryption of data, the use of computing and storage environments with heightened security, and clear and documented procedures for project members to follow."
msgstr "為確保您在計畫中處理的個人資料受到適當程度的保護，您應採用技術與程序保護措施，確保資料主體的權利不受侵害。此類措施包括但不限於資料的擬匿名化與加密、使用安全性較高的運算與儲存環境，以及提供清楚且經文件化、可供計畫成員遵循的程序。"

#: answer/22e612e0-c72d-42fa-9a37-a55232e72c72/label
msgid "Please specify"
msgstr "請說明"

#: question/7cc7b00c-6f1e-4ad9-9742-f02df552dbee/title
msgid "Select level of identifiability for the  stored data"
msgstr "選擇所儲存資料的可識別程度"

#: question/7cc7b00c-6f1e-4ad9-9742-f02df552dbee/text
msgid ""
"Anonymisation refers to the processing of personal data in a manner that makes it impossible to identify individuals from them. For example, the data can be rendered down to a general level (aggregated) or converted into statistics so that individuals can no longer  be identified from them. \n"
"\n"
"Pseudonymisation refers to the processing of personal data in such a manner that the personal data can no longer be attributed to a specific person without the use of additional information, i.e. any identifying characteristics are replaced with\n"
"a pseudonym."
msgstr ""
"匿名化 (Anonymization) 指的是，以某種方式處理個人資料，使他人無法從資料中識別出個人。例如，資料可被降為較概括的層級（如彙整後的資料），或轉換為統計資料，讓任何人都無法再從中辨識出個人身分。\n"
"\n"
"擬匿名化 (Pseudonymization) 則是指，以某種方式處理個人資料，使其在未搭配額外資訊的情況下，無法再將資料歸屬於特定個人，也就是將任何可識別個人的特徵以「假名」取代。"

#: answer/40a6b522-c130-44ec-924b-5316e0826bc2/label
msgid "Irrevocably anonymised"
msgstr "已不可逆匿名化"

#: answer/4cac7782-c9f7-4520-a88a-8b7688b7587d/label
msgid "Pseudonymised"
msgstr "已擬匿名化"

#: answer/930599c4-d002-42b7-bc0b-fa9565382d8c/label
msgid "Identifiable"
msgstr "可辨識的"

#: question/f646ba6e-21bc-4e66-8265-c8fdbe115c1f/title
msgid "Elaborate on your other safeguards"
msgstr "請詳細說明您其他保障措施"

#: question/f646ba6e-21bc-4e66-8265-c8fdbe115c1f/text
msgid "List technical and procedural safeguards to ensure the privacy protection of the research subjects."
msgstr "請列出技術與程序性保護措施，以確保受試者的隱私受到保護。"

#: question/15ade1cb-af43-40be-b8b1-2b801812dab1/title
msgid "Do you plan to transfer data outside the EU/EEA?"
msgstr "您是否計畫將資料傳輸至歐盟／歐洲經濟區 (EU/EEA) 以外？"

#: question/15ade1cb-af43-40be-b8b1-2b801812dab1/text
msgid ""
"Where personal data are transferred to a third country or to an international organization, appropriate measures (technical and organizational) must be put in place to protect the data.\n"
"If sufficient protection levels are not offered by the countries, the addition of specific data protection clauses must be added to contracts.\n"
"\n"
"Keep in mind that a processor shall not transfer data outside the EU/EEA without the data controller’s approval and instructions, and that it should be subject to contractual agreements as imposed by the data controller."
msgstr ""
"若個人資料傳輸至第三國或國際組織，必須採取適當的技術與組織措施來保護資料。\n"
"如果相關國家未提供充分保護水準，則必須在契約中加入特定資料保護條款。\n"
"\n"
"請記得，未經資料控制者核准與指示，資料處理者不得將資料傳輸至歐盟／歐洲經濟區之外；且此類傳輸應受資料控制者所要求的契約協議約束。"

#: question/db902645-6aef-426a-aa2c-30e96a4b3afb/title
msgid "Describe the measures put in place to protect data "
msgstr "請說明您採取的資料保護措施。 "

#: question/db902645-6aef-426a-aa2c-30e96a4b3afb/text
msgid "Describe the measures put in place to protect data during the transfer as well as the measures taken to ensure GDPR compliance by third parties, e.g. by establishing agreements."
msgstr "請說明在資料傳輸過程中所採取的保護措施，以及為確保第三方符合 GDPR 而採行的措施（例如透過簽訂協議）。"

#: reference/0b460273-3e3b-4289-8194-19c7cf1b05b1/label
msgid "RDMkit on Data Security"
msgstr "RDMkit 中的資料安全"

#: reference/df93fa41-88cb-451a-aa05-95a18cf02e73/label
msgid "RDMkit about Data Sensitivity"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料敏感性頁面"

#: reference/612660d5-dedc-4c4d-9176-06a887b47f14/label
#: reference/9090a519-777e-40e8-98ce-75760ff90244/label
#: reference/2a6ffbc9-6a07-4d5a-8df6-e7c44ce2356c/label
msgid "RDMkit on Human Data"
msgstr "RDMkit 的人類資料頁面"

#: reference/15f661c7-2bfa-4687-823e-80692f3efd61/label
msgid "DMEG on Data Protection"
msgstr "DMEG 的資料保護頁面"

#: reference/4c559ae4-fbde-45a9-bb03-53fb626198ec/label
msgid "DMEG on Personal Data"
msgstr "DMEG (Data Management Expert Guide) 中的個人資料"

#: question/ebcbf4c6-ce25-4a0b-9e82-039a88498203/title
msgid "Is the data collection subject to ethical legislation?"
msgstr "這項資料蒐集是否受倫理法規所規範？"

#: question/3782d32b-91b5-432f-8f93-92bb22868a22/title
msgid "Is the collection covered by ethical review?"
msgstr "這項資料蒐集是否已納入倫理審查範圍？"

#: question/3782d32b-91b5-432f-8f93-92bb22868a22/text
msgid "If the answer is positive, you should have specified the relevant ethical review details under the \"Research Project\" question in the Administrative information chapter."
msgstr "如果答案為是，您應已在「行政資訊」章節的「研究計畫」問題中填寫相關倫理審查資訊。"

#: reference/c653312c-e9b1-4d3c-b23f-26ba0c429cd4/label
msgid "DMEG on Ethical Process Review"
msgstr "DMEG (Data Management Expert Guide) 中的倫理流程審查"

#: question/b464593d-fb92-4ad9-88e1-764306bb3051/title
msgid "Does the collection of data involve human subjects?"
msgstr "資料的蒐集是否包含人類受試者？"

#: question/a2b1fa38-792a-4628-9765-93476a38cffb/title
msgid "Have informed consents been collected from the research subjects?"
msgstr "是否已取得受試者的知情同意？"

#: question/a2b1fa38-792a-4628-9765-93476a38cffb/text
msgid "Note: Be aware that different laws might define the mandatory content of an informed consent in different ways. Therefore, an informed consent that is valid under one law (e.g. ethical legislation), might not be valid under another law (e.g. GDPR). Informed consents acquired before the GDPR might not be valid if consent is to be used as the legal basis for processing."
msgstr "注意：不同法律可能會以不同方式定義知情同意的必要內容。因此，依某一法律（例如倫理相關法規）有效的知情同意，依另一法律，例如 GDPR，不一定有效。若要以同意作為處理的法律依據，GDPR 生效前取得的知情同意可能並不有效。"

#: question/63b6e695-2371-412c-bed3-f13e157da0b4/title
msgid "Are there any data use restrictions?"
msgstr ""

#: question/63b6e695-2371-412c-bed3-f13e157da0b4/text
msgid ""
"Are there any limitations on the data use e.g. only for research on certain types of diseases, sharing only within certain geographical boundaries, etc.?\n"
"\n"
"Describing data use in a formalised way by using the data use ontology (DUO) greatly improves the data reusability."
msgstr ""
"對於資料的使用是否有任何限制，例如：僅限於特定類型疾病的研究、僅限在特定地理範圍內共享等？\n"
"\n"
"使用「資料使用本體」(Data Use Ontology, DUO) 以正式化方式描述資料使用，能大幅提升資料的可再次使用性。"

#: answer/3ed68fbb-ec13-46ab-806b-247c16c1ecbd/label
msgid "There will be no use restrictions"
msgstr "不會有使用限制"

#: answer/03704872-aa57-4d0a-b977-89bdb4331853/label
msgid "There will be restrictions"
msgstr "會有使用限制"

#: question/81f18ab3-ab64-46a7-bf26-9e7d663d4362/title
msgid "What are the background of the restrictions?"
msgstr "這些限制的依據是什麼？"

#: choice/caac09f2-be5c-4ba4-82dc-7f0ee33ab67d/label
msgid "GDPR"
msgstr "歐盟《個人資料保護規則》(GDPR)"

#: choice/1f758ac9-71c1-4dfb-85a6-09e2a206ab9a/label
msgid "Ethical approval"
msgstr "倫理審查核准"

#: choice/18605a14-9945-4294-9cb8-e211ccfe5c85/label
msgid "Restrictions in the consent"
msgstr "同意書中的限制"

#: question/0ac70ded-3864-4c7e-90a1-ea13a5fc9975/title
msgid "Please specify what the restrictions are"
msgstr "請具體說明有哪些限制"

#: reference/7c4f4af7-abaf-481c-b1c5-ab43b5b82c2c/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on permitted uses of data"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的資料允許使用範圍頁面"

#: question/cb7d17a8-30c0-489d-a43c-702b27d97611/title
msgid "How are the rights of the collected data arranged?"
msgstr "對於所蒐集資料的權利歸屬是如何規劃安排的？"

#: answer/f310952b-e946-4315-bb32-bf127d1bf96a/label
msgid "Our data is legally not copyrightable, there is no legal rightsholder"
msgstr "我們的資料依法不受著作權保護，因此不存在法律上的權利人"

#: answer/91d6ee6f-c501-4d1c-a6e7-9da1789f68de/label
msgid "The Principal Investigator will be the rightsholder"
msgstr "由計畫主持人擔任權利人"

#: answer/ef4ac36a-eea0-42b4-8292-b89090a1b5ef/label
msgid "The institute will be the rightsholder"
msgstr "由機構擔任權利人"

#: answer/115a165f-9d3f-440d-a822-4bd2795c264e/label
msgid "We have a consortium agreement that arranges Intellectual Property"
msgstr "我們已有聯盟協議 (consortium agreement) 安排智慧財產權 (Intellectual Property, IP) 事宜"

#: answer/0fd3cd1c-e0e8-41d5-9beb-3f1faba0fb91/label
msgid "The rights  for the data is arranged in another way"
msgstr "資料相關權利將以其他方式安排"

#: question/06655161-9a91-47f4-af3b-9d2a5e6db19b/title
msgid "How else is the intellectual property for the data collected in the project arranged?"
msgstr "本計畫所蒐集資料的智慧財產權將如何另行安排？"

#: reference/26ecbf8d-d40a-476a-b527-9e9c7896eb48/label
msgid "DMEG on Copyright"
msgstr "DMEG 的著作權頁面"

#: question/b2fb6b4e-2961-40a4-a9ec-faf4e49a978b/title
msgid "Are you running the project in a collaboration between different groups or institutes?"
msgstr "您的計畫是否與不同的團隊或機構協作？"

#: question/a5dbea23-b7d6-4e31-a1a5-ec5007ec7848/title
msgid "Is there a collaboration agreement in the project that describes who can have access to what data?"
msgstr "計畫中是否有合作協議，說明誰可以取用哪些資料？"

#: answer/4505bb3f-63b0-4c28-97a8-d12fbafb2b7a/advice
msgid "A collaboration agreement is really something to consider."
msgstr "擬訂協作協議是值得考慮的一件事。"

#: reference/59bd5fee-3d92-4d90-a04e-4aa18a1e07ea/label
msgid "See also description of Data Sharing in RDMkit"
msgstr "另請參見RDMkit 中關於資料共享的說明"

#: chapter/10a10ffd-bfe1-4c6b-bbb6-3dfb1e63a5d5/title
msgid "Processing data"
msgstr "資料處理"

#: chapter/10a10ffd-bfe1-4c6b-bbb6-3dfb1e63a5d5/text
msgid ""
"In the processing phase, the data will be undergoing the mostly automated steps for processing, before the analysis and interpretation.\n"
"\n"
"In this chapter, many questions are focusing on the compute environment that is used to process the data and make it available for interpretation by project partners. Some of those questions (e.g. on workflow systems and data provenance) are also relevant for the work in the interpretation phase."
msgstr ""
"在處理階段，資料會先經過大多數自動化的處理步驟，之後才進入分析與詮釋。\n"
"\n"
"本章有許多問題聚焦於運算環境：該環境用來處理資料，並使資料可供計畫合作夥伴進行詮釋。其中有些問題（例如關於工作流程系統和資料溯源的問題）也與詮釋階段的工作相關。"

#: question/72099c46-16e7-47a2-a320-cc768b7085fe/title
msgid "Will you be using a shared working space to work with your data?"
msgstr "您是否會使用共享的工作空間來處理您的資料？"

#: question/72099c46-16e7-47a2-a320-cc768b7085fe/text
msgid "Will you be using a working space containing data and software specific to the project that is shared between all the people working on the data in the project? Sometimes such a system is called a *Virtual Research Environment*."
msgstr "您是否會使用一個包含本計畫特定資料與軟體的工作空間，並讓計畫中所有處理資料的人共同使用？這類系統有時稱為 *「虛擬研究環境」*。"

#: answer/1d6ba101-fd62-43c8-ab53-76bc31847f58/label
msgid "No, participants in the project each have different collections of data and tools"
msgstr "否，計畫參與者各自使用不同的資料與工具"

#: question/c1e83bdf-5914-44c2-8414-0a4e7fbaf272/title
msgid "Are data that project members and partners store themselves adequately backed up and traceable?"
msgstr "計畫成員與合作夥伴自行儲存的資料，是否已妥善備份且可追蹤？"

#: answer/ec92df2d-f6db-4cc8-8317-ae24ab4fa08a/label
msgid "Yes, protected against both equipment failure and human error"
msgstr "是，可同時防範設備故障與人為錯誤"

#: question/5607d0bb-6b9e-4211-821c-785acc3aa25e/title
msgid "Will this work space be run by dedicated specialists?"
msgstr "這個工作空間是否會由專責人員負責營運？"

#: question/5607d0bb-6b9e-4211-821c-785acc3aa25e/text
msgid "If your work space is run and maintained by specialists, e.g. the ICT department of one of the institutes involved in the projects, this means that backup and restore as well as access management is properly addressed."
msgstr "如果您的工作空間是由專責人員負責營運與維護，例如由參與計畫的某個機構之資訊通訊部門負責，這表示備份與復原，以及取用管理，都已獲得妥善處理。"

#: question/df36fb68-131c-4f31-a42b-684abf523bbc/title
msgid "How will you work with your data?"
msgstr "您會如何操作與使用您的資料？"

#: question/df36fb68-131c-4f31-a42b-684abf523bbc/text
msgid "There are several questions regarding the dynamics of the data in the working area, who works with it, the software that is run on it, etc."
msgstr "以下有幾個問題涉及工作空間中資料的動態變化、由誰處理這些資料、在資料上執行哪些軟體等。"

#: question/73bfcfcf-a619-4f6a-a901-2e8ce01d039a/title
msgid "What kind of data will you have in your work space?"
msgstr "您的工作空間中會有哪些資料類型？"

#: question/73bfcfcf-a619-4f6a-a901-2e8ce01d039a/text
msgid "When making the work space, it helps to know whether you expect to work with very many small files, a few very large files, whether you will use a (SQL) database to store most of the data. Maybe your data is suitable for a system like Hadoop? Such information can be collected here."
msgstr "建立工作空間時，若能先了解您預期會處理的資料型態，會很有幫助。例如：是否會使用大量的小型檔案、少數幾個大型檔案，或是否會使用 SQL 資料庫來儲存大部分資料。也可能您的資料適合使用像 Hadoop 這類系統。這些資訊都可以在這裡蒐集。"

#: question/f6e66f4f-7b11-420f-a4b6-5fc972bc66d9/title
msgid "Do you need the work space to be close to the compute capacity?"
msgstr "您是否需要讓工作空間鄰近運算資源？"

#: question/f6e66f4f-7b11-420f-a4b6-5fc972bc66d9/text
msgid "If you have large volumes of data that are intensely and repeatedly used by the computing work flow, it may be needed to keep the storage in the same place as where the computing takes place."
msgstr "如果您有大量資料，且運算工作流程會密集並反覆使用這些資料，可能需要將資料儲存在與運算執行位置相同的地方。"

#: reference/83081d6a-7e18-4ccf-97cd-f89193e73382/description
msgid "Compute capacity planning"
msgstr "運算資源容量規劃"

#: question/50f9d580-3e62-434b-81ff-86daed56aca8/title
msgid "Will you be working with your data in another form than the way it will be archived?"
msgstr "您處理資料時所使用的形式，是否會不同於資料最終典藏時的形式？"

#: question/50f9d580-3e62-434b-81ff-86daed56aca8/text
msgid "Archival and working with data have different requirements. You want archived information to be in a form that others could read and in a format that is also understandable in a number of years. When working with the data, you need to be able to address it efficiently. If the two differ, you need to plan for conversions."
msgstr "資料典藏與資料處理有不同的需求。典藏資訊應採用他人能夠讀取、且多年後仍可理解的形式與格式。處理資料時，則需要能夠有效率地存取資料。若兩者有所不同，就需要規劃資料轉換。"

#: answer/df08a7fa-61af-418f-9eb8-965ba50efcc8/label
msgid "No, data format will be archived in the same way we work with it"
msgstr "不會，資料格式會以我們處理時所使用的相同方式進行典藏"

#: answer/02b8d129-3300-47cb-811a-e86a40c5d8bd/label
msgid "Yes, archival will require a conversion step"
msgstr "會，典藏時需要進行一個轉換步驟"

#: question/4ee4d67d-62c5-47f0-a741-f2629b65cf8a/title
msgid "How does the storage need change over time?"
msgstr "資料儲存需求將如何隨時間改變？"

#: question/4ee4d67d-62c5-47f0-a741-f2629b65cf8a/text
msgid "To perform capacity planning, it is important to know what the need for storage capacity at the beginning and the end of the project will be."
msgstr "若要進行容量規劃，了解計畫開始與結束時各需要多少儲存容量，是很重要的。"

#: answer/eef277cb-1032-401e-b242-e74afde575dc/label
msgid "Storage needs will be the same during the whole project"
msgstr "整個計畫期間的儲存需求都會維持不變"

#: answer/014d23a8-93a8-4fd2-ba1c-8656177f37b2/label
msgid "Storage needs are large at the beginning and will be reduced later"
msgstr "一開始的儲存需求會比較大，之後會逐漸降低"

#: answer/ab40db7f-ea89-4830-b507-4f2f08a9453e/label
msgid "Storage needs are small at the beginning and will grow later"
msgstr "一開始的儲存需求較小，之後會逐漸增加"

#: answer/51a8248e-8659-47fd-a8e3-112eed64f65b/label
msgid "Storage needs are largest in the middle of the project"
msgstr "儲存需求會在計畫中期達到最高"

#: question/8526a988-9561-42c6-8af4-7c96aa4c536d/title
msgid "When will your raw data become available?"
msgstr "原始資料會在什麼時候進入計畫工作空間？"

#: answer/adfc7ca3-c8e3-465b-8eb2-4327b8780684/label
msgid "Raw data will come in right at the start"
msgstr "原始資料會在計畫一開始就進入工作空間"

#: answer/19755f9d-8ec2-4fd9-8bdf-b25d5889d7ee/label
msgid "Raw data will come in during the project"
msgstr "原始資料會在計畫期間陸續進入工作空間"

#: question/01cd836b-915e-4751-b543-b326bf812594/title
msgid "How much of the raw data do you need to keep in the work space?"
msgstr "在工作空間中，您需要保留多少原始資料？"

#: question/01cd836b-915e-4751-b543-b326bf812594/text
msgid "Sometimes the raw data is relatively large, and it pays of to clean it quickly."
msgstr "有時原始資料相當龐大，因此值得盡快加以清理。"

#: answer/fe62c9a0-a621-46b6-bc42-881d0c3d8719/label
msgid "Raw data will need to stay in the work space"
msgstr "原始資料需要保留在工作空間中"

#: answer/aad7d438-a8af-4462-9728-77e2493bcacc/label
msgid "Raw data can be cleaned out or archived quickly"
msgstr "原始資料可以很快清除，或移到典藏儲存空間"

#: question/ba381732-f499-419f-8744-e13807af83e3/title
msgid "Do your raw data need to be archived?"
msgstr "您的原始資料是否需要長期典藏或歸檔？"

#: answer/904859c4-b9bf-44b6-9a64-933e489089e6/label
msgid "No, it is also stored elsewhere can be recovered easily"
msgstr "不會，這些資料也儲存在其他地方，因此可以輕易復原"

#: answer/e4da5030-9de8-4fe9-81d9-28a75edc09d9/label
msgid "No, it can be remeasured easily and more cheaply than archiving"
msgstr "否，這些資料可以輕易重新量測，成本也比典藏更低"

#: reference/e4e53d85-6774-4472-b7cb-0f9eaad04a15/description
msgid "Timing archival of raw data"
msgstr "安排原始資料的典藏時程"

#: answer/93555e7b-d17c-4341-9ad9-9f2f833a3193/label
msgid "Raw data do not form a major part of the storage needs"
msgstr "原始資料不是儲存需求的主要部分"

#: answer/0ddd0082-eae1-4c48-ba4a-30912f0643e7/label
msgid "Raw data will only be loaded in the work space on demand from the primary archives"
msgstr "原始資料只會在有需要時，才從主要檔案庫載入到工作空間中"

#: question/c0944ac9-f286-48f2-b864-4641d0fcdd55/title
msgid "Did you plan how much intermediate data you will get during analysis and how long each step needs to be kept?"
msgstr "您是否已規劃分析過程中會產生多少中間資料，以及各階段資料需要保存多久？"

#: answer/96b1aa0f-56db-4613-b424-3fe33349386b/label
msgid "The volume of intermediate data will not be significant"
msgstr "中間資料的資料量不會太大"

#: answer/9a0cfd22-adce-46e6-b7ec-8ed581ac95be/label
msgid "A large volume of intermediate data will be in the work space"
msgstr "大量的中間資料會存放在工作空間中"

#: question/deb647ec-a001-4370-87b8-a5b1e2479f87/title
msgid "Is it possible to store intermediate temporary data on a separate (scratch) area that is not backed up?"
msgstr "是否可以將暫時性的中間資料存放在另外一個不備份的暫存區？"

#: question/deb647ec-a001-4370-87b8-a5b1e2479f87/text
msgid "If the intermediate results are in your main work space, a restore in case of a problem could take much more time. It may be faster to recover it by re-running computations."
msgstr "如果中間資料放在主要工作空間中，一旦發生問題需要還原，可能會花上很多時間。這時候，重新執行運算來復原資料，可能會比較快。"

#: answer/55bab6f7-6ab9-4eb7-ae2b-1947cce2da84/label
msgid "We will use the main work space for temporary data"
msgstr "我們會使用主要工作空間來存放暫時性資料"

#: answer/5cbefa56-bc0c-4704-a9a4-3535ec513057/label
msgid "We can offload intermediate results to a scratch area that is not backed up"
msgstr "我們可以將中間結果卸載到不會備份的暫存區"

#: question/3a076e83-73b0-4cdd-bb71-c5d41469a191/title
msgid "Are you sure you will not need a backup of the data stored on the scratch file systems (any scratch you use)?"
msgstr "您確定不需要備份儲存在暫存檔案系統中的資料，包括您使用的任何暫存空間嗎？"

#: reference/94544b24-90e3-4d95-a0c0-bfed45cbdac9/label
msgid "How CSC restored 850 million temporary files"
msgstr "CSC 如何復原 8.5 億個暫存檔案"

#: question/89f78871-68bd-4190-9ee7-57ec3b4c2356/title
msgid "Will you have different versions of intermediate data that need to be kept?"
msgstr "是否會有需要保留的不同版本中間資料？"

#: question/89f78871-68bd-4190-9ee7-57ec3b4c2356/text
msgid "Consider storing only the workflow parameters if the data itself could be reproduced quickly."
msgstr "若資料本身可快速重製，可考慮僅儲存工作流程的參數。"

#: question/50a9c060-91e9-4e34-8cb2-2d41fa493f9e/title
msgid "Will you need to temporarily archive data sets (e.g. to tape)?"
msgstr "您是否需要暫時典藏資料集（例如存放至磁帶）？"

#: question/50a9c060-91e9-4e34-8cb2-2d41fa493f9e/text
msgid "Usually, data sets will be archived if it is unlikely you need them in the short term, but it would be hard to create them again, and/or they are essential for reproducing your work. Archival storage of large volumes can be significantly cheaper than keeping it in the working area for an extensive period."
msgstr "通常，如果短期內不太可能需要使用某些資料集，但重新產生這些資料集並不容易，或這些資料集對於重現您的工作至關重要，就會將其典藏。對於大量資料，使用典藏儲存空間的成本，可能會比長時間存放在工作空間中低得多。"

#: reference/1fa0cc82-65e6-492f-b982-19ea2636ed95/description
msgid "Data archive setup"
msgstr "資料典藏庫設定"

#: question/f4065e54-d27a-45de-be4c-10384feacd0d/title
msgid "How will your first data come in?"
msgstr "您的第一批資料會如何進來？"

#: answer/2271d2cd-de50-460b-85a1-dddf9d28776c/label
msgid "No special planning is needed for the initial data"
msgstr "沒有特別規劃初始資料的到來"

#: answer/9ad1d4fd-997d-45a8-8cc4-f594a8e4fdf8/label
msgid "Initial data will need to be made available through a local network copy"
msgstr "需要透過區域網路複製初始資料"

#: answer/202c1232-9f5e-4a68-b0e0-3986a7bc96fa/label
msgid "We will need a high-speed network connection to copy the initial data"
msgstr "我們需要高速網路連線來複製初始資料"

#: answer/94aa40a4-9b14-4923-a26a-3523566329e3/label
msgid "Initial data will arrive on separate media and will need to be copied to the work space"
msgstr "初始資料將透過個別儲存媒體送達，並需要複製到工作空間中"

#: question/2ed7b5c7-2452-4087-b4ed-d15ca31a4e65/title
msgid "How will project partners access the work space?"
msgstr "計畫合作夥伴將如何取用計畫工作空間？"

#: question/b1faddd1-2f9f-48a8-b9a7-d8f6f8c02470/title
msgid "Who will arrange access control?"
msgstr "誰會負責取用管控？"

#: answer/d45f521d-f541-4f40-a3d8-d4a9ecdc65e3/label
msgid "No special provisions are needed"
msgstr "不需要特別措施"

#: answer/9b723841-1bd4-487c-b45c-f0a369330b3a/label
msgid "Project management will need to be able to give people access"
msgstr "計畫管理人員需要能夠授予人員取用權限"

#: answer/4bb35a94-e387-4460-bcf3-d638f248e52c/label
msgid "The work space should be connected to a single-sign-on system"
msgstr "工作空間應連接到單一登入系統"

#: question/f99580d5-b3ea-498c-86ac-f7326bd999c2/title
msgid "Will the work space storage need to be remote mounted?"
msgstr "工作空間儲存區是否需要以遠端掛載的方式使用？"

#: answer/f848f3ec-08c8-4197-bd4f-6d438bac4d70/label
msgid "No, data will be copied if it needs to be processed elsewhere"
msgstr "不會，若資料需要在其他地方處理，會先複製過去"

#: answer/bdf255fd-6dd6-4f1e-a9e2-d6aec9d01678/label
#: answer/8fee76df-9eef-4912-9b11-31ebad574ced/label
msgid "No, all data processing will be done in the same environment (virtual research environment)"
msgstr "否，所有資料處理都會在同一個環境中完成（虛擬研究環境）"

#: answer/6baa53fe-c657-4da3-bb65-9b71f7141c6d/label
msgid "Yes, for occasional exploration"
msgstr "是的，用於偶爾進行資料探索"

#: answer/5ab6d069-f46c-4514-8114-79c9fe01a93f/label
#: answer/06a34c86-3c48-4fa4-8888-0ae6b613068f/label
msgid "Yes, for actual computations, requiring high performance"
msgstr "是，實際運算需要高效能資源"

#: question/f14750e9-3a39-4aae-b2c8-845583934c1d/title
msgid "Will data be copied out and in to the workspace storage by remote users?"
msgstr "遠端使用者是否會將資料複製進／複製出工作空間儲存區？"

#: answer/2c2cd046-89e0-4f55-bafa-92eb5f77c3a8/label
msgid "No, this should not be allowed"
msgstr "不，不應允許這麼做"

#: answer/8fa969a0-7477-41be-aefc-a54a8045c954/label
msgid "Yes, occasionally"
msgstr "是，偶爾會"

#: question/6b3f13db-407a-44e0-9d23-e6dd6a20ad59/title
msgid "Are data integrity and reliability requirements also met by the other storage spaces used in the project?"
msgstr "計畫中使用的其他儲存空間是否也同樣符合資料完整性與可靠性的要求？"

#: answer/c7a0181c-1921-4b21-9481-f4274d48876c/label
msgid "This is not needed"
msgstr "不需要"

#: reference/5b22075d-c62f-4e7f-8a57-79c930d81094/description
msgid "Workflow that is split over multiple work locations"
msgstr "分散在多個工作地點的工作流程"

#: reference/7aa33891-6563-4cd3-bb08-2f0d3b6f818a/label
#: reference/dddd6258-9d36-4d5c-9fe3-15369f825b04/label
msgid "RDMkit on Data Processing"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料處理頁面"

#: reference/23a14548-8397-490f-94e9-0d799c01e319/label
#: reference/45d989ae-e78a-4d80-9af7-168ebb0d681b/label
#: reference/f3fd7baf-c902-4f01-b979-2f1136a1df36/label
msgid "RDMkit on Data Analysis"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料分析頁面"

#: question/b171ec17-d7b5-4726-ae22-0d892b106cf8/title
msgid "How available/reliable should must the work space be?"
msgstr "工作空間的可用性與可靠性要求為何？"

#: question/b171ec17-d7b5-4726-ae22-0d892b106cf8/text
msgid "There are a number of questions that can help you to decide whether your work space will be reliable enough for your project."
msgstr "有幾個問題可以協助您判斷工作空間對計畫而言是否足夠可靠。"

#: question/25e06912-08a2-40e4-af76-cfbc5ada9925/title
msgid "How do you prevent a total loss of data in the work space?"
msgstr "您將如何防止工作空間中的資料發生全面性遺失？"

#: answer/44810299-8618-4a79-a732-13cc2ff21903/label
msgid "The work space provides sufficient guarantees"
msgstr "工作空間提供足夠保障"

#: answer/766e16e4-21c7-4030-9eda-1973f51061d4/label
msgid "All essential data is also stored elsewhere"
msgstr "所有重要資料也儲存在其他地方"

#: question/19640692-1c97-4574-8b3d-f4f6e1e6b564/title
msgid "Is there software in the work space? Can it also be restored quickly?"
msgstr "工作空間中是否有軟體？若有，是否也能夠快速還原？"

#: answer/7b572fda-9d67-44e9-b1c3-6dfc42c34d89/label
msgid "There is no software"
msgstr "沒有軟體"

#: answer/1217ef1b-01fd-48e6-900d-60edb99b4621/label
msgid "Software in the work space is only a copy"
msgstr "工作空間中的軟體僅為副本"

#: answer/af2e1ca5-9a21-4c3b-a973-e9f41fd613da/label
msgid "Special care will be taken for the software and configurations"
msgstr "會特別注意軟體與設定檔"

#: question/0548db0c-bd34-40ce-be73-7a13a5e8eb7d/title
msgid "Can you handle it when the work space is off line for a while?"
msgstr "當工作空間暫時離線時，您是否有能力應對？"

#: answer/ef611a20-d5f9-4ea6-bb02-a7122bfd7eed/label
msgid "We could handle a few days of offline time per year"
msgstr "我們每年可以接受幾天工作空間離線"

#: answer/d96d5e47-aec8-4576-9e3a-734ab58dfe62/label
msgid "We can only miss the work space for a few hours during work hours"
msgstr "我們只能在工作時間內接受工作空間中斷幾個小時"

#: answer/b6da4858-f72c-498b-a827-d4632a458098/label
msgid "Problems during the evenings and weekends can not wait for work hours to be repaired"
msgstr "若問題發生在晚上或週末，不能等到上班時間再處理"

#: question/6531dd45-f628-4aa7-a2c5-82c639b79ab8/title
msgid "How long can you wait for a restore if the storage fails?"
msgstr "若儲存系統故障，您可接受的資料還原等待時間有多長？"

#: answer/c9d8c9ed-ba2d-4108-b798-493cdf9225df/label
msgid "We can wait for repair and a restore"
msgstr "我們可以等待修復與還原"

#: answer/27db87e3-46b2-4705-b98c-47ddf4b4cd56/label
msgid "A spare copy needs to be deployed quickly"
msgstr "需要快速部署一份預備的副本"

#: answer/5797b252-0550-46e1-bf13-c65edd2df45e/label
msgid "No waiting is possible, a hot copy must be ready to take over"
msgstr "不能有等待時間，必須備有可立即接管的熱備份副本"

#: question/aacf28a0-aab9-4436-8b2b-95ef755ae32a/title
msgid "How long can you wait for a restore if you accidentally damage a file?"
msgstr "若您不慎損毀某個檔案，您可承受的資料還原時間有多長？"

#: answer/42fb53ea-76ed-494b-8582-f080d952a3ed/label
msgid "Days"
msgstr "數天"

#: answer/91463928-1cf4-43e0-bb4e-d1fc7b077ac8/label
msgid "Hours"
msgstr "數小時"

#: answer/a639ec31-e226-404e-97fb-567d2f52e321/label
msgid "Any user needs to be able to restore an old copy instantaneously"
msgstr "任何使用者都必須能夠即時還原舊版副本"

#: question/98d9789b-32fc-4e2f-876a-47760ad7c7ec/title
msgid "Will you make backup copies of project data that is not in the work space?"
msgstr "對於未儲存在工作空間中的計畫資料，您是否會另外建立備份？"

#: question/98d9789b-32fc-4e2f-876a-47760ad7c7ec/text
msgid "Are there any data files e.g. on laptops of project members? Also: supercomputing centers and other high performance computer centers often write in their terms of use that you need to take care of your own backups."
msgstr "計畫成員的筆記型電腦等設備中是否存有任何資料檔案？此外，高速計算中心及其他高效能運算中心通常會在使用條款中註明，使用者須自行負責資料備份。"

#: answer/7c732053-6df4-466b-8732-0db2bd1e1ffc/label
msgid "This is left to the project participants"
msgstr "這由計畫參與者自行處理"

#: answer/a1ead63a-1bc8-42e6-8bdc-3e1e8a901307/label
msgid "There is no data elsewhere"
msgstr ""

#: answer/278810f9-6396-4203-9fa6-6cd3a003159c/label
msgid "All data elsewhere is adequately backed up"
msgstr "所有他處資料皆已適當備份"

#: answer/0884ac19-9bde-4bf1-afdd-0794c2c69092/label
msgid "We make (automated) backups of all data stored outside of the working area"
msgstr "我們會自動備份所有儲存在工作空間之外的資料"

#: question/80d403f3-3f29-4f37-9040-b901ae9afa37/title
msgid "How will access to the work space be controlled?"
msgstr "工作空間的存取權限將如何管理？"

#: answer/302e4b9b-9a9c-4fb0-9745-5f8ff4cca746/label
msgid "Only all project members have read/write access to the data"
msgstr "只有計畫成員可以讀取及寫入資料"

#: answer/154cd5fc-a79f-4c2e-be67-6985813bbc8d/label
msgid "Anyone in the institute has read access to the data; all project members have read/write access"
msgstr ""

#: answer/b21c9f70-78e7-4975-b776-59e372285662/label
msgid "Only project members will have read access; only selected project members will be able to write data"
msgstr "只有計畫成員具有資料的讀取權限；僅部分指定的計畫成員具有資料的寫入權限"

#: answer/b19ba76a-4b6a-45f6-8ab5-8bbfb92c7b2c/label
msgid "Anyone in the institute can read data, only project members can request write access"
msgstr "機構內任何人皆可讀取資料；只有計畫成員可以申請資料的寫入權限"

#: question/bc5e3dbf-2923-4025-a49a-f204b01d4018/title
msgid "Data storage systems and file naming conventions"
msgstr "資料儲存系統與檔案命名規範"

#: question/bc5e3dbf-2923-4025-a49a-f204b01d4018/text
msgid "It is a good idea to pre-define how data will be organised in the project work space, and to set conventions for how any data files and folders will be named."
msgstr "預先規劃資料在計畫工作空間中的組織方式，並制定資料檔案與資料夾的命名規則，是一個很好的做法。"

#: question/38ebf5d0-f7a3-4cf5-93eb-6ee3143c8a69/title
msgid "How much storage space will the project require for all data and software, including temporary storage?"
msgstr "本計畫總共需要多少儲存空間，包含所有資料、軟體以及暫存空間？"

#: answer/9c0ce039-9762-40b3-96dc-666bd519c723/label
msgid "So little that it is not a problem"
msgstr "資料量很少，不至於成為問題"

#: question/974f3ad3-90b3-4e00-b751-8c5a5629b2cf/title
msgid "Estimated data volume in Gigabytes"
msgstr "預估資料量（單位：GB）"

#: question/b6d0922c-6e9c-45f8-b687-79310744601a/title
msgid "What part of the data will have the largest volume?"
msgstr "哪一部分資料的資料量最大？"

#: answer/044ef740-c26d-434c-88a9-9a25ef4c719a/label
msgid "Raw/Input Data"
msgstr "原始／輸入資料"

#: answer/044ef740-c26d-434c-88a9-9a25ef4c719a/advice
msgid ""
"Note that if the raw data is from a public resource, you may be able to avoid storing it altogether and processing it immediately from the public resource. If you have to download it before using, you can store it on a volume that is not backed up, because you can simply reproduce it.\n"
"\n"
"If you have a large volume of newly collected raw input data, publishing it as soon as possible into a public resource may reduce the pressure on the storage requirements."
msgstr ""
"請注意，如果原始資料來自公共資源，您也許可以完全避免儲存，而是直接從公共資源處理。若必須先下載才能使用，可以將其存放在不備份的儲存區上，因為您可以直接重新產生。\n"
"\n"
"如果新蒐集的原始輸入資料量很大，盡早發布到公共資源中，可能有助於減輕儲存需求的壓力。"

#: answer/70442fd3-bea2-4e97-81f5-e9b33eec6cac/label
#: answer/5b49df5e-1d06-446f-a518-33a06928b598/label
msgid "Intermediate data"
msgstr "中間資料"

#: answer/70442fd3-bea2-4e97-81f5-e9b33eec6cac/advice
msgid ""
"If the intermediate data is larger than either input or output data, you may consider minimizing the time it is stored. Make the balance between the CPU time needed if you need to re-calculate it versus the storage requirements. Sometimes it is possible to avoid storage at all by immediately running the whole analysis work flow.\n"
"\n"
"It may also be useful to consider storing the intermediate data on a separate data volume from the rest of the project storage, which may not be backed up. This can not only reduce the storage costs, but also if the backup needs to be used it is better if it strictly contains the data that is needed for a restore, otherwise a restore i case of a problem may take much longer than strictly necessary."
msgstr ""
"如果中間資料比輸入或輸出資料更大，可以考慮盡量縮短其保存時間。請在重新計算所需的 CPU 時間與儲存需求之間取得平衡。有時也可以透過立即執行完整分析工作流程，完全避免儲存中間資料。\n"
"\n"
"也可以考慮將中間資料存放在與其他計畫儲存空間分開的資料卷上，而且該資料卷可以不備份。這不僅能降低儲存成本；若日後需要使用備份，備份中最好只包含還原所必需的資料，否則發生問題時的還原作業可能會比必要時間長得多。"

#: answer/379327e3-485d-4121-a9ec-d790ae6f5bcf/label
msgid "Output data"
msgstr "輸出資料"

#: answer/eaedc13a-242b-417d-b084-5ef152c352ab/label
msgid "There is no significant difference"
msgstr ""

#: question/a12aa967-28a5-4a9b-8df8-f7c533205ea4/title
msgid "Are you using a filesystem with files and folders?"
msgstr "您是否正在使用包含檔案與資料夾的檔案系統？"

#: question/a12aa967-28a5-4a9b-8df8-f7c533205ea4/text
msgid "Are some of the data in the project stored in a filesystem with files and folders?"
msgstr "計畫中部分的資料是否儲存在以檔案與資料夾組織的檔案系統中？"

#: question/cc76bce4-f4df-40e0-b28b-dc64b95b7c7b/title
msgid "Will you use a folder for each sample/subject?"
msgstr "是否會為每個樣本／受試者建立一個資料夾？"

#: question/c9ed47c7-49f7-4ea5-895d-1d17c19c36e4/title
msgid "What is the naming convention for this folder?"
msgstr "此資料夾的命名規則是什麼？"

#: question/c9ed47c7-49f7-4ea5-895d-1d17c19c36e4/text
msgid "What appointment have you made for the naming of the folders? Make sure names are relatively short, and avoid spaces and special characters.\n"
msgstr "您針對資料夾命名做了哪些約定？請確保名稱儘量簡短，並避免使用空格與特殊字元。\n"

#: question/f8eeb548-f5af-4fc8-a5fd-88fdf28b0de1/title
msgid "Will you use a (sub)folder for each (repeated) analysis?"
msgstr "是否會為每次（重複）分析建立一個（子）資料夾？"

#: question/ecb23397-d44d-4623-8233-481e753492ea/title
msgid "What are the naming conventions for the analysis folders?"
msgstr "分析資料夾的命名規則是什麼？"

#: question/ecb23397-d44d-4623-8233-481e753492ea/text
#: question/dad8247a-3553-48dc-8518-d64057cded1e/text
msgid "What appointment have you made for the naming of the folders? Make sure names are relatively short, and avoid spaces and special characters."
msgstr "您針對資料夾命名做了哪些約定？請確保名稱儘量簡短，並避免使用空格與特殊字元。"

#: question/c39edad5-fc9a-4649-9c8f-dbebd6902578/title
msgid "Will you use a (sub)folder for each step in the analysis workflow?"
msgstr "是否會為分析工作流程中的每個步驟建立一個（子）資料夾？"

#: question/dad8247a-3553-48dc-8518-d64057cded1e/title
msgid "What are the naming conventions for these folders?"
msgstr "這些資料夾的命名規則是什麼？"

#: question/3d0e0a6e-24c0-421c-8656-fc7c1e6f79be/title
msgid "What appointments have you made about the naming of files?"
msgstr "您對檔案命名做了哪些約定？"

#: question/3d0e0a6e-24c0-421c-8656-fc7c1e6f79be/text
msgid "Make sure names are relatively short, and avoid spaces and special characters. You can use underscore characters, and consider using unique identifiers for the samples/experiments. You can consider to add versioning using the date in YYYYMMDD format."
msgstr "請確保名稱相對簡短，並避免使用空格與特殊字元。您可以使用底線，並可考慮為樣本／實驗使用唯一識別碼。您也可以考慮以 YYYYMMDD 格式的日期加入版本標示。"

#: question/a2e22a59-4747-4c29-84c0-3a9cbd859249/title
msgid "Did you document how you manage file versioning?"
msgstr "您是否有記錄檔案版本管理的方式？"

#: reference/68a842d8-280a-43fc-82c6-1de8b9821d17/label
msgid "RDMkit on Data Organisation"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料組織頁面"

#: reference/1d5185e5-b4f3-40c5-8a6e-b8f3dfe098f5/label
msgid "DMEG on File Structure"
msgstr "DMEG 的檔案結構頁面"

#: question/dc39957e-688a-4f71-a6a8-57f52509e7cf/title
msgid "Will you be storing data in an \"object store\" or a \"document store\" system?"
msgstr "您是否會將資料儲存在「物件儲存」或「文件儲存」系統中？"

#: question/dc39957e-688a-4f71-a6a8-57f52509e7cf/text
msgid "Some \"file\" storage systems do not have a tree structure like we know in a file system, but rather have direct pointers to any file in the system. Such systems are called \"object stores\" or \"document stores\". Examples are Amazon S3 and CEPH, or MongoDB."
msgstr "有些「檔案」儲存系統不像一般檔案系統那樣採用我們熟悉的樹狀結構，而是透過可直接指向系統中任一檔案的方式來存取。這類系統稱為「物件儲存」或「文件儲存」，例如 Amazon S3、CEPH 和 MongoDB。"

#: question/7dcf6059-b22c-44e9-8048-c8b8b90764ca/title
msgid "What are the naming conventions for objects in the store?"
msgstr "物件儲存中的物件命名規則是什麼？"

#: question/7dcf6059-b22c-44e9-8048-c8b8b90764ca/text
msgid "Make sure names are relatively short, and avoid spaces and special characters. You can use underscore characters, and consider using unique identifiers for the samples/experiments, workflow invocations, and processing steps. You can consider to add versioning using the date in YYYYMMDD format."
msgstr "請確保名稱相對簡短，並避免使用空格與特殊字元。您可以使用底線，並可考慮為樣本／實驗使用唯一識別碼。您也可以考慮以 YYYYMMDD 格式的日期加入版本標示。"

#: reference/70820c40-99b2-4a5e-9bb5-71135d6c92e0/label
msgid "Wikipedia on object storage"
msgstr "Wikipedia 的物件儲存頁面"

#: reference/e27878a0-c9f0-4aef-8f15-858418336a75/label
msgid "RDMkit on Data Storage"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料儲存頁面"

#: question/4539a575-6bdd-4077-a2fd-71b8121e2e06/title
msgid "Will you use a database system to store project data?"
msgstr "您是否會使用資料庫系統儲存計畫資料？"

#: question/bf52613c-1bfb-47b6-87cc-42f54de79129/title
msgid "How will you handle changes in the data?"
msgstr "您會如何處理資料的變更？"

#: question/bf52613c-1bfb-47b6-87cc-42f54de79129/text
msgid "Database systems can be configured to keep all data, so that it is possible to reconstruct any past state of the data. How are changes in the data handled by your database?"
msgstr "資料庫系統可設定為保留所有資料，以便重建資料在過去任一時間點的狀態。請說明您的資料庫如何處理資料變更？"

#: answer/24219df8-dfb8-4c7d-94fa-fd329e9468b7/label
msgid "Data in the database will be read-only"
msgstr "資料庫中的資料會採唯讀模式"

#: answer/29ba619b-28a1-46c3-b6aa-40a7668b6fe8/label
msgid "We will be allowing Create, Update and Delete"
msgstr "我們會允許建立、更新與刪除"

#: answer/7f3ccbe5-7650-4c85-b60f-141e269b5976/label
msgid "Modifications will be made by Expiring the existing data and Adding updated data"
msgstr "修改會透過將既有資料設為失效，並新增更新後資料的方式進行"

#: question/65730a4d-40db-46c9-b6d2-2b44b35f617e/title
msgid "Are you storing (some of your) data in an application specific manner?"
msgstr "您是否使用特定應用程式儲存（部分）資料？"

#: question/65730a4d-40db-46c9-b6d2-2b44b35f617e/text
msgid "Are you using e.g. an Electronic Lab Notebook (ELN) or Electronic Data Capture (EDC) application? Such applications often have their own data structure that can only be accessed through the application."
msgstr "您是否使用電子實驗室記錄本 (ELN; Electronic Lab Notebook)或電子資料擷取 (EDC; Electronic Data Capture) 系統等工具？這類應用程式通常具有其專屬的資料結構，且僅能透過該應用程式存取。"

#: answer/d5575f62-2083-403f-b41c-5560a5387da8/advice
msgid "Note that using the data that is stored in such a system will need to be exported in some standard way before it becomes available for other data analysis tools."
msgstr "請注意，儲存在此類系統中的資料，在可供其他資料分析工具使用之前，必須先以某種標準方式匯出。"

#: reference/0cf8efcf-8300-4fdc-9d4f-fcf7b9dc5671/label
msgid "RDMkit on data storage"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料儲存頁面"

#: reference/2757f8e9-e3a8-44fb-af90-f650570305c0/label
#: reference/ed8502b4-0043-4847-8db5-62377f135a3e/label
msgid "DMEG on Storage"
msgstr "DMEG 的儲存頁面"

#: question/4ba3304e-225c-4916-bbf7-754de381253c/title
msgid "Workflow development"
msgstr "工作流程開發"

#: question/4ba3304e-225c-4916-bbf7-754de381253c/text
msgid "It is likely that you will be developing or modifying the workflow for data processing. There are a lot of aspects of this workflow that can play a role in your data management, such as the use of an existing work flow engine, the use of existing software vs development of new components, and whether every run needs human intervention or whether all data processing can be run in bulk once the work flow has been defined."
msgstr "您很可能會開發或修改資料處理工作流程。此工作流程中的許多面向都可能影響資料管理，例如是否使用既有工作流程引擎、使用既有軟體或開發新元件，以及每次執行是否都需要人工介入，或是在定義好工作流程後即可批次執行所有資料處理。"

#: answer/4d74014e-588d-4a1d-a343-9bc3a4d72e25/label
msgid "This has been arranged"
msgstr "已安排妥當"

#: answer/bb00eb32-e1c2-4288-a874-02264f757cb3/label
msgid "More guidance is desired"
msgstr "需要更多指引"

#: question/13c2a033-423c-4bb3-b596-840de2f6c9c9/title
msgid "Will you be exploring parameters to the workflow, or run in bulk?"
msgstr "您會探索工作流程參數，還是批次執行工作流程？"

#: question/13c2a033-423c-4bb3-b596-840de2f6c9c9/text
msgid "What will be the operational mode for your workflows? Will you be exploring options by changing tools and tweaking parameters? Of will you be running the same exact workflow on a large number of data files?"
msgstr "您的工作流程會採用哪一種運作模式？您會透過更換工具與調整參數來探索不同選項，還是會對大量資料檔案執行完全相同的工作流程？"

#: answer/ec5b49f0-2a91-47fa-aee2-9636b8f9f2d0/label
msgid "We will be exploring parameters to the workflow"
msgstr "我們會探索工作流程參數"

#: answer/a91af528-0ab7-4b23-8b27-b131a7731dce/label
msgid "We will be running in bulk"
msgstr "我們會批次執行工作流程"

#: answer/f357ae1a-6563-48dd-add2-580e1f1a565d/label
msgid "A bit of both"
msgstr "兩者兼具"

#: question/14ed71a8-80c6-465a-94db-1115502297bd/title
msgid "What data will the workflow developers or implementers use?"
msgstr "工作流程開發者或實作者會使用哪些資料？"

#: question/14ed71a8-80c6-465a-94db-1115502297bd/text
msgid "The people implementing the data analysis work flow for your project probably need test data that they can use to see whether what they build works. How will this be arranged?"
msgstr "為您的計畫實作資料分析工作流程的人，可能需要測試資料來確認建置出的內容是否能正常運作。這將如何安排？"

#: answer/e8779d3b-8292-429e-a9b1-3df49c495674/label
msgid "They do not need data"
msgstr "他們不需要資料"

#: answer/9d7f9c48-0907-4798-b7bd-454505a54b1a/label
msgid "They can use existing data from another project"
msgstr "他們可以使用其他計畫的既有資料"

#: answer/3996826a-b67a-42e7-9223-f2a438fddbe6/label
msgid "They can use data from our project"
msgstr "他們可以使用我們計畫的資料"

#: question/c56f2e8f-bb78-412e-b238-974a14482f28/title
msgid "When will they have access?"
msgstr "工作流程開發者何時可以取用資料？"

#: answer/94f0f330-54fd-425f-a644-b8a7c674026f/label
msgid "Data will be available at the start of the project, no waiting needed"
msgstr "計畫開始時即可取用資料，無需等待"

#: answer/4844d32a-be6a-490a-b12e-3a31503d7bd1/label
msgid "They can start with a subset as soon as our first data comes"
msgstr "第一批資料可供使用後，他們就可以先使用這資料的一部份"

#: answer/e5bc08e1-815f-44f6-94ea-3a32e1808d51/label
msgid "Workflow development will commence as soon as our data is available"
msgstr "資料可供使用後，即會開始工作流程開發"

#: answer/e5bc08e1-815f-44f6-94ea-3a32e1808d51/advice
msgid "Take this into account when doing the time planning for the critical path"
msgstr "在規劃關鍵路徑的時程時，請將此納入考量"

#: question/d206fcaf-a238-48ef-925e-6f006d39f2af/title
msgid "How will data security be dealt with?"
msgstr "您會如何處理資料安全？"

#: answer/01a9f738-7950-4ee0-b9d0-ecd0df8fa7f2/label
msgid "Data security is not an issue"
msgstr "資料安全沒有顧慮"

#: answer/2359684e-be7f-4990-8f2e-84079ceb48c3/label
msgid "Data will not be on systems owned by workflow developers"
msgstr "資料將不會儲存在由工作流程開發者持有的系統上"

#: answer/340ae978-4435-4b20-87bf-0d65d82ac7b2/label
msgid "Data will always be encrypted"
msgstr "資料都會加密"

#: question/9a1c0153-3eae-40d5-8e91-66e108ef1fe8/title
msgid "List existing software components you will use in the analysis workflow"
msgstr "請列出您會在分析工作流程中使用的既有軟體元件"

#: question/9a1c0153-3eae-40d5-8e91-66e108ef1fe8/text
msgid "Your workflow may be available in components from different sources. Specify the different parts that you recognize and that you will each acquire in a different way."
msgstr "您的工作流程可能由來自不同來源的多個軟體元件組成。請列出您能辨識的各個元件，並說明您會如何取得它們。"

#: question/9c08ca3b-7cf9-4275-99c5-7be1aa14659f/title
#: question/76254a17-95d4-4f02-826e-eefd360bc38c/title
msgid "Software component:"
msgstr "軟體元件："

#: question/996df4e8-90ea-4aaf-8c3d-d92b3d145dd3/title
msgid "Where are you getting this software from?"
msgstr ""

#: question/996df4e8-90ea-4aaf-8c3d-d92b3d145dd3/text
msgid "Please specify a web address if available."
msgstr ""

#: question/cfb67fc9-4a65-4221-87ca-7ca7c99f13a4/title
msgid "What version of this software will you use?"
msgstr "您會使用此軟體的哪一個版本？"

#: answer/d707aef1-856d-4ab1-903a-2bccdd0c9a65/label
msgid "The exact version that we point to"
msgstr "我們指定的確切版本"

#: answer/6730b8b5-7abe-41e5-b97c-08e1f32fb523/label
msgid "The current version, and we will stick with that"
msgstr "目前版本，並且我們會固定使用該版本"

#: answer/e3e4240a-0785-4a76-9dd6-ce073abf643b/label
msgid "Whatever is the latest version at the time the analysis is run"
msgstr "執行分析時的最新版本"

#: question/b482e4e9-9435-4e2c-9ce5-e35845ba53b0/title
msgid "Will you re-run any analysis when a new version comes out?"
msgstr "新版本發布時，您是否會重新執行任何分析？"

#: answer/de969453-db1e-48b3-9024-6ed9fc23152f/label
msgid "If there is potentially a better result"
msgstr "如果可能有更好的結果"

#: answer/de969453-db1e-48b3-9024-6ed9fc23152f/advice
#: answer/7e0cd029-7588-4a94-9bfc-506dda26066d/advice
msgid "Make sure to take that into account when calculating the need for compute resources"
msgstr "請務必在估算所需運算資源時，將這點納入考量"

#: question/b66496d0-6fd4-4854-8f07-961045de4b7c/title
msgid "How is your experience with this software?"
msgstr "您對此軟體的熟悉程度為何？"

#: answer/30aedfab-3199-43b8-bcc6-caffad6148f0/label
msgid "We know the software well"
msgstr "我們很熟悉這個軟體"

#: answer/4140dd2d-aeb0-4cb8-960b-b46e74305dd5/label
msgid "We know the authors well"
msgstr "我們很熟悉軟體作者"

#: answer/e97a9384-85b6-464a-9d06-3a22f29a4465/label
msgid "We will gather experience by visiting others who have used it"
msgstr "我們會向使用過該軟體的人請教，以累積經驗"

#: answer/d1a1cac8-a82c-4ef4-8f25-7dc196bdcf70/label
msgid "We will use the manual"
msgstr "我們會參考使用手冊"

#: question/2109e98d-fe60-412d-8e72-48b47a181627/title
msgid "List new software components you will develop for the analysis workflow"
msgstr "請列出您會為分析工作流程開發的新軟體元件"

#: question/2109e98d-fe60-412d-8e72-48b47a181627/text
msgid "Not all components you need may be available already. Please list here what you will be developing yourself. Do not underestimate the time needed to integrate components into a work flow!"
msgstr "您需要的元件可能並非都已存在。請在此列出您將自行開發的項目。請不要低估將元件整合到工作流程中所需的時間！"

#: question/dbf05c2a-0108-4cae-947d-c0383140f006/title
msgid "Please specify the software repository you use for development"
msgstr "請具體說明在開發時，您會用哪個軟體儲存庫 (software repository)"

#: question/dbf05c2a-0108-4cae-947d-c0383140f006/text
msgid "Preferably use a direct URL other users could use"
msgstr "最好使用其他使用者也可以直接使用的網址"

#: question/99f4a43c-9848-488a-9b99-ff8dd6a4269c/title
msgid "Did you consider existing options?"
msgstr "您是否考量了現有的（軟體）選項？"

#: answer/1f53a431-ec8d-4a16-875a-c2f7843a2294/label
msgid "Nothing like this exists"
msgstr "目前沒有類似的東西"

#: answer/1f53a431-ec8d-4a16-875a-c2f7843a2294/advice
msgid "really?"
msgstr "真的嗎？"

#: answer/37f92ce2-48e9-4437-bb34-b034b69ad4a2/label
msgid "Authors of similar alternatives are not willing to work with us"
msgstr "其他類似替代方案的作者不願意與我們合作"

#: answer/45aa7af4-137a-4db6-abd7-2260e32f40a5/label
msgid "Alternatives exist, but we prefer to develop our own"
msgstr "有替代選項，不過我們偏好自己開發"

#: answer/f43fbe42-2e6c-4c96-a66d-a717c68e63ec/label
msgid "This will be one of the prime distinctive outcomes of our project"
msgstr "這會是我們計畫主要的特色成果之一"

#: question/3b0f752e-e46b-4c8b-835f-14c426036ece/title
msgid "What licence will you use for your tool?"
msgstr ""

#: question/3b0f752e-e46b-4c8b-835f-14c426036ece/text
msgid "Make sure the licence is compatible with all components you use, and also make sure the licence is made explicit in the repository."
msgstr ""

