msgstr "chipster"

#: question/558f01a3-2563-4114-9244-812b212c9791/title
msgid "Do you plan taking special measures to guarantee the integrity of tools in the workflow?"
msgstr "您是否計劃採取特別措施，來確保工作流程中工具的完整性？"

#: answer/fe13a1d8-06be-430c-a486-7346b769b48f/advice
msgid "Consider changing this!"
msgstr "考慮修改這部分！"

#: question/4b4d5878-970b-41aa-bbf5-15072e704417/title
msgid "Will you only use well-scrutinised open source tools?"
msgstr ""

#: question/5ea8a4fd-4bed-48a9-aacf-71e2d4953eb4/title
msgid "Will you have all changes checked by a second developer before deploying them?"
msgstr "您是否會在部署前，讓第二位開發者檢查所有變更？"

#: question/cd44886c-877f-4387-b299-f8d81b559f73/title
msgid "How will you handle upgrades to tools?"
msgstr "您將如何處理工具的升級？"

#: answer/805ed3e6-a9c0-4f57-b62b-c82c42b4761b/label
msgid "We will trust a new release and deploy"
msgstr "我們會信任新版本並部署"

#: answer/272626a8-90f7-4339-9f9b-a3fc7f1c8968/label
msgid "We will offer multiple versions of tools for the end user to choose"
msgstr "我們會提供多個工具版本供終端使用者選擇"

#: answer/9437d4c6-46e3-4f59-88e0-a1eea71d912f/label
msgid "We will only deploy selected stable upgrades to tools"
msgstr "我們只會部署經挑選且穩定的工具升級版本"

#: answer/b585a5f5-accf-43c1-9ccf-4e88e08ca132/label
msgid "We will test all tool changes on a subset of our own data before deployment"
msgstr "我們會先使用自己的部分資料測試所有工具變更，再進行部署"

#: answer/67bf1b45-722b-44ed-877f-37eaf66dc41b/label
msgid "We will not change tool versions after the initial selection"
msgstr "初次選定後，我們不會變更工具版本"

#: answer/67bf1b45-722b-44ed-877f-37eaf66dc41b/advice
msgid "Please consider how you will be solving issues/problems you find yourself and that are fixed in a new release"
msgstr "請思考當您自行發現問題，而新版本已修復這些問題時，您將如何處理"

#: question/099902bd-1637-4e32-a744-b95031030c6c/title
msgid "Will you test whether known correct results are obtained over time?"
msgstr "您是否會定期測試，確認仍能產生已知正確的結果？"

#: answer/4cc765a2-39b3-4790-bd7d-979361677a20/label
msgid "Yes, we will regularly make test runs on the same data"
msgstr "是，我們會定期使用相同資料執行測試"

#: answer/c9c66274-13b1-4ab8-8245-56ab7415d858/label
msgid "Yes, we will automatically make test runs on the same data"
msgstr "是，我們會自動使用相同資料執行測試"

#: reference/908be822-51b8-4f6b-9e61-7036f73dd0d3/description
msgid "Validation input data"
msgstr "驗證用輸入資料"

#: question/df3aff84-acf9-4614-996b-e69f7ddb96de/title
msgid "Are all tools you use under your complete control?"
msgstr "您使用的所有軟體工具，是否都在您的完全掌控之下？"

#: answer/af507b8a-824b-4198-9adf-c54f984f4fb5/label
msgid "No, we use tools maintained by others"
msgstr "不，我們使用的是由他人維護的工具"

#: question/94898b30-877d-4776-a03a-c57c93a725ac/title
msgid "How will you deal with the situation where support for a tool is dropped?"
msgstr "當某項工具停止支援時，您將如何因應？"

#: answer/d3fe6de8-b411-41c7-a336-c49e37d4b9d1/label
msgid "We will keep running it unchanged"
msgstr "我們會維持原樣繼續執行"

#: answer/8e9bcaec-cc3a-45e3-a430-3cbf1488a2a3/label
msgid "We will start to do necessary maintenance ourselves"
msgstr "我們會開始自行維護必要項目"

#: answer/523531e2-b2ae-4fbd-90a3-c2c007a9f04e/label
msgid "We will look for alternatives"
msgstr "我們會尋找替代方案"

#: answer/614310a5-9bfd-49ae-9bec-5ec45cacad22/label
msgid "Yes, we only use tools that we can maintain ourselves"
msgstr "是，我們只使用自己能維護的工具"

#: reference/df070071-38a9-4250-a035-445c12f95af3/description
msgid "Control over tools in the workflow engine"
msgstr "對工作流程引擎中工具的控制權"

#: question/730bf055-5e8e-4837-992c-d8a071855b4f/title
msgid "Will you make your workflow FAIR?"
msgstr "您是否會讓工作流程符合 FAIR 原則？"

#: question/730bf055-5e8e-4837-992c-d8a071855b4f/text
msgid "If you publish your workflow in a FAIR way, others will be able to build on your work more easily."
msgstr "如果您以符合 FAIR 原則的方式發布您的工作流程，其他人將能更容易在您的成果基礎上進一步發展。"

#: reference/0d83c012-eb25-4078-a5e2-139fe6b31cb7/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on making Workflows FAIR"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook：讓工作流程符合 FAIR 原則"

#: question/1991077f-04ae-4808-90a5-e4b2f82e30bf/title
msgid "How will you make sure to know what exactly has been run?"
msgstr "您會如何確認實際執行了哪些工作？"

#: question/5e111fc1-9d17-4ec8-aafb-1694a538a3aa/title
msgid "Will you keep results together with all processing scripts or workflows including documentation of the versions of the tools that have been run?"
msgstr "您是否會將結果與所有處理腳本或工作流程一併保存，並附上所執行工具的版本資訊文件？"

#: question/a972fba5-7586-4156-bdf8-8251288dc341/title
msgid "Will you make use of the metadata fields in your output data files to register how the data was obtained?"
msgstr "您是否會利用輸出資料檔案中的後設資料欄位，記錄資料取得方式？"

#: question/a972fba5-7586-4156-bdf8-8251288dc341/text
msgid "File formats like VCF (for genetics) and TIFF (for images) have possibilities to document metadata in the file header. It is a good idea to use work flow tools that use these fields to document what was done to obtain the data."
msgstr "像 VCF（用於基因資料）和 TIFF（用於圖像）這類檔案格式，都可以在檔案標頭中記錄後設資料。建議使用能夠利用這些欄位的工作流程工具，記錄資料取得的過程及處理步驟。"

#: question/decb7c9c-c6dc-4027-8c0e-18934c852ca6/title
msgid "Will you use a central repository for all tools and their versions as used in your project?"
msgstr "您是否會使用中央儲存庫管理計畫中使用的所有工具及其版本？"

#: question/decb7c9c-c6dc-4027-8c0e-18934c852ca6/text
msgid "Especially if analysis and processing of data in the project is done on multiple different computers by different people, it is a good idea to have your own repository of tools and their blessed versions."
msgstr "特別是當計畫中的資料分析與處理是由不同人員在多台不同的電腦上進行時，建立自己的工具及其穩定發布版本的儲存庫會是一個好主意。"

#: reference/257d126a-611d-475d-a86d-752131f7c7e8/label
msgid "RDMkit on Package management systems"
msgstr "RDMkit 的軟體套件管理系統頁面"

#: question/4c7cd15f-90f9-4ab3-8082-38da4f642de1/title
msgid "Will you use a central repository for reference data used in your project?"
msgstr "您是否會使用中央儲存庫管理計畫中使用的參考資料？"

#: question/4c7cd15f-90f9-4ab3-8082-38da4f642de1/text
msgid "Especially if analysis and processing of data in the project is done on multiple different computers by different people, it is a good idea to have your own repository of reference data versions."
msgstr "特別是當計畫中的資料分析與處理是由不同人員在多台不同的電腦上進行時，建立自己的參考資料版本儲存庫會是一個好主意。"

#: question/49199b05-73d7-4912-a5ca-bc1e14a09468/title
msgid "Will you make use of standard workflow engines and automatic work flows for all data analysis in the project?"
msgstr "您是否會在計畫的所有資料分析中使用標準工作流程引擎與自動化工作流程？"

#: question/49199b05-73d7-4912-a5ca-bc1e14a09468/text
msgid "It is much easier to guarantee consistency and reproducibility if all data processing is done using automated work flows, especially if the workflow engine automatically keeps adequate provenance data."
msgstr "如果所有資料處理都使用自動化工作流程來完成，就更容易確保一致性與可重現性；若工作流程引擎會自動保留足夠的資料溯源資訊，效果尤其明顯。"

#: reference/d522881a-9f3e-45fc-a420-f444e4da3ad0/description
msgid "Provenance as selection criterion for workflow engine"
msgstr "將溯源資訊作為工作流程引擎的選擇準則"

#: question/56bc8ebb-aba5-4745-8034-17ed3fe4fe07/title
msgid "Are all software tools in the work flow professionally maintained, with version control?"
msgstr "工作流程中使用的所有軟體工具是否皆有專業維護，並採用版本控制？"

#: question/56bc8ebb-aba5-4745-8034-17ed3fe4fe07/text
msgid "Will you be able to find and reproduce exactly which version was used for any analysis? Not only for the major tools in the workflows, but also for all 'glue' code and small tools you created especially for the project?"
msgstr "您是否能查明任一分析所使用的確切版本，並加以重現？這不只包括工作流程中的主要工具，也包括所有串接用程式碼，以及您專為本計畫建立的小型工具？"

#: question/918d5fd1-ea37-468f-8acd-ca3e80203900/title
msgid "How will you validate the integrity of the results?"
msgstr "您會如何驗證研究結果的完整性？"

#: question/e8a08f27-9f82-4147-b446-822d34a5d468/title
msgid "Will you run a subset of your jobs several times across the different compute infrastructures you are using?"
msgstr "您是否會在所使用的不同運算基礎設施上，重複執行作業子集？"

#: question/e8a08f27-9f82-4147-b446-822d34a5d468/text
msgid "There are surprisingly many complications that can cause (slight) inconsistencies between results when workflows are run on different compute infrastructures. A good way to make sure this does not bite you is to run a subset of all jobs on all different infrastructure to check the consistency."
msgstr "當工作流程在不同運算基礎設施上執行時，許多意想不到的複雜因素都可能導致結果之間出現（輕微）不一致。避免這類問題的好方法，是在各個不同基礎設施上執行所有作業中的一個子集，以檢查結果是否一致。"

#: question/a3a4ce37-4ced-41df-8ec6-e42d87a6a3f1/title
msgid "Will you be instrumenting the tools into pipelines and workflows using automated tools?"
msgstr "您是否會使用自動化工具，將各項工具整合到管線與工作流程中？"

#: question/a3a4ce37-4ced-41df-8ec6-e42d87a6a3f1/text
msgid "Surrounding all tools in your data processing and analysis workflows with the 'boilerplate' code necessary on the computer system you are using is tedious and error prone. Especially if you are using the same tools in multiple different work flows and/or on multiple different computer architectures. Automated instrumentation, e.g. by using a workflow management system, can prevent many mistakes."
msgstr "在資料處理與分析工作流程中，若要為每個工具加入您所使用電腦系統所要求的「樣板程式碼」，不僅繁瑣，也容易出錯。尤其是在多個不同工作流程，或多種不同電腦架構上使用相同工具時，更是如此。透過工作流程管理系統等方式進行自動化整合，可以避免許多錯誤。"

#: question/34a3ef8b-4a17-4030-9157-ed1c1bf60b80/title
msgid "Will you use independently developed duplicate tools or workflows for critical steps to reduce or eliminate human errors?"
msgstr "您是否會在關鍵步驟使用獨立開發的重複工具或工作流程，以減少或消除人為錯誤？"

#: question/34a3ef8b-4a17-4030-9157-ed1c1bf60b80/text
msgid "Validation of results without a golden standard is very hard. One way of doing it is to develop two solutions for a problem (two independent workflows or two independently developed tools) to check whether the results are identical or comparable."
msgstr "在沒有黃金標準的情形下，要來驗證結果就非常困難。其中一種做法是針對同一個問題開發兩套解法（兩個獨立工作流程，或兩個獨立開發的工具），用來檢查結果是否相同或可比較。"

#: question/faf72b3d-ac29-41d1-97f2-5223b199a086/title
msgid "Will you run part of the data set repeatedly to catch unexpected changes in results?"
msgstr "您是否會反覆執行部分資料集，以捕捉結果中的意外變化？"

#: question/faf72b3d-ac29-41d1-97f2-5223b199a086/text
msgid "Running a small subset of the data repeatedly can be useful to catch unexpected problems that would otherwise be very hard to detect."
msgstr "反覆執行一小部分資料，有助於找出那些原本很難偵測到的意外問題。"

#: reference/fbe68369-30cb-422b-b5c1-fd871bb16331/description
msgid "Validation of tools updates"
msgstr "工具更新的驗證"

#: question/e87ef779-2c4b-4c0d-a1f1-821290123a3c/title
msgid "Do you need to do compute capacity planning?"
msgstr "您是否需要進行運算資源容量規劃？"

#: question/e87ef779-2c4b-4c0d-a1f1-821290123a3c/text
msgid "If you require substantial amounts of compute power, amounts that are not trivially absorbed in what you usually have abailable, some planning is necessary. Do you think you need to do compute capacity planning?"
msgstr "如果您所需的運算能力相當龐大，已超出您平時可輕易負荷的範圍，那麼就有必要進行一些規劃。您認為自己需要進行運算資源容量規劃嗎？"

#: question/30027b9a-2077-4c74-9048-f0532ada9b03/title
msgid "Do you know how much CPU power, memory and I/O band width a typical analysis will take?"
msgstr "您是否清楚一次典型分析需要多少 CPU 運算能力、記憶體與 I/O 頻寬？"

#: question/30027b9a-2077-4c74-9048-f0532ada9b03/text
msgid "Did you run pilot jobs? Do you know this information from comparable projects? Did you test whether the work scales up as you expected if you run more than one job?"
msgstr "您是否執行過試行作業？這些資訊是否來自類似計畫？您是否測試過，在同時執行多個作業時，工作負載是否能如預期擴展？"

#: question/dd918787-ffb1-499e-98f8-42050758c7ce/title
msgid "What type of compute architecture is most suitable for your work? Will you have that available?"
msgstr "哪一種運算架構最適合您的工作？您是否能取得該架構？"

#: answer/75be8d48-34ba-4ac5-ba2c-b9fd435fe705/label
msgid "We will use cluster computing"
msgstr "我們會使用叢集運算"

#: answer/3a67d096-5028-48bf-8028-407db2cd3083/label
msgid "We will use grid computing"
msgstr "我們會使用網格運算"

#: answer/6ce8d928-2bb9-4df1-8d08-cbea2fc355fd/label
msgid "We will use cloud computing"
msgstr "我們會使用雲端運算"

#: answer/3a79dfdf-be0c-4835-bb89-4e1bc899cfbc/label
msgid "We will use a mix of computing architectures for different parts of the work"
msgstr "我們會針對工作的不同部分，使用多種運算架構"

#: question/851a72ac-9497-4d8a-ae1a-6509d021a20b/title
msgid "Is there sufficient experience with the chosen computing platform in the project, and sufficient time to support the project partners?"
msgstr "計畫團隊是否具備使用所選運算平台的足夠經驗，並有足夠時間支援計畫合作夥伴？"

#: answer/b1bdced0-f4f2-48f4-907f-d5fed58e15a2/label
msgid "We will recruit"
msgstr "我們會招募相關人員"

#: answer/2756894c-fe93-47da-ba87-3a31a06a1b70/label
msgid "Training has been arranged"
msgstr "已安排訓練"

#: answer/0fb8abbe-26fa-4756-a1e9-43476e5e1fd1/label
msgid "Our people will be able to call for help"
msgstr "我們的人員可尋求協助"

#: answer/23ce8320-0b90-4360-a9db-6001ad9e7582/label
msgid "We have sufficient knowledge in the project"
msgstr "計畫團隊具備足夠知識"

#: question/d8150021-19d7-4e92-90c3-d9c3d62d188e/title
msgid "Have you established with the provider when will you need the compute capacity?"
msgstr "您是否已與服務提供者確認何時需要運算容量？"

#: question/d8150021-19d7-4e92-90c3-d9c3d62d188e/text
msgid "Do you need the compute capacity also for development? Can you start developing locally and start with a deployment test later?"
msgstr "您在開發階段是否也需要運算容量？是否可以先在本機開發，之後再進行部署測試？"

#: question/4c71d62c-3184-43d7-bdec-f762c682035e/title
msgid "Is all required compute capacity available close to the project working storage area?"
msgstr "所有必要的運算資源是否都位於計畫工作儲存空間附近？"

#: question/a39fb276-8c46-49e7-bfb9-af8ba876726f/title
msgid "Did you plan the required network capacity between storage and compute services?"
msgstr "您是否已規劃儲存服務與運算服務之間所需的網路容量？"

#: answer/010b4ce6-0f52-437d-9971-681acdf37524/label
msgid "There are no special networking requirements"
msgstr "沒有特殊網路需求"

#: answer/acec64f8-f20b-4295-85d6-a8831ee6a1a3/label
msgid "Copying or network delays are considered to be acceptable"
msgstr "可接受資料複製或網路傳輸造成的延遲"

#: answer/b477c114-fa99-41db-aa52-b63c36ce662d/label
msgid "We will be able to use a dedicated network connection"
msgstr "我們可以使用專用網路連線"

#: question/3788d53f-c79f-43d2-b67b-7479f05cddb0/title
msgid "Can all data be legally transported and processed at the computing site?"
msgstr "所有資料是否都能依法傳輸至該運算地點並在當地處理？"

#: question/3788d53f-c79f-43d2-b67b-7479f05cddb0/text
msgid "Are the risks of data leaks covered?"
msgstr "是否已處理資料外洩風險？"

#: question/a0d52f2d-6828-42b0-a1f1-cda4ed7dad3b/title
msgid "Can your work flow and work flow system make use of \"trivial\" parallelism in the computations?"
msgstr "您的工作流程與工作流程系統是否能在計算中運用「簡單」平行處理？"

#: question/a0d52f2d-6828-42b0-a1f1-cda4ed7dad3b/text
msgid "If you need to perform many similar calculations of different input data (e.g. samples or simulations), these can often be executed at the same time on different nodes in a compute system. This is sometimes called \"trivial parallelism\". Even though it is named \"trivial\", this still requires that the work flow and workflow system support this (e.g. by making sure all file names are unique, and that not many threads are trying to read or write the same file at the same time). \n"
msgstr "如果您需要針對不同輸入資料（例如樣本或模擬）執行許多相似計算，這些計算通常可以在運算系統的不同節點上同時執行。這有時稱為「簡單平行處理」。雖然名稱中有「簡單」一詞，但仍需要工作流程與工作流程系統支援這種做法，例如確保所有檔名皆具唯一性，並避免過多執行緒同時嘗試讀取或寫入同一個檔案。 \n"

#: question/410f3709-c283-4974-83c8-6c5d24899a68/title
msgid "Will different groups work on different parts of the workflow? Will parts of the computing be done on 'local' infrastructure to the group?"
msgstr "不同團隊是否會處理工作流程的不同部分？部分運算是否會在各團隊的「本地」基礎設施上執行？"

#: answer/be99bdcc-76f2-43c3-b277-064062360dc1/label
msgid "All steps of the workflow will be performed at central computing locations"
msgstr "工作流程的所有步驟都會在集中式運算環境中執行"

#: answer/a2c4514b-61e4-47cf-ae54-7006fea37ec2/label
msgid "Some steps may be performed at local computing locations"
msgstr "某些步驟可能會在各團隊的本地運算環境中執行"

#: question/9e34d326-5f7b-494b-bc2e-2131eef6f844/title
msgid "Is there sufficient network capacity to the other computing locations?"
msgstr "是否有足夠的網路容量可連接至其他運算地點？"

#: reference/468bad94-ef86-4d24-8e97-d635fb1f68b0/description
msgid "Copying data into and out of the main working area of the project"
msgstr "將資料複製進／複製出計畫主要工作空間"

#: question/614ab69d-55a6-4214-b384-00ba21ce92a1/title
msgid "Is the risk of information loss, leaks and vandalism acceptably low?"
msgstr "資訊遺失、外洩及遭受惡意破壞的風險是否已降至可接受的程度？"

#: question/614ab69d-55a6-4214-b384-00ba21ce92a1/text
msgid "There are many factors that can contribute to the risk of information loss or information leaks. They are often part of the behavior of the people that are involved in the project, but can also be steered by properly planned infrastructure."
msgstr "有許多因素可能造成資訊遺失或資訊外洩風險。這些因素通常與計畫相關人員的行為有關，但也可以透過妥善規劃的基礎設施來引導與降低。"

#: question/90324a7b-f3c9-4ed8-b301-edc9869cb7b3/title
msgid "Do project members store data or software on computers in the lab or external hard drives connected to those computers?"
msgstr "計畫成員是否會將資料或軟體儲存在實驗室的電腦上，或儲存在連接至這些電腦的外接硬碟中？"

#: question/90324a7b-f3c9-4ed8-b301-edc9869cb7b3/text
msgid "When assessing the risk, take into account who has access to the lab, who has (physical) access to the computer hardware itself. Also consider whether data on those systems is properly backed up"
msgstr "評估風險時，請考量誰可以進入實驗室、誰可以（實體）接觸電腦硬體本身。也請考量這些系統上的資料是否有妥善備份"

#: question/abaf4a70-17d4-449c-9b95-5b3bcfed7e9b/title
msgid "Do project members carry data with them?"
msgstr "計畫成員是否會隨身攜帶資料？"

#: question/abaf4a70-17d4-449c-9b95-5b3bcfed7e9b/text
msgid "Does anyone carry project data on laptops, USB sticks or other external media?"
msgstr "是否有成員將計畫資料隨身存放在筆記型電腦、USB 隨身碟或其他外部儲存媒體中？"

#: question/6aff9a57-acea-4f6d-ac98-9a067e03cc8e/title
msgid "Are all data carriers encrypted?"
msgstr "是否所有資料載體皆已加密？"

#: question/26c19dc0-3e75-4ff6-a3b8-126ac54894aa/title
msgid "Are accounts on laptops password protected?"
msgstr "筆記型電腦上的帳號是否有密碼保護？"

#: question/84ec46bd-e714-4d98-8525-cdd0d58777ef/title
msgid "Do project members store project data in cloud accounts?"
msgstr "計畫成員是否將計畫資料儲存在雲端帳戶中？"

#: question/84ec46bd-e714-4d98-8525-cdd0d58777ef/text
msgid "Think about services like Dropbox, but also about Google Drive, Apple iCloud accounts, or Microsoft Office 365."
msgstr "請考慮 Dropbox 這類服務，也包括 Google Drive、Apple iCloud 帳號或 Microsoft Office 365。"

#: answer/b5e75eac-3db1-4736-8b22-7f8ed99218ab/advice
msgid "Make sure your users are aware of the risks of cloud storage (not so much that the cloud is unreliable, but there is no protection against \"accidentally\" sharing a cloud folder with people outside the project)."
msgstr "請務必讓您的使用者了解雲端儲存的風險（倒不見得是雲端本身不可靠，而是對於不小心將雲端資料夾分享給計畫外的人，沒有防護機制）。"

#: question/2d57daa6-df2e-4bf9-b024-710e74781d88/title
msgid "Do project members send project data or reports per e-mail or other messaging services?"
msgstr "計畫成員是否會透過電子郵件或其他即時通訊服務傳送計畫資料或報告？"

#: question/a454fffd-f4a4-426d-b758-6d70bc4ee96b/title
msgid "Do all data centres where project data is stored carry sufficient certifications?"
msgstr ""

#: question/39d8dad9-7666-405c-b35c-9e430c9691ed/title
msgid "Are all project web services addressed via secure http (https://)?"
msgstr "所有計畫的網路服務是否皆透過安全的 HTTP (HTTPS) 連線存取？"

#: question/dc327e53-cf4f-44e7-8e66-40ddf1b4ae0a/title
msgid "Have project members been instructed about the risks (generic and specific to the project)?"
msgstr "是否已向計畫成員說明相關風險（包括一般性風險及本計畫特有的風險）？"

#: question/dc327e53-cf4f-44e7-8e66-40ddf1b4ae0a/text
msgid "Project members may need to know about passwords (not sharing accounts, using different passwords for each service, and two factor authentication), about security for data they carry (encryption, backups), data stored in their own labs and in personal cloud accounts, and about the use of open WiFi and HTTPS."
msgstr "計畫成員可能需要了解密碼相關事項（例如不共用帳號、每項服務使用不同密碼，以及雙因素身分驗證）、隨身攜帶資料的安全性（加密、備份）、儲存在自己實驗室與個人雲端帳號中的資料，以及開放式 Wi-Fi 與 HTTPS 的使用。"

#: question/67c34ee1-2e71-423c-97a7-fe6aa3723465/title
msgid "Did you consider the possible impact to the project or organisation if information is lost?"
msgstr ""

#: answer/a8a4dc7d-bf8c-44e3-b8b2-3e04f206f460/label
#: answer/7c9c8543-b8f8-47b0-8279-757dbc14922f/label
#: answer/ae0c3b93-f054-4052-91c0-fa9c518f5ca8/label
msgid "Yes; the impact is negligible"
msgstr ""

#: answer/a0ec7128-1c2d-4034-b621-211bd01a9839/label
#: answer/6306207c-7be6-4cdf-86c4-33e0d9898479/label
#: answer/b1e1861b-b55f-406f-b915-b440c64d8747/label
msgid "Yes; the impact is acceptably low"
msgstr ""

#: answer/928db5fa-e16f-4c28-a321-ad62e1849b90/label
#: answer/efec7b38-d9a9-4495-8ba7-625dd7da6a09/label
#: answer/e8943baf-4c0c-4f30-8b57-88c06f3bc4ad/label
msgid "Yes; the impact is significant and requires action"
msgstr ""

#: question/a20ddc5d-e883-4bc4-9948-36a2cb477d10/title
msgid "Did you consider the possible impact to the project or organisation if information leaks?"
msgstr ""

#: question/a20ddc5d-e883-4bc4-9948-36a2cb477d10/text
msgid "Your institute may have a generic risk assessment; you should be informed about this."
msgstr "您的機構可能已有通用的風險評估機制；您應了解相關內容。"

#: question/8cd49d8f-9af0-4ea9-985a-5d45142ac388/title
msgid "Did you consider the possible impact to the project or organisation if information is vandalised?"
msgstr ""

#: question/d5990471-0618-42cd-92cb-bbbfd4f61532/title
msgid "Are personal data sufficiently protected?"
msgstr "個人資料是否受到充分的保護？"

#: answer/5d518250-a5d3-47f1-ada8-aa64c9ce3370/label
msgid "We are not using any personal information"
msgstr "我們不使用任何個人資料"

#: answer/75b86c10-4aeb-4f1a-89cd-8b380a2287b1/label
msgid "Yes, all personal information will be processed in pseudonymised form only"
msgstr ""

#: question/59748a7b-f729-404d-babe-3147e2c6b247/title
msgid "How is pseudonymisation handled?"
msgstr ""

#: answer/72c0a64f-a3ec-4d9e-bf37-ee0b25c2a084/label
msgid "We pseudonymise inside the project, only limited people can access the keys"
msgstr ""

#: answer/1653a04e-20e2-4929-9fd5-8c35402ac359/label
msgid "Pseudonymisation is handled by an independent party in order to allow data coupling"
msgstr ""

#: question/5d51a103-ec07-4c20-b269-f2f59f26d2cd/title
msgid "Who is the independent party that keeps the pseudonymisation keys?"
msgstr ""

#: answer/c5bdfb9d-33a7-4d0b-82cf-cde1911ad5bc/label
msgid "We have another way of pseudonymisation"
msgstr ""

#: question/eb876df3-5fb5-4885-9ab6-7dbfa6ba7427/title
msgid "What way are you pseudonymizing data?"
msgstr "您會以什麼方式對資料進行擬匿名化？"

#: reference/86f7c739-cfdf-4b3a-a032-3bda9bbf6404/label
#: reference/3fe12009-cd7c-4e4e-a7f8-2617c25c33c7/label
#: reference/00af9ed1-2627-45d7-89e8-63876fd92a2f/label
#: reference/68a9e378-e7ef-48bd-9e65-62937f7804d0/label
#: reference/4302bc15-31f1-42c0-b921-183847404605/label
#: reference/f22531ad-862e-48fa-a521-18e6998b1f7d/label
msgid "RDMkit on Data Sensitivity"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料敏感性頁面"

#: answer/ca0df149-cb95-404a-a925-0a1fc5052d1d/label
msgid "Yes, all data will be collected anonymously"
msgstr "是，所有資料都會以匿名方式蒐集"

#: answer/ca0df149-cb95-404a-a925-0a1fc5052d1d/advice
msgid "Note that it is very hard to make data anonymous, and GDPR requires that you regularly verify that it is still anonymous."
msgstr "請注意，要將資料真正匿名化非常困難；GDPR 也要求您定期確認資料仍維持匿名狀態。"

#: answer/44348fa8-fd12-49ea-ad7f-48ff88215829/label
msgid "Yes, all data will be anonymised as early as possible"
msgstr ""

#: answer/44348fa8-fd12-49ea-ad7f-48ff88215829/advice
msgid ""
"Please note that GDPR law in Europe specifies that data is only anonymous as long as nobody in the world has enough information to re-identify the subject.\n"
"\n"
"Furthermore, GDPR requires that you regularly verify that it is still anonymous."
msgstr ""
"請注意，歐盟《個人資料保護規則》規定，只有在全世界沒有任何人掌握足以重新識別資料主體的資訊時，資料才算是已匿名化。\n"
"\n"
"此外，GDPR 也要求您定期確認資料仍維持匿名狀態。"

#: question/acc82522-327a-4c76-8c24-f8034f7dc1d4/title
msgid "Do you have a contingency plan?"
msgstr "您是否有突發事件的應變計畫？"

#: question/acc82522-327a-4c76-8c24-f8034f7dc1d4/text
msgid "What will you do if the compute facility is down?"
msgstr "如果運算設施停擺，您會怎麼做？"

#: answer/05a642e0-4d1c-4c1e-ac9e-06463c2e97f4/label
msgid "We will wait until the problem is fixed"
msgstr "我們會等到問題修復"

#: answer/b430a132-0c46-4e16-9508-190801976633/label
msgid "We have an alternative"
msgstr "我們有替代方案"

#: chapter/83438863-0aa0-4458-b14b-2b2c0d4f811d/title
msgid "Interpreting data"
msgstr "對資料的解釋"

#: chapter/83438863-0aa0-4458-b14b-2b2c0d4f811d/text
msgid "The interpretation of the data consists of the last steps of processing (often with manual interventions), visualisation, and data integration. In this chapter many questions about data interoperability will come up."
msgstr "資料詮釋包含處理的最後幾個步驟（通常伴隨人工介入）、視覺化與資料整合。本章會涉及許多關於資料是否可相互操作的問題。"

#: question/a797cab9-0829-4787-a096-1b5cedc9147f/title
msgid "List the data formats you will be using for interpretation and describe their structure"
msgstr "請列出您將用於解釋的資料格式，並描述其結構"

#: question/a797cab9-0829-4787-a096-1b5cedc9147f/text
msgid ""
"Give each type of data a name that you recognise.\n"
"\n"
"If you have data in many different structures, integrating the data may be more challenging."
msgstr ""
"請為每種類型的資料取一個您可以辨識的名稱。\n"
"\n"
"若您的資料採用多種不同結構，資料整合可能更具挑戰。"

#: question/63ed4349-9743-4fd1-96df-73dbb7e4f05b/title
msgid "Data type"
msgstr "資料類型"

#: question/63ed4349-9743-4fd1-96df-73dbb7e4f05b/text
msgid "You will be presented with suggestions from [FAIRSharing](https://fairsharing.org/), but you also have the option to manually enter the data type that is not listed there."
msgstr "系統會顯示來自 [FAIRsharing](https://fairsharing.org/) 的建議項目，但您也可以手動輸入未列於其中的資料類型。"

#: question/87fe7235-0a0f-4788-8f44-04523461655f/title
msgid "How is this data structured?"
msgstr "這份資料的結構為何？"

#: answer/b308b8bb-83ed-4599-ae28-39c5c1218cbf/label
msgid "A structured domain specific file with data and metadata fields"
msgstr "包含資料與後設資料欄位的特定領域結構化檔案"

#: question/37531bec-1488-4204-807d-762794b538e9/title
msgid "Can all of the data you want to couple be captured in that format?"
msgstr "該資料格式是否能完整記錄您想要串接的所有資料？"

#: question/45efdccf-761e-4414-b6a8-1d28ddaeafec/title
msgid "Will you be doing it that way?"
msgstr "您是否會採用這種做法？"

#: question/8018e15f-6c7e-433a-8686-ae0d695c7fc7/title
msgid "Does the domain specific format come with its own suite of integration tools that you will use?"
msgstr "您所使用的特定領域資料格式，是否附有可供使用的整合工具組？"

#: answer/e8334918-27f8-4e1c-aa9f-5e8191b7fabb/label
msgid "A table or set of tables (consisting of 'data records')"
msgstr "一個表格或一組表格（由「資料記錄」組成）"

#: question/6bfde30e-90e7-4422-b984-d571196194e0/title
msgid "Does each column have a header?"
msgstr "每個欄位是否都有欄位名稱？"

#: question/6bfde30e-90e7-4422-b984-d571196194e0/text
msgid "In a table, the data items are arranged in columns. Is there a header for each of these describing what is in there?"
msgstr "在表格中，資料項目是以欄排列的。每個欄位是否都有欄位名稱，說明欄位內的內容？"

#: answer/595acdbc-f0d7-4550-9c56-9177f3c5695b/advice
msgid "You will need to have a header in order to make the data interoperable and reusable"
msgstr "您需要使用欄位名稱，才能讓資料可相互操作且可再次使用"

#: question/cacee0fd-7de5-4e07-aa94-1661cb853558/title
msgid "Are all column headers unambiguous?"
msgstr "是否所有欄位名稱都清楚且不具歧義？"

#: question/cacee0fd-7de5-4e07-aa94-1661cb853558/text
msgid "A human being quickly 'understands' data items and their relations. For good data reusability, it is necessary that computers can understand your data too."
msgstr "人類可以快速「理解」資料項目及其與其他資料之間的關係；為了讓資料更容易再次使用，電腦也必須能夠理解您的資料。"

#: answer/1485ec8b-094c-49bb-8de1-ce214c83790f/advice
msgid "Check whether you can find an ontology for each of your data items"
msgstr "請確認您是否能為每一個資料項目找到合適的知識本體 (ontology)"

#: question/6ab36a2a-23ca-484d-b3d7-0c1a4eea821a/title
msgid "Do all columns/headers have a data type?"
msgstr "每個欄位是否都有對應的資料類型？"

#: question/6ab36a2a-23ca-484d-b3d7-0c1a4eea821a/text
msgid "A label like 'temperature' only makes sense to a computer if it is also clear what the units are and what temperature has been measured. In many cases, it is also important how it was measured."
msgstr "像「溫度」這樣的名稱，對電腦而言只有在清楚標示使用的單位以及測量的是哪一種溫度時才有意義。在許多情況下，測量方法也相當重要。"

#: answer/7108a5e7-f804-4410-b40d-cabed6b3da15/advice
msgid "Check whether you can find a data type (potentially in a data type registry) for each of your data items"
msgstr "請確認您是否能為每一個資料項目找到對應的資料類型（或可參考資料類型登錄冊）"

#: question/c47d330a-2eb4-472e-be48-d06b3ec9b8e8/title
msgid "Are the limitations to allowed data values in each column explicit?"
msgstr "各欄位允許的資料值限制是否明確？"

#: question/c47d330a-2eb4-472e-be48-d06b3ec9b8e8/text
msgid "If there are reasonable limitations to the values in a column, or even a limited set of allowed values, it is very good for data validation and reusability if these limitations are explicit, and e.g. software used for data entry and editing will not allow anything else."
msgstr "如果某一欄位中的數值有合理的限制範圍，或甚至只允許有限的一組值，那麼若能將這些限制明確規定下來，將非常有助於資料驗證，也能讓資料更容易再次使用；例如，用於資料輸入與編輯的軟體就不應允許輸入其他不符合規定的值。"

#: answer/6bda04d8-1f32-4ace-ab8b-1121ea7c526e/advice
msgid "Check whether there is a way to explicitly limit data values."
msgstr "請確認是否有方法能明確限制資料值的範圍。"

#: reference/03640bc5-605b-4a3a-a5de-2dae66542b66/label
msgid "Rightfield: Template fields in Microsoft Excel"
msgstr "Rightfield: Microsoft Excel 中的範本欄位"

#: question/0259866a-50b2-4f77-858f-982c9e16091d/title
msgid "Is it clear what a row in the table represents?"
msgstr "是否清楚表格中的每一列代表什麼？"

#: question/ccaaf562-ebed-4d94-b168-b8398ed25546/title
msgid "Does each row have an identifier?"
msgstr "每一列資料是否都有識別碼？"

#: question/f90914d8-2731-4cd1-bbf8-2710a5e08c43/title
msgid "Is there a distinguishing way a missing value in the table can be recognised?"
msgstr ""

#: question/f90914d8-2731-4cd1-bbf8-2710a5e08c43/text
msgid "Sometimes, and empty field or a zero is indicating a missing value. But is that really unique? Could there be valid empty or zero fields? Has the convention for missing values been made explicit somewhere?"
msgstr "有時候，空欄位或數值 0 會被用來表示遺漏值。但這樣的表示方式真的具有唯一性嗎？是否也可能存在有效的空欄位或值為 0 的欄位？對於遺漏值的表示慣例，是否已在某處明確說明？"

#: question/0451d421-4c97-452e-b399-4fe278b97147/title
msgid "Is the relation between each of the columns and the record identifier clear?"
msgstr "每個欄位與記錄識別碼之間的關係是否清楚？"

#: question/0451d421-4c97-452e-b399-4fe278b97147/text
msgid "It may appear that in a table with 'patients' as rows, a column labeled 'disease' coupled to an ontology has a clear meaning. But that is not always explicit enough! A 'disease' could e.g. be the disease that the patient is suffering from, but it could also be an earlier diagnose, a suspected diagnose, or the disease a family member recently died of."
msgstr "在以「病人」為列的表格中，標示為「疾病」並連結到本體的欄位，看似有清楚意義。但這不一定足夠明確！「疾病」可能是病人罹患的疾病，也可能是先前診斷、疑似診斷，或造成家族成員近期死亡的疾病。"

#: question/bdaba73c-02e0-4ff1-acb3-a68df891c36a/title
msgid "Are all the relations between the column headers explicit?"
msgstr "所有欄位名稱之間的關係是否皆已明確定義？"

#: question/bdaba73c-02e0-4ff1-acb3-a68df891c36a/text
msgid "For a good understanding of tabular data, you need to make the relationship between each pair of columns explicit. E.g. if one column is 'disease' and another is 'treatment', you want to make sure that this is the chosen treatment that this person is undergoing for the given disease."
msgstr "為了正確理解表格式資料，您需要明確說明各欄位之間的關係。例如，若一個欄位是「疾病」，另一個欄位是「治療方式」，您需要清楚表示，此治療方式確實是此人因為該疾病所接受的療程。"

#: answer/d7911ab4-d3cc-4dc2-95cc-4aba7b0d010a/label
msgid "Complex data, like a graph"
msgstr "複雜的資料，例如圖形"

#: question/46e07a92-2070-4212-96ea-8b98da488292/title
msgid "Are you representing the graph in RDF?"
msgstr "您是否會以 RDF 表示此圖形？"

#: question/46e07a92-2070-4212-96ea-8b98da488292/text
msgid "RDF is the graph representation used in the 'semantic web'"
msgstr "RDF 是「語意網」使用的圖形表示方式"

#: question/3196c225-2842-4766-9768-381fd6ee1e05/title
msgid "Are all the URIs in the RDF resolving to common ontologies?"
msgstr "RDF 中所有 URI 是否皆可解析至通用知識本體( common ontologies)？"

#: question/3196c225-2842-4766-9768-381fd6ee1e05/text
msgid "The FAIR principles ask for the use of FAIR ontologies. It is better when using RDF to make use as much as possible of concepts that are in established and well-maintained ontologies on the internet."
msgstr "FAIR 原則要求使用符合 FAIR 原則的知識本體 (ontology)。在使用 RDF 時，最好盡可能採用網路上已建立且維護良好的本體中的概念。"

#: answer/30a6e365-dbf6-4567-96c3-b7301d0fd0ca/label
msgid "No, we made our own ontologies for our work; concepts are not mapped to common ontologies"
msgstr "不，我們為自身的工作建立了自己的本體；相關概念並未對應到通用知識本體 (common ontology)"

#: answer/945aae79-4eed-4115-ac19-d295158a19f6/label
msgid "No, we exclusively refer to our own ontologies for some classes of objects"
msgstr "不，對於某些類別的物件，我們只會參照我們自己的知識本體 (ontology)"

#: answer/88f9fb7b-12a9-481a-9239-cbf43206056e/label
msgid "Yes, (almost) all our concepts are either from common ontologies, or mapped to common ontologies"
msgstr "是，（幾乎）所有概念都來自通用知識本體 (common ontology)，或已對應到通用本體"

#: answer/13d7f11e-c329-45e8-8912-63755c8524d5/label
msgid "Images, audio or video tracks, with some structured metadata attached"
msgstr "附帶一些結構化後設資料的影像、音訊或影片檔"

#: answer/4e6d2cb0-1901-41dd-9902-6066739c9ab5/label
msgid "Differently"
msgstr "其他方式"

#: question/024bb661-70d4-4da6-a938-934a3935b16a/title
msgid "Describe the structure of the data"
msgstr "請描述資料的結構"

#: reference/ae540a5d-7f3c-4bf0-99a4-539d70a1dc6e/label
msgid "RDMkit on Machine Actionability"
msgstr "RDMkit 的機器可操作性頁面"

#: question/109ed7ea-ef1d-4719-b2b4-eb4f7202c65c/title
msgid "Will you be doing integration or linking of different data types?"
msgstr "您是否會整合或連結不同資料類型？"

#: question/109ed7ea-ef1d-4719-b2b4-eb4f7202c65c/text
msgid ""
"If you are getting different types of data from different sources and want to use them together it is likely that you will need to match items and glue everything together. This can be done with traditional table database technology, but it is also possible to use Linked Data and RDF.\n"
"\n"
"You may also need to use \"mappings\" to match data together."
msgstr ""
"如果您從不同來源取得不同類型的資料，並希望一起使用，通常需要先將各個項目彼此對應，再把所有資料整合起來。這可以透過傳統表格式資料庫技術完成，也可以使用資料連結 (Linked Data) 與 RDF。\n"
"\n"
"您也可能需要使用「對映」，將資料彼此對應並整合。"

#: question/ff85db18-565c-4177-a397-9a8cf4c7b374/title
msgid "What will be your approach?"
msgstr "您會採用什麼方法？"

#: question/ff85db18-565c-4177-a397-9a8cf4c7b374/text
msgid "Linked data is very suitable to integrate data, especially if the data sources are already represented as linked data."
msgstr "資料連結 (Linked Data) 非常適合用於資料整合，尤其當資料來源本身已經以資料連結表示時。"

#: answer/01aaaf8a-ee94-4cd0-8e36-adcb7ac9d18d/label
msgid "We will use \"flat files\""
msgstr "我們會使用扁平檔案"

#: answer/3c75eb37-03d7-414c-8bd3-0afa8170bfbc/label
msgid "We will use a tabular database"
msgstr "我們會使用表格式資料庫"

#: answer/3c75eb37-03d7-414c-8bd3-0afa8170bfbc/advice
msgid "Many standard database systems are available and often these are programmable in SQL."
msgstr "可用的標準資料庫系統很多，而且通常可以用 SQL 進行程式化操作。"

#: answer/9cea7792-3e4c-42a6-b7e0-1abbdc9e2a5b/label
msgid "We will use linked data"
msgstr "我們會使用資料連結 (Linked Data)"

#: question/811965f0-b1b7-4b4b-92a6-01cd83b08fa2/title
msgid "Are your data sources using linked data?"
msgstr "您的資料來源是否使用資料連結 (Linked Data)？"

#: answer/395c9651-9d92-48f7-b1fc-cdccbd681f57/label
msgid "Partly"
msgstr "部分"

#: question/fad678c7-99e4-48e2-a708-fe0dfa1381b8/title
msgid "Will you provide your results as semantically interoperable linked data?"
msgstr "您是否會以語意上可相互操作的資料連結 (Linked Data) 形式提供結果？"

#: question/532ddc6a-3415-4df8-8fa1-002ee486fd42/title
msgid "Are your sources using the same vocabularies or ontologies where possible?"
msgstr "您的資料來源是否盡可能使用相同的詞彙表或知識本體 (ontology)？"

#: question/532ddc6a-3415-4df8-8fa1-002ee486fd42/text
msgid "If sources are using different semantic resources, you will need to plan time to find or make the right mappings."
msgstr "若資料來源使用不同的語意資源，您需要預留時間來尋找或建立適當的對映。"

#: answer/9bd923d3-3132-4c0c-aec2-442186c893f5/advice
msgid "You should estimate how much time you will need for mapping the vocabularies together."
msgstr "您應估算將詞彙表彼此對映所需的時間。"

#: answer/11d2fd0d-59f2-42ce-a34a-84fac3f51862/label
msgid "We have another approach"
msgstr "我們有另一種方法"

#: question/266bcba8-9e8a-457c-8c2f-5a992a32512c/title
msgid "What approach?"
msgstr "採用什麼方法？"

#: reference/e9c41e81-ec67-43e2-aa9c-01e8c8841b12/label
msgid "Linked data (wikipedia)"
msgstr "Wikipedia：資料連結 (Linked Data)"

#: reference/b289c48c-b586-419f-8099-db94ce323398/description
msgid "Data warehousing tools"
msgstr "資料倉儲工具"

#: reference/412739e0-2dd4-475d-b4aa-0c5cb2e3d3bc/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on Interlinking data using mappings"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的「使用對映連結資料」頁面"

#: question/f67e1539-5c7d-4df7-8259-e4f2edfa2685/title
msgid "Will you be using common ontologies?"
msgstr "您是否會使用通用知識本體 (common ontologies)？"

#: answer/3e5ef321-76f3-4c65-a49f-4e03f6a23def/advice
msgid "Choose the ontologies before you start."
msgstr "請在開始之前先選定要使用的知識本體 (ontology)。"

#: question/9d44b89e-300d-4227-8642-c6b38b8b882d/title
msgid "List the ontologies you will be using"
msgstr "請列出您將使用的知識本體 ( ontologies )"

#: question/212a7e54-557d-4319-9f57-33148ae80a69/title
msgid "Name of the ontology"
msgstr "知識本體 (ontology)名稱"

#: question/6cf69cc9-bd6c-4e51-98a2-817d1d211720/title
msgid "Link to the ontology"
msgstr "知識本體 (ontology)連結"

#: reference/bc1a7f76-a2e4-426b-a360-48ea0a6cce80/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on selecting an ontology lookup service"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的知識本體 (ontology) 查詢服務選擇指南"

#: question/d0306914-c253-472c-869f-19a60578c087/title
msgid "Will there be potential issues with statistical normalisation?"
msgstr ""

#: question/dbb6dcdf-dd2e-4829-8c03-16b2339ebd5a/title
msgid "Will you be integrating different data sources to get more samples or more data points?"
msgstr "您是否會整合不同資料來源，以取得更多樣本或更多資料點？"

#: question/18f9b8ec-bf1b-4035-8eac-3fd329613a7c/title
msgid "Have these been collected with sufficiently identical protocols?"
msgstr "這些資料的蒐集協定是否足夠一致？"

#: question/d5d21ad3-720c-4a6a-bd5a-09f14b15666f/title
msgid "Will you be integrating different data sources in order to get more information for each sample or data point?"
msgstr "您是否會整合不同資料來源，以取得每個樣本或資料點的更多資訊？"

#: question/63b020de-664a-4271-807c-a6f4361d6439/title
msgid "Did you already select the variables on which you will join the data sets?"
msgstr "您是否已選定要用哪些變項來串接不同的資料集？"

#: question/c6fdeacb-4a1f-4948-988a-0c6458cdf7b9/title
msgid "Will you make sure that you do not inadvertently create a biased subset?"
msgstr "您是否會確保不會無意間建立有偏差的子集？"

#: question/c6fdeacb-4a1f-4948-988a-0c6458cdf7b9/text
msgid "Some parameters you select on may have been collected only for a subset of the subjects or data points. An obvious example is if you match on secondary education type, you will bias to people over 18 years old because younger people do not have this field. In many cases the selection bias may be a lot less obvious and special measures exist to verify that the diversity of the sample is not reduced by the integration step."
msgstr "您用來作為篩選條件的某些參數，可能只在受試者或資料點的某個子集中被蒐集到。明顯的例子是：如果您以中等教育類型作為配對條件，結果就會偏向 18 歲以上的人，因為年紀較小者並沒有這個欄位。在許多情況下，這種選擇偏差可能沒有那麼明顯；已有一些專門的方法，可用來驗證資料整合步驟是否降低了樣本的多樣性。"

#: question/6b3d62a5-1d4d-49e1-aaf1-0a8b398a7ac3/title
msgid "Could the coupling of data create a danger of re-identification of pseudo- or anonymised personal data?"
msgstr ""

#: answer/aad55658-91c1-4fb8-8869-c0dc1b02b96d/advice
msgid "Plan either preventative or corrective measures"
msgstr "請規劃預防性或矯正性措施"

#: question/15eb6fe6-7b21-493b-a5a0-09ac63212ab6/title
msgid "Did you make a conscious decision to be either accurate or complete?"
msgstr "您是否有意識地在準確性與完整性之間做出取捨？"

#: question/15eb6fe6-7b21-493b-a5a0-09ac63212ab6/text
msgid "If the coupling parameters are lenient, you will find more connections than when they are strict. But you may find that they are less accurate. This is a balance."
msgstr "如果資料串接參數設定得較寬鬆，您會找到比設定嚴格時更多的連結；但您可能也會發現，這些連結的準確性較低。這之間需要取得平衡。"

#: answer/d12bd4e1-2fed-4ea0-b428-fe6f735d740a/label
msgid "Accurate is more important"
msgstr "準確性更為重要"

#: answer/ced5f19d-eaa9-4576-82d4-7ef97741a7e0/label
msgid "We can balance the two"
msgstr "我們可以在兩者之間取得平衡"

#: answer/626fd6e7-8f74-4675-a097-5416f40685e2/label
msgid "Completeness of the mapping is most important"
msgstr "對映關係的完整性最為重要"

#: question/dc4f1dc7-4608-45f9-8503-aa05536f4d97/title
msgid "Do you have all tools to couple the necessary data types?"
msgstr "您是否具備串接必要資料類型所需的所有工具？"

#: question/e1dba221-ad5a-474e-a2e3-9b4e472959fa/title
msgid "Will you be using a federated analysis approach?"
msgstr "您是否會採用聯邦式分析方法？"

#: question/e1dba221-ad5a-474e-a2e3-9b4e472959fa/text
msgid ""
"In some cases it is not practical to bring all data together:\n"
"* It may be legally hard to collect the data in one place for analysis\n"
"* It may be technically hard to transport data to a single place for analysis\n"
"\n"
"In such cases, a Federated analysis approach may be applicable. Examples of such techniques are DataShield and the Personal Health Train. Secure multi-party computation may be useful too to prevent information leaking between parties."
msgstr ""
"在某些情況下，將所有資料彙集到同一處並不實際：\n"
"* 受法律因素限制，可能難以將資料彙集到同一處進行分析\n"
"* 受技術因素限制，可能難以將資料傳輸到同一處進行分析\n"
"\n"
"在這些情況下，可以採用聯邦式分析方法。這類技術的例子包括 DataShield 與 Personal Health Train。安全多方計算也可能有助於防止參與方之間發生資訊洩漏。"

#: question/460803f2-cc23-4c57-b50e-c5177a3c11d5/title
#: resourcePage/1b4ea983-9b5c-4a81-80ed-44d30d30d204/title
msgid "Will you be doing (automated) knowledge discovery?"
msgstr "您是否會進行（自動化）知識探索？"

#: chapter/d5b27482-b598-4b8c-b534-417d4ad27394/title
msgid "Preserving data"
msgstr "保存資料"

#: chapter/d5b27482-b598-4b8c-b534-417d4ad27394/text
msgid "In this chapter, issues regarding data publication and long term archiving are addressed."
msgstr "本章處理資料發布與長期典藏相關議題。"

#: question/4e0c1edf-660c-4ebf-81f5-9fa959dead30/title
msgid "Specify a list of data sets you will be producing"
msgstr "請列出您將產製的資料集"

#: question/4e0c1edf-660c-4ebf-81f5-9fa959dead30/text
msgid "Add all the data sets you will be producing. Give each a short name, sufficient for yourself to know what data it is about. It is useful to think about a data set as some collection of data that will be ending up in the same place."
msgstr "新增所有您會產製的資料集。給每個資料集一個簡短的名稱，讓自己知道這份資料是什麼。將資料集視為最終會存於相同位置的資料集合，有助於您管理資料。"

#: question/205a886d-83d7-4359-ae63-7103e05357c3/title
msgid "Description of the data set"
msgstr "資料集的描述"

#: question/205a886d-83d7-4359-ae63-7103e05357c3/text
msgid "What type of data is in this data set? Examples could be \"Field observations\", \"raw instrument data\", \"genomic variants\"."
msgstr "這個資料集中包含哪一種類型的資料？例如：「田野觀察資料」、「原始儀器資料」、「基因組變異」。"

#: question/3a8ed3fc-b1a6-4119-80ed-238804861734/title
msgid "What type of data is in this data set?"
msgstr "此資料集包含哪一類資料？"

#: answer/79f7797e-f7b1-4930-b691-84bee936af20/label
msgid "Raw data"
msgstr "原始資料"

#: answer/4fa0c31a-bd3b-4ae0-8f56-639ae2212124/label
msgid "Processed data leading to unpublishable results"
msgstr "無法發表結果的處理後資料"

#: answer/626a610e-34ac-40ca-8bf6-7926f580ae80/label
msgid "Processed data leading to published results"
msgstr "已發表結果的處理後資料"

#: question/19f71935-c4fa-4085-98a6-82686d656526/title
msgid "Specify a link to the paper"
msgstr "請指定論文連結"

#: question/19f71935-c4fa-4085-98a6-82686d656526/text
msgid "Provide a DOI if possible."
msgstr "若可行，請提供 DOI。"

#: question/cf727a0a-78c4-45a7-aa9b-cf7650ae873a/title
msgid "Identifier of the data set"
msgstr "資料集識別碼"

#: question/cf727a0a-78c4-45a7-aa9b-cf7650ae873a/text
msgid ""
"Please add all \"formal\" identifiers you have for this data set: these can be handles or DOIs or any other type. One important purpose of these identifiers is to be able to find the dataset back.\n"
"\n"
"A good identifier is _persistent_ (i.e. it does not change, and also the same identifier will never be used for another data set), _globally unique_ (nobody else uses the same identifier for a different data set) and _resolvable_ (you can actually locate the data set if you only know the identifier).\n"
"\n"
"Note that if you will be publishing the dataset in a repository, the repository may also assign a persistent identifier. You will be able to specify such additional identifiers under the \"publication\"-questions. Specify one main identifier here."
msgstr ""
"請加入此資料集的所有「正式」識別碼，例如 Handle、DOI 或其他類型的識別碼。這些識別碼的一項重要用途，是讓日後仍能找到該資料集。\n"
"\n"
"良好的識別碼應具備持續性（也就是不會變動，且同一個識別碼永遠不會再編配給另一個資料集）、全域唯一性（其他人不會將同一個識別碼用於不同資料集），並且可解析（只知道識別碼時，也能實際找到該資料集）。\n"
"\n"
"請注意，如果您會將資料集發布到資料儲存庫，該資料儲存庫也可能會編配持續識別碼。您可以在「發布」相關問題中指定這類額外識別碼。請在此指定一個主要識別碼。"

#: question/5c22cf59-89e3-43a1-af10-1af43a97bcb2/title
msgid "What type of identifier?"
msgstr "哪一種類型的識別碼？"

#: question/5c22cf59-89e3-43a1-af10-1af43a97bcb2/text
msgid ""
"Which type of identifier is this?   \n"
"Provide the type of identifier. You will be presented with suggestions from [FAIRsharing](https://fairsharing.org/), but you also have the option to manually enter the identifier type that is not listed there."
msgstr ""

#: question/9e13b2d3-5f00-4e19-8a52-5c33c5b1cb07/title
msgid "The actual identifier"
msgstr "識別碼"

#: question/a063da1c-aaea-4e18-85ec-f560d833f292/title
msgid "Will this data set be published?"
msgstr "這個資料集是否會發布？"

#: question/a063da1c-aaea-4e18-85ec-f560d833f292/text
msgid ""
"Will you publish the data set somewhere? Will it be findable for other people, even if not the whole world? What is not meant here is a paper about the interpretation of the data, but the data itself.\n"
"\n"
"Note that this does not necessarily mean that the data set becomes openly available, conditions for access and use may apply. "
msgstr ""
"您是否會將資料集發布到某個地方？即使不是向全世界開放，它是否仍可被其他人找到？這裡指的不是資料詮釋的論文，而是資料本身。\n"
"\n"
"請注意，這不一定表示資料集會完全開放；資料取用與使用可能仍會附帶條件。 "

#: question/2a34dbf7-3a9e-446e-9dfd-695903bd2a07/title
#: question/a18f00f4-0eef-4665-851a-6becde6c3226/title
#: question/ecd0f420-8b9e-4899-ada7-3e6a682b0e8b/title
#: question/5cf47d97-d32f-4cb4-8fb3-49f3717f0980/title
msgid "Why not?"
msgstr "原因是什麼？"

#: answer/deff3d55-a7bb-426e-94e7-8b6d46a27f8e/label
msgid "It is raw data that never needs to be reprocessed"
msgstr "這是永遠不需要重新處理的原始資料"

#: answer/309ee279-cd5a-47dd-ad11-7b111d0ac1ff/label
msgid "This data set only led to unpublishable results"
msgstr "這個資料集只產生了無法發表的結果"

#: answer/309ee279-cd5a-47dd-ad11-7b111d0ac1ff/advice
msgid "Are you sure the data set would not be re-usable in another context? Or that it could be valuable to prevent others having to perform the same experiment and coming to the same negative results?"
msgstr "您確定這個資料集無法在其他情境中再次使用嗎？或者，它是否能避免他人重複進行相同實驗、得到相同的負面結果？"

#: answer/cf378a0e-9efe-4221-a7a7-c0631fd71c3e/label
msgid "It is intermediate data that is easily reproduced"
msgstr "這是容易重新產生的中間資料"

#: answer/f040fdff-e9d4-4777-a482-af584fd7b3ba/label
msgid "There is no value, nobody will ever reuse it"
msgstr "沒有價值，永遠不會有人再次使用"

#: answer/f040fdff-e9d4-4777-a482-af584fd7b3ba/advice
msgid ""
"Are you sure? \n"
"\n"
"There may be very different reasons to reuse a data set than you can think of! E.g. an interview recording can be used for voice analysis or for studying the acoustics of a room, which is not what the interviewer had in mind when it was made."
msgstr ""
"您確定嗎？\n"
"\n"
"再次使用資料集的原因可能遠超您的想像！例如：訪談錄音可以用於語音分析或研究室內聲學，這並非訪談者在錄音時所預想的用途。"

#: answer/c0b6d52a-2fde-4e3f-835f-e49fffc67ccb/label
msgid "It is too expensive"
msgstr "成本太高"

#: answer/f9bd9b58-c400-4a0f-b66f-0ce991e0e3e2/label
msgid "It was lost"
msgstr "已遺失"

#: answer/9af201fa-bf32-4e44-b44d-efea6f69d631/label
msgid "There are other reasons"
msgstr "還有其他原因"

#: question/c3f2eeb9-a9e7-46e7-a5df-8d9ca50ed8ce/title
msgid "What other reasons?"
msgstr "還有哪些其他原因？"

#: question/81d3095e-a530-40a4-878e-ced42fabc4cd/title
msgid "Specify where you will distribute this data from"
msgstr "請指定此資料集將透過哪些位置提供取用"

#: question/81d3095e-a530-40a4-878e-ced42fabc4cd/text
msgid "Add each of the locations where this data set will be made available. Give each of these a short name that identifies it to yourself."
msgstr "請新增此資料集將可被取用的每個位置，並為每個位置設定一個便於您辨識的簡短名稱。"

#: question/80a682bd-8a5c-4a52-935d-680509838a4e/title
msgid "What repository will this data be stored in?"
msgstr "這份資料會儲存在哪一個資料儲存庫？"

#: question/80a682bd-8a5c-4a52-935d-680509838a4e/text
msgid ""
"Domain repositories often have the best functionality to make the data findable and reusable: even though it may look like a database that could be reused in a completely different field would be better findable in a generic repository, the limited availability of domain-specific metadata make that less valuable.\n"
"\n"
"Many repositories are listed in [FAIRsharing](https://fairsharing.org/)\n"
"\n"
"If a repository offers to give your data set a DOI or alternative persistent identifier it is a good idea to use that option."
msgstr ""

#: answer/1dc412c6-da92-4cc2-8639-316c0c6ec5ff/label
msgid "A domain-specific repository"
msgstr "特定領域的資料儲存庫"

#: question/221c322e-dff5-438f-8a2e-90e762681156/title
#: question/371362c3-c2d1-419e-a7d6-b891a976a1fd/title
msgid "What repository?"
msgstr "哪一個資料儲存庫？"

#: question/221c322e-dff5-438f-8a2e-90e762681156/text
#: question/371362c3-c2d1-419e-a7d6-b891a976a1fd/text
#: question/a41a57ef-ac45-4f82-96ec-bdb39f54d401/text
msgid "You will be presented with suggestions from [FAIRSharing](https://fairsharing.org/), but you also have the option to manually enter the repository name that is not listed there."
msgstr "系統會顯示來自 [FAIRSharing](https://fairsharing.org/) 的建議項目，但您也可以手動輸入未列於其中的資料儲存庫名稱。"

#: question/b1492627-9cb6-465a-945a-a2a7ff9a8189/title
msgid "Will you contact the repository beforehand?"
msgstr "您是否會事先聯繫該資料儲存庫？"

#: question/b1492627-9cb6-465a-945a-a2a7ff9a8189/text
msgid "Contacting the repository early may be useful to establish conditions, formats, and metadata requirements for submission. It may also be necessary to establish whether the repository can accommodate your data"
msgstr "在研究初期儘早與資料儲存庫聯繫，可能有助於確立提交的條件、格式和後設資料要求。此外，這也有助於確認該資料儲存庫是否能收存您的資料"

#: answer/c86c80b4-72b3-4194-956a-27e40d3c23eb/label
msgid "No, this submission is routine both for us and the repository"
msgstr "否，這項提交對我們以及該資料儲存庫來說都是例行作業"

#: answer/e09562c0-346c-4c95-b470-c5810aab18fa/label
msgid "Yes, we have contacted the repository"
msgstr "是，我們已聯繫該資料儲存庫"

#: answer/93c590a5-60a6-481d-9482-9145435143a2/label
msgid "Yes, we will contact the repository"
msgstr "是，我們會聯繫該資料儲存庫"

#: answer/d3886c3e-6cf7-4b3e-8bc7-307b47719871/label
msgid "A general-purpose repository (e.g., Zenodo)"
msgstr "通用型資料儲存庫，例如 Zenodo"

#: answer/fb96d008-f31a-4a1a-b203-b3f9bb32fcc8/label
msgid "Our national repository"
msgstr "我們的國家資料儲存庫"

#: answer/fb96d008-f31a-4a1a-b203-b3f9bb32fcc8/advice
#: answer/df0b2ee3-8e4d-42a1-9bb2-c69228074406/advice
msgid "Disadvantage of a general purpose repository is the lack of data-specific features (e.g. 'play' instead of 'download' for an audio file) and limited findability"
msgstr "通用型資料儲存庫的缺點在於缺乏特定資料類型所需的功能（例如，音訊檔只能「下載」，不能直接「播放」），而且資料較不容易被找到"

#: answer/df0b2ee3-8e4d-42a1-9bb2-c69228074406/label
msgid "Our institutional repository"
msgstr "我們的機構資料儲存庫"

#: answer/afd9f4d5-20e0-4fa0-a42a-376c132ff5b0/label
msgid "A special-purpose repository for the project"
msgstr "此計畫專用的資料儲存庫"

#: question/f83a9afd-c6de-452b-be9f-bd76e5eb6b54/title
msgid "Will you be able to support this repository for a sufficiently long time?"
msgstr "您是否能夠長期支援這個資料儲存庫？"

#: question/f83a9afd-c6de-452b-be9f-bd76e5eb6b54/text
msgid "Maintaining a repository is a long term commitment that can most of the time not be funded from project money. Think about who will be doing the system maintenance, hardware maintenance, and who will make necessary code changes to accommodate future (safe) versions of the system"
msgstr "維護資料儲存庫是一項長期承諾，通常無法由計畫經費支應。請思考誰會負責系統維護、硬體設備維護，以及誰會進行必要的程式碼修改，以支援系統未來的安全版本"

#: answer/dc921fac-cf77-4d3d-bb9c-907d37f838ef/advice
msgid "Oops! That would mean that it is possible that the data will no longer be available for re-use after a while? Consider alternative options for publishing the data set."
msgstr "糟了！那將表示這些資料過一段時間後，可能就無法再被取得以供再次使用。請考慮其他可發布該資料集的方式。"

#: question/cbbfb0da-caf1-4c04-b72f-de39c4a8fb33/title
msgid "What is the service level you will be offering to users of the data/repository?"
msgstr "您將為資料或資料儲存庫的使用者提供哪一種服務層級？"

#: question/cbbfb0da-caf1-4c04-b72f-de39c4a8fb33/text
msgid "The amount of funding needed to maintain a repository is strongly dependent on the services offered"
msgstr "維運資料儲存庫所需的經費額度，很大程度上取決於該資料儲存庫提供的服務內容"

#: answer/dc1082fd-1c90-492c-833c-3e0909c643bb/label
msgid "Download only"
msgstr "僅提供下載"

#: answer/dc1082fd-1c90-492c-833c-3e0909c643bb/advice
msgid "That functionality level can surely be found in another place too!"
msgstr "若僅提供下載功能，對使用者而言，其他地方通常也能提供類似的服務！"

#: answer/da6725a2-62bb-4fe7-a76f-a4e396646b19/label
msgid "A search and simple access interface"
msgstr "搜尋與簡易取用介面"

#: answer/d65ddfda-9b08-4ab6-90e5-07df748d7929/label
msgid "An advanced processing service"
msgstr "進階處理服務"

#: answer/d65ddfda-9b08-4ab6-90e5-07df748d7929/advice
msgid "Make sure to budget sufficient compute resources for the users"
msgstr "請確保為使用者編列足夠的運算資源"

#: question/f691ad73-1284-4c7d-999d-34bb0612dd42/title
msgid "Did you arrange for system administration (at least security updates) and hardware maintenance for the server(s)?"
msgstr "您是否有安排伺服器的系統管理作業（至少包含資安更新）及硬體設備維護？"

#: answer/4dd69e44-097b-42fc-98a4-4ce379453d46/advice
msgid "You really need to arrange this."
msgstr "您真的需要安排這件事。"

#: reference/2e0ed21b-2180-4497-8c41-fd2609904400/label
msgid "FAIRSharing"
msgstr "FAIRSharing"

#: reference/e83b0c27-e218-447b-bc0d-7041521e01a1/label
msgid "Registry of Research data Repositories"
msgstr "研究資料儲存庫的登錄冊"

#: reference/b07291f6-fc6d-4e05-8d72-0a41ea5fa6ba/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on depositing to a generic repository like Zenodo"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的「將資料寄存於 Zenodo 等通用型儲存庫」頁面"

#: question/82fc0a41-8be0-407c-b2f8-95bf5b366187/title
msgid "Who will the data in this place be shared with?"
msgstr "此處的資料會與誰共享？"

#: answer/1fd3e838-f92a-4086-8308-de17f6fa9d73/label
msgid "Open: The data will be shared with anyone, as long as they obey conditions of the licence"
msgstr ""

#: answer/985366e7-7504-4f67-a8ee-90c340ff977a/label
msgid "Shared: The data will be shared with a predefined list of people, e.g. coworkers"
msgstr "共享：資料將與預先指定的人員名單共享，例如同事"

#: answer/a8adc972-a2b6-4f5b-837b-20f83a685ed6/label
msgid "Closed: This is an archive, it is not meant to share the data with anyone"
msgstr "封閉：這是一個典藏庫，並非用來與他人共享資料"

#: answer/a8adc972-a2b6-4f5b-837b-20f83a685ed6/advice
msgid "Note that there are questions later specific to archival."
msgstr "請注意，後面還有一些專門針對典藏的問題。"

#: question/3d89e23d-ff5c-45da-97a8-169ad8c39be6/title
msgid "Licences under which this distribution of the data set will be available"
msgstr ""

#: question/3d89e23d-ff5c-45da-97a8-169ad8c39be6/text
msgid "Please add each license that this data set will be available as. For each license you will be able to specify when it starts being applicable, so that you can e.g. specify that the data is restricted for a few months and open afterwards."
msgstr "請加入此資料集可適用的每一種授權條款。您可以為每一種授權條款指定開始適用的時間，例如指定資料先限制取用數個月，之後再開放。"

#: question/ca0f9465-3116-4824-8651-b592151c5368/title
msgid "Under what licence will the data set be made available?"
msgstr ""

#: answer/d27a6e0f-55ea-4b25-bfb9-dcb4d6346fe0/label
msgid "They will be freely available for any use (public domain or CC0)"
msgstr "這些資料可供任何用途自由使用，例如公眾領域或 CC0"

#: answer/9186e183-e328-41f9-b012-149d0bbad9ea/label
msgid "They will be freely available with obligation to quote the source (e.g. CC-BY)"
msgstr "這些資料可自由使用，但必須標明來源，例如 CC-BY"

#: answer/734d5f4e-91c0-4019-8164-8c70c2e0c8f2/label
msgid "They will be available under some restrictions"
msgstr "這些資料會在某些限制下提供"

#: question/30426255-b153-4f3e-bf20-f13573160a64/text
msgid "Please summarise the restrictions. Note that it is a good idea to publish the final conditions for use of the data openly, so that interested researchers can know beforehand whether they will be able to get access to the data before actually placing a request."
msgstr "請總結這些限制。請注意，公開發布資料最終的使用條件是個好主意，如此一來，有興趣的研究人員在正式提出申請之前，便能事先了解自己是否能獲准取用該資料。"

#: question/375792f1-d7c3-4c8d-bf9e-f15ffa38e2fb/title
msgid "Link to the licence text"
msgstr ""

#: question/375792f1-d7c3-4c8d-bf9e-f15ffa38e2fb/text
msgid "If the license is available as a text on the internet, please specify its URL here."
msgstr "如果該授權條款的內文可於網路上取得，請在此填寫其網址。"

#: question/f78fb7e9-2f26-493c-a19b-04e153c17274/title
msgid "How will re-users be able to get access?"
msgstr "日後想再次使用資料的人會如何取用資料？"

#: question/f78fb7e9-2f26-493c-a19b-04e153c17274/text
msgid "Consider that users of a data set will need to be able to get access several years after the project is finished. The best way to arrange this is to put the responsibility for checking the rights to access the data with a fixed body in an organisation, a data access committee, rather than one of the investigators of the project."
msgstr "請考量資料集的使用者可能需要在計畫結束數年後仍能取用資料。為了妥善安排這一點，最好的做法是將資料取用權限的審核責任，交由組織內的固定單位（例如資料取用委員會）負責，而非由計畫中的研究人員負責。"

#: answer/15e7beff-1d71-4515-9517-26e222e672e5/label
msgid "By request to the contact person"
msgstr "向聯絡人提出請求"

#: answer/15e7beff-1d71-4515-9517-26e222e672e5/advice
msgid "Consider what will happen if the contact person moves jobs."
msgstr "請考慮若該聯絡人換工作，後續將如何處理。"

#: answer/f68a6141-3f78-4efb-8a80-2a482e75a862/label
msgid "Through a Data Access Committee"
msgstr "透過資料取用委員會"

#: answer/e856687f-772c-462a-b0e1-071ffffaab8e/label
msgid "Through another process"
msgstr "透過另一個程序"

#: question/8a7e4cc0-8806-4c7a-a662-66e38376769c/title
msgid "What process?"
msgstr "什麼程序？"

#: question/a572c436-5d57-4385-ac9a-d6f117881444/title
msgid "Will the conditions be published as part of open metadata?"
msgstr "這些條件是否會作為開放後設資料的一部分發布？"

#: question/28d494ef-26c0-4632-956e-5cafcc498a32/title
msgid "Starting date"
msgstr "開始日期"

#: question/28d494ef-26c0-4632-956e-5cafcc498a32/text
msgid "From which date will data be available under this license?"
msgstr "資料將自何日期起依本授權條款提供？"

#: reference/f4b4c1a4-95df-4803-a601-2ac1843d0658/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on licensing"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的授權條款頁面"

#: question/d21fdb06-22bf-418e-aa40-dc5ef1485f56/title
msgid "Will this data be assigned a persistent identifier?"
msgstr "這份資料是否會被編配持續識別碼？"

#: question/d21fdb06-22bf-418e-aa40-dc5ef1485f56/text
msgid ""
"Datasets can be assigned persistent identifiers. Just like journal articles get assigned DOIs, these are often also used for data sets. Note that the DOI of a paper is not a persistent identifier for its supplementary information.\n"
"\n"
"Many repositories make sure that your data get a persistent and resolvable identifiers. In other cases, you should take care of this yourself."
msgstr ""
"資料集可被編配持續識別碼。就如同期刊論文會被編配 DOI 一樣，DOI 也常被用於資料集。請注意，論文的 DOI 並不等同於其補充資料的持續識別碼。\n"
"\n"
"許多資料儲存庫可以確保您的資料具有可解析且持續的識別碼。在其他情況下，則需要由您自行處理。"

#: question/c928d464-4ae7-447c-82f6-bc525d2596a9/title
msgid "Who assigns the persistent identifier?"
msgstr "誰會編配持續識別碼？"

#: answer/50eb4b5d-2455-48aa-b1f1-b4abca495e4d/label
msgid "A project data steward or principle investigator"
msgstr "計畫資料託管員或計畫主持人"

#: answer/290d7b18-f851-41eb-8024-e23bba79592e/label
msgid "An institutional data steward"
msgstr "機構資料託管員"

#: answer/a31e0fc2-4bde-4482-8747-d250042a1589/label
msgid "The repository"
msgstr "儲存庫"

#: question/7f55274c-a5f5-4f6a-94d8-531ea0077462/title
msgid "Will the repository make sure the persistent identifier can be resolved to a digital object?"
msgstr "儲存庫是否能確保持續識別碼可解析到某個數位物件？"

#: question/7f55274c-a5f5-4f6a-94d8-531ea0077462/text
msgid "Often a persistent identifier will be put as the last part of a URL to *resolve* it to either a page with metadata or directly to the data itself."
msgstr "持續識別碼通常會被放在網址的最後一部分，以便將其解析到一個包含後設資料的頁面，或直接解析到資料本身。"

#: question/46039bea-87e6-4c61-8567-4e819404b4d0/title
msgid "Will you be adding a reference to the published data to at least one data catalogue?"
msgstr "您是否會在至少一個資料目錄中加入指向已發布資料的參照？"

#: question/46039bea-87e6-4c61-8567-4e819404b4d0/text
msgid ""
"Data is sometimes difficult to locate, especially if it is not in a domain-specific repository. Data catalogues may increase findability: they put the metadata for data sets that are located in different places together in one location that is well known to researchers in a particular field. \n"
"\n"
"Data sets can be mentioned in multiple data catalogues without the need for duplicating the data: the data catalogues point to where the actual data can be found.\n"
"\n"
"An example is [Narcis](https://dans.knaw.nl/nl/over/diensten/narcis) (for research data in the Netherlands)."
msgstr ""
"資料有時不容易找到，尤其是沒有存放在特定領域的資料儲存庫時。資料目錄有助於讓資料更容易被找到：它會將分散在不同位置的資料集後設資料彙整到同一個平台，而這個平台通常是該領域研究人員熟悉的地方。\n"
"\n"
"資料集可以同時被收錄於多個資料目錄，無需重複儲存資料本身：資料目錄可提供指引，連結至實際存放資料的位置。\n"
"\n"
"一個例子是 [Narcis](https://dans.knaw.nl/nl/over/diensten/narcis)（荷蘭的研究資料目錄）。"

#: answer/aaae5c5b-0aa9-4619-bb68-de0cd27f14da/label
msgid "No, the data will be stored in a repository that is the prime source of data for re-use in the field"
msgstr "否，資料會儲存在該領域供資料再次使用的主要資料儲存庫中"

#: reference/b128903f-a545-4323-b127-f4a0ff998608/label
msgid "What is a data catalogue (Dataversity)"
msgstr ""

#: question/f99b1723-c8e4-44b9-af22-f66955eda1e2/title
msgid "Will there be different versions of this data over time?"
msgstr "這些資料是否會隨時間產生不同版本？"

#: question/05655914-e1f4-4578-a7d4-bae17579fce8/title
msgid "How will the versions be recognised?"
msgstr "如何辨識不同版本？"

#: choice/74158bea-966b-4c53-ba0d-1c9c47536f57/label
msgid "They will be dated"
msgstr "會加上日期"

#: choice/b509d5d3-81e1-450a-86ab-cec423091181/label
msgid "They will be clearly numbered"
msgstr "會有清楚編號"

#: question/1302cb21-6a98-490e-b64d-acf4744a8b1a/title
msgid "Will a user of this data need specific software to be able to use it?"
msgstr "資料使用者是否需要特定軟體才能使用此資料？"

#: question/1302cb21-6a98-490e-b64d-acf4744a8b1a/text
msgid "Some data types may be closely coupled to specific software packages. If that is the case for this data set, please name and point out the required software."
msgstr "某些資料類型可能與特定軟體套件密切綁定。若此資料集屬於這種情況，請列出所需軟體，並說明可從何處取得。"

#: question/14f7a766-c28e-400e-8426-53f7b4e5b90b/title
msgid "Why isn’t specialised software required?"
msgstr ""

#: question/b8543a67-2a6b-4f45-a0b0-d245227f9818/title
msgid "What software is needed to use the data?"
msgstr "需要哪一種軟體才能使用此資料？"

#: question/f29e2dbd-8edc-4ac3-92ba-96a6d507789b/title
msgid "PID for the software, or URL where the software can be found"
msgstr "該軟體的 PID，或可找到該軟體的網址"

#: question/1cb559e7-2e6f-44fe-9bd1-9a354ba7fbdf/title
msgid "Will documentation for this software be included in the metadata?"
msgstr "此軟體的文件是否會納入後設資料？"

#: question/58307a1d-f840-4fe1-be8a-87758bb98d42/title
msgid "Will this software (e.g. in open source code) be included?"
msgstr "是否會一併提供此軟體（例如以開放原始碼形式提供）？"

#: question/5f5cc5b6-a17c-4cf5-b6fc-ecfd655c0fe6/title
msgid "When will the data set be published?"
msgstr "此資料集何時會發布？"

#: answer/58468158-3e03-4f3d-a262-6fffb05bf08f/label
msgid "As soon as possible after collecting it"
msgstr "資料蒐集完成後儘快"

#: answer/428ccd38-fb39-4e18-9d5c-92d80ba019ee/label
msgid "After initial cleanup"
msgstr "初步清理完成後"

#: answer/45a2acbe-0ebc-40f7-b2e4-c7c87af6faa8/label
msgid "After all our processing has finished"
msgstr "所有處理完成後"

#: answer/d157e15a-f5c6-46c5-be4f-a260c4ba7954/label
msgid "When the project is wrapped up"
msgstr "計畫收尾時"

#: answer/be4cefce-2f81-42ad-a83c-330b4b3bb7b3/label
msgid "The data will be published after an embargo"
msgstr "延後開放期限結束後"

#: reference/bc4bc2de-eb60-4f7d-bec9-6c8207a43a3d/label
msgid "RDMkit on Data Sharing"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料共享頁面"

#: question/f876a937-c295-4a12-9dfb-6ffc7395c8db/title
msgid "Are there qualified references to other data sets?"
msgstr "是否有指向其他資料集、且明確說明關係的參照？"

#: question/f876a937-c295-4a12-9dfb-6ffc7395c8db/text
msgid "A qualified reference is a cross-reference that explains its intent. For example, X is regulator of Y is a much more qualified reference than X is associated with Y, or X see also Y. The goal therefore is to create as many meaningful links as possible between (meta)data resources to enrich the contextual knowledge about the data."
msgstr "「具明確關係說明的參照」是指能說明其意圖的交叉參照。舉例來說，「X 是 Y 的調節因子」比「X 與 Y 相關」或「X 另見 Y」更能清楚說明參照的意義。因此，目標是在（後設）資料資源之間盡可能建立有意義的連結，以豐富資料的脈絡知識。"

#: question/7828d3a0-29bf-450e-aee9-473457a225fd/title
msgid "Which qualified references to other data sets will be included?"
msgstr ""

#: question/7828d3a0-29bf-450e-aee9-473457a225fd/text
msgid "Please list any references to other data sets, e.g. from your project or from earlier research. "
msgstr "請列出任何指向其他資料集的參照，例如指向本計畫中的其他資料集，或先前研究資料集的參照。 "

#: question/abb6ac92-6508-4a24-b262-5d64db4ae731/title
msgid "Identifier of the data set that will be referred to"
msgstr "被參照資料集的識別碼"

#: question/c70e49f9-09e4-456a-814b-bbaa8fde887c/title
msgid "The relationship between this dataset and the referred data set"
msgstr "此資料集與所參照資料集之間的關係"

#: reference/c57507b2-9581-465d-ba9a-7dcd8cfab8c0/label
msgid "FAIR principle \"I3\""
msgstr "FAIR 原則 I3 頁面"

#: reference/92c92ca3-f15d-4460-8c63-461f1e801196/label
#: reference/e20ad7f1-602e-4e9c-be05-e69914501c91/label
msgid "RDMkit on Data Preservation"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料保存頁面"

#: question/d4e6a244-07fb-4573-b93f-c20a9409ac7c/title
msgid "How long will this data set be kept?"
msgstr "此資料集會保存多久？"

#: question/d4e6a244-07fb-4573-b93f-c20a9409ac7c/text
msgid "For optimum reusability data needs to be available for as long as possible. There may be financial reasons why you can't keep the data any longer; there may be legal, contractual or regulatory reasons requiring you to delete the data."
msgstr "為達到最佳可再次使用性，資料需要盡可能長期保持可被取用。不過，您可能因財務因素而無法繼續保存資料；也可能因法律、契約或法規要求而必須刪除資料。"

#: answer/59305ef2-2dd0-4553-8d7b-29186e0b8cd5/label
msgid "As long as technically possible"
msgstr "在技術上可行的範圍內盡可能長期保存"

#: answer/bb6b4f0a-9908-4473-9982-30084ff4f6ab/label
msgid "Until it needs to be deleted for legal, contractual or regulatory reasons"
msgstr "直到因法律、契約或法規原因而需要刪除為止"

#: answer/7b5f059a-ae7e-4f7f-92e8-119911e568b2/label
msgid "For a fixed period (prepaid)"
msgstr "保存一段已預付費用的固定期間"

#: question/346118ee-265f-4104-8409-161ea9a57f75/title
msgid "How long will the data be kept?"
msgstr "資料會被保留多久？"

#: question/346118ee-265f-4104-8409-161ea9a57f75/text
msgid "Specify the period, and optionally add how this relates to the minimum period that you are required to keep the data and/or a reason for choosing this period."
msgstr "請指定期間，並可選擇補充此期間與您必須保留資料的最低期限之間的關係，或說明選擇此期間的理由。"

#: reference/f733a466-0a9f-44ce-a3e9-69573246be41/label
msgid "RDMkit on Storage"
msgstr "RDMkit 的儲存頁面"

#: question/3b3fbcc6-c405-4151-8dce-e11dbd46b1bd/title
msgid "Will the metadata be available even when the data no longer exists?"
msgstr "即使資料不再存在，後設資料是否仍可取得？"

#: question/3b3fbcc6-c405-4151-8dce-e11dbd46b1bd/text
msgid "This is a one of the FAIR principles."
msgstr "這是 FAIR 原則之一。"

#: reference/a82f95f5-9f70-472a-acfb-613177cd8429/label
msgid "RDMkit on Documentation and Metadata"
msgstr "RDMkit 的文件與後設資料頁面"

#: question/a1d76760-053c-4706-80a2-cfb6c6a061f3/title
msgid "Does this dataset contain personal data?"
msgstr "此資料集是否包含個人資料？"

#: question/a1d76760-053c-4706-80a2-cfb6c6a061f3/text
msgid ""
"Is there anything in this dataset that could be tied to a person? This could be a physical characteristic, but also behavior of a person, movements, communications. Note that e.g. readouts about the performance of an airplane are considered to contain personal data of the pilot!\n"
"\n"
"The GDPR states that the processing (including storing) of personal data should stop when the intended purpose of the processing is done. There are, however, exemptions to this e.g. when the processing is done for research purposes. Also, from a research ethics point of view, research data should be kept to make it possible for others to validate published research findings and reuse data for new discoveries. This is also governed by what the data subjects have been informed about regarding how you will treat the data after project completion. The recommendation is to deposit the sensitive data in the appropriate controlled access repositories if such are available, but this requires that the data subjects are informed and have agreed to this."
msgstr ""
"此資料集中是否有任何內容可能連結至特定個人？這可能是生理特徵，也可能是個人的行為、行蹤或通訊。請注意，例如飛機性能讀數也會被視為包含飛行員的個人資料。\n"
"\n"
"歐盟《個人資料保護規則》 (GDPR) 規定，當個人資料處理（包括儲存）的預定目的已完成時，應停止處理。不過，也有例外情況，例如為研究目的而進行的處理。此外，從研究倫理角度來看，研究資料也應保存下來，使他人能驗證已發表的研究成果，並再次使用資料以促成新的發現。這也取決於資料主體曾被告知計畫結束後將如何處理資料。建議做法是，若有合適的受管控取用資料儲存庫可用，應將敏感資料寄存於其中；但前提是已告知資料主體，並取得其同意。"

#: question/cc95b399-7d8d-4232-bccf-686f78c91bff/title
msgid "Does this dataset contain sensitive information?"
msgstr "此資料集是否有敏感資訊？"

#: question/cc95b399-7d8d-4232-bccf-686f78c91bff/text
msgid "Personal information can be sensitive if it is for instance about the health, sexual orientation, religion of a person. But there are also other classes of sensitive information: e.g. locations of rare species in biodiversity could be sensitive and should not leak to poachers."
msgstr "個人資料若涉及健康、性傾向或宗教等內容，就可能是敏感資訊。但敏感資訊也有其他類別，例如生物多樣性中稀有物種的位置可能是敏感資訊，不應外洩給盜獵者。"

#: reference/d01dcf36-54ad-432d-9751-98abd2dbc2ab/label
msgid "RDMkit on Collecting Data"
msgstr "RDMkit 的資料蒐集頁面"

#: question/d5784d24-0e66-4821-bd62-a711fb6d7a40/title
msgid "Will you be archiving data (using so-called 'cold storage') for long term preservation already during your project?"
msgstr "您是否會在計畫進行期間，即將資料封存至所謂的「冷儲存 (cold storage)」中，以進行長期保存？"

#: question/d5784d24-0e66-4821-bd62-a711fb6d7a40/text
msgid "Much of the raw data you have will need to be archived for your own later use somewhere. This is often done off-line on tape, not on the disks of the compute facility. Please note that this does not refer to the data publication."
msgstr "您所擁有的大部分原始資料，之後都需要在某處加以典藏，以供您日後自行使用。這通常是在離線環境下以磁帶進行，而不是存放在運算設施的磁碟上。請注意，這裡指的並不是資料發布。"

#: question/b16e76a9-34a8-4ba5-9420-b58bebaeac8d/title
#: resourcePage/5395ebb2-21d5-4e11-b1dd-76a117f2a419/title
msgid "Can the original data be regenerated?"
msgstr "原始資料是否可以重新產生？"

#: question/7f8ff791-8593-4e00-93f9-e31c5dff5ffb/title
msgid "When is the raw data archived?"
msgstr "原始資料何時典藏？"

#: answer/fbe7ef0d-3199-47de-ad28-1b9299200156/label
msgid "As soon as it comes in, in chunks"
msgstr "資料一進來就分批典藏"

#: answer/92dc2ba0-2cac-4710-8dc7-c1cf6e573235/label
msgid "As soon as it has all arrived, in one session"
msgstr "資料全部到齊後，一次典藏"

#: answer/c861d005-a681-4a3a-a54b-7a229b6662ee/label
msgid "All at once with the results at the end of the project"
msgstr "計畫結束時，連同結果一起典藏"

#: reference/3575556d-82dd-43bd-b9f1-5f1f28dbee86/description
msgid "Archiving raw data from the working area"
msgstr "將工作區域中的原始資料進行典藏"

#: question/c659c36f-d142-4453-8d8b-db7c05f31371/title
msgid "Is the archived data changing over time, needing re-archival?"
msgstr "已典藏的資料是否會隨時間發生變化，而需要重新典藏？"

#: question/1147485f-b9a9-486c-8341-27e05718c508/title
msgid "Do you need frequent backups?"
msgstr "您是否需要頻繁備份？"

#: question/1147485f-b9a9-486c-8341-27e05718c508/text
msgid "The general term 'backup' is used for protection against two different kinds of problems: equipment failure and human error. Protections against these two may need different solutions. Both are considered backup for this and subsequent questions."
msgstr "「備份」這個一般用語可指防範兩種不同問題：設備故障與人為錯誤。針對這兩者的防護可能需要不同解決方案。在本題與後續問題中，兩者都視為備份。"

#: answer/e2ad7b2b-cc9a-445b-8a94-c41032a7e787/label
msgid "No, data changes infrequently"
msgstr "否，資料很少變動"

#: answer/67d52405-a902-4661-8158-91ab1d268832/label
msgid "Yes, data changes frequently"
msgstr "是，資料經常變動"

#: reference/aa54555f-b312-41a5-9c24-609b2d7d9346/label
msgid "DMEG on Backups"
msgstr "DMEG 的備份頁面"

#: question/f6476ea3-1ec5-447b-a776-4f0bfca38f8f/title
msgid "Will you be relying on these backups to recover from human error (accidental changes or deletions)?"
msgstr "您是否會依賴這些備份，從人為錯誤（意外變更或刪除）中復原？"

#: answer/899b6dc9-59fa-4246-b152-915d4864f771/advice
msgid "This puts other demands on the possibility to restore files. Make sure this is covered"
msgstr "這會對檔案還原能力提出其他要求。請確保已涵蓋這一點"

#: question/c2a38110-f7a3-432f-ae98-4e448e496b44/title
msgid "Will the archive be stored on disk or on tape?"
msgstr "典藏資料會儲存在磁碟還是磁帶上？"

#: answer/18f50141-094d-426b-8a75-4c4fce59389b/label
msgid "Disk"
msgstr "硬碟"

#: answer/ebbe4ef1-ec2a-44b8-bbc9-f15a743c438f/label
msgid "Tape"
msgstr "磁帶"

#: question/41a8d19b-2468-4c60-9f5e-7a8fee26eedb/title
msgid "Will the archive be stored in a remote location, protecting the data against disasters?"
msgstr "典藏資料是否會儲存在遠端位置，以保護資料免受災害影響？"

#: question/ed3d43ad-d2b5-4194-8b05-08c95da0a7f2/title
msgid "Will the archive need to be protected against loss or theft?"
msgstr "典藏資料是否需要防範遺失或竊取？"

#: question/2c797727-559d-4bcf-a4a1-713accfcd602/title
msgid "Will the archive be encrypted?"
msgstr "典藏資料是否會加密？"

#: answer/ad3ab129-dab0-421c-9840-e35b53931768/label
msgid "No, the data does not need protection"
msgstr "不，該資料無須保護"

#: question/905d4cda-afa1-4cc0-8df6-3d989c7b8b2e/title
msgid "Is it clear who has access to the key? Also in case of a required data restore?"
msgstr "是否清楚誰可以取用金鑰？需要還原資料時也一樣嗎？"

#: reference/decf61b1-7afa-447d-aeae-0b8e55d87abd/description
msgid "Access rights to the archive"
msgstr "典藏庫取用權限"

#: question/7458c3bc-60aa-44ba-8d59-a0672dc8de63/title
msgid "Is it clear who has physical access to the archives?"
msgstr "是否清楚誰可以實體存取典藏資料？"

#: question/87abded2-1edb-4f69-bd6c-8b90f7706206/title
msgid "Will your project require the archives to be available on-line?"
msgstr "您的計畫是否要求典藏資料可線上取用？"

#: question/b3caa015-cdd5-4812-84b5-596855a30545/title
msgid "Will data integrity be guaranteed?"
msgstr "是否會保障資料完整性？"

#: question/b3caa015-cdd5-4812-84b5-596855a30545/text
msgid "If the 'master copy' of the data is available on line, it should probably be protected against being tampered with."
msgstr "如果資料的「主要副本」可在線上取用，通常應加以保護，以避免遭人竄改。"

#: question/86459c42-89ee-4874-bb54-fec0881332e0/title
msgid "Is there an interface and a defined process for people to request access to the data?"
msgstr "是否有介面與明確流程，讓人們申請取用資料？"

#: question/b7d9008e-9691-44f0-a026-0f63d808db39/title
msgid "Has it been established who has access to the archive, and how fast?"
msgstr "是否已確定誰可以取用典藏庫，以及多快可以取用？"

#: question/47559455-2969-41f4-aee8-e9ce558ab2f0/title
msgid "Has it been established who can ask for a restore during the project?"
msgstr "是否已確定計畫期間誰可以申請資料還原？"

#: question/3d837696-3a99-4362-86a3-f460dd878b75/title
msgid "If the data is voluminous, will the project be able to cope with the time needed for a restore?"
msgstr "如果資料量龐大，該計畫是否能夠因應資料還原所需的時間？"

#: question/feb954c1-c38e-4615-addd-4c714a06809a/title
msgid "Has authority over the data been arranged for when the project is finished (potentially long after)?"
msgstr "是否已安排計畫結束後（可能是很久以後）資料管理的權責歸屬？"

#: reference/b0430030-df3e-4d67-897f-335fa6185858/description
msgid "Archive encryption"
msgstr "典藏庫加密"

#: question/2dd94cbc-42f3-4077-b6da-83e0275290c5/title
msgid "Has it been established how long the archived data need to be kept? For each of the different parts of the archive (raw data / results)?"
msgstr "是否已確定典藏資料需要保存多久？是否針對典藏資料的不同部分（如原始資料／研究結果）分別訂定保存期限？"

#: question/e23201aa-df56-4ade-9406-baa1fb6b1c0c/title
msgid "Will the data still be understandable and reusable after a long time?"
msgstr "經過長時間後，資料是否仍可理解並可再次使用？"

#: question/e23201aa-df56-4ade-9406-baa1fb6b1c0c/text
msgid "See also all questions about keeping metadata and data formats. Make sure the metadata is kept close to the data in the archive, and that community supported data formats are used for all long term archiving."
msgstr "另請參閱所有關於保存後設資料與資料格式的問題。請確保在典藏庫中，後設資料與資料一同妥善保存，且所有長期典藏皆使用社群所支持的資料格式。"

#: reference/7d1b6960-92db-4074-b908-74132bce1444/description
msgid "Archiving data when the project is finished"
msgstr "當計畫完成後典藏資料"

#: question/f9d84278-b61d-4314-94e9-12644bfa1d00/title
msgid "Will you be archiving your data in 'cold storage' after the project finishes?"
msgstr "計畫結束後，您是否會以「冷儲存」方式典藏資料？"

#: question/f9d84278-b61d-4314-94e9-12644bfa1d00/text
msgid "Will you be storing (in cold storage) copies of your own data for a longer period after the project has ended? Possibly as a continuation of archival as part of data storage strategy during the project? Data archival is distinct from data publishing, an archive is usually strictly limited in who can access the data."
msgstr "計畫結束後，您是否會以「冷儲存」方式長期保存自己的資料副本？這可能是計畫期間資料儲存策略中典藏作業的延續。資料典藏不同於資料發布；典藏庫通常會嚴格限制可取用資料的人員。"

#: question/6467fff1-33ae-47f6-829c-9e3817298d1f/title
msgid "Who will be paying for the long term storage?"
msgstr "誰會支應長期儲存成本？"

#: answer/3aabde57-dabd-456f-b351-1b81a74bb2d5/label
msgid "It will be paid from the grant"
msgstr "由補助經費支應"

#: answer/2171b472-3569-468a-911f-5df375cb244f/label
msgid "It will be paid out of departmental budgets from one or more of the project participants"
msgstr "由一位或多位計畫參與者所屬部門的預算支應"

#: answer/f6dba54d-bb72-4fcf-bebc-f5651adba0c0/label
msgid "This is a service budgeted by one or more of the participating institutes"
msgstr "這是由一個或多個參與機構編列預算支應的服務"

#: question/22f28294-f990-4686-87dd-ecca65a0ed26/title
msgid "What is the minimum lifetime of the archive?"
msgstr "資料典藏的最短保存期限為何？"

#: answer/15f9c764-1aaa-4de1-b65d-b92ae6bd3fb8/label
msgid "5 years"
msgstr "5 年"

#: answer/37672102-6b96-4c69-a24a-ce3b8672ccc1/label
msgid "10 years"
msgstr "10 年"

#: answer/c0c80589-203d-4564-8f00-89d5cd538fae/label
msgid "15 years"
msgstr "15 年"

#: answer/820c78f6-81d0-442f-80c7-bfa3d04b282a/label
msgid "Another period"
msgstr "其他期限"

#: question/075e934b-e9a3-45b6-a91e-5e19a1e56e06/title
msgid "For how many years will the archive minimally be kept?"
msgstr "典藏資料至少會保存多少年？"

#: answer/3116fe33-8baf-4085-a8ba-688e8b062b78/label
msgid "It is arranged in a different way"
msgstr "另有其他安排"

#: question/0b42bbcc-5102-4619-b8e3-9409dbc0379a/title
msgid "How is the archival period arranged?"
msgstr "資料典藏的保存期限如何安排？"

#: question/1a754b08-2a93-4d90-ac52-96f2a69097bf/title
msgid "Can the archival period be extended?"
msgstr "資料典藏的保存期限是否可延長？"

#: question/e5f3081b-df3a-4059-83e2-5c69baa83c49/title
msgid "Why will the archival period not be extended?"
msgstr "為什麼不延長典藏期間？"

#: answer/91a03f0c-3d3d-4bfe-a7eb-46749706e749/label
msgid "The archival period is limited by law or contract"
msgstr "典藏期限受法律或契約限制"

#: answer/cb6a4747-0bf3-447d-8d7d-dc1b7a077be0/label
msgid "The archival period is limited by budget"
msgstr "典藏期限受預算限制"

#: question/5d153cdd-9d37-4e38-b5eb-1b867ed01e32/title
msgid "Who will decide whether the archival period is extended?"
msgstr "由誰決定是否延長典藏期間？"

#: answer/1c805499-e407-489c-81ee-87ac76b6b2b6/label
msgid "One of the principle investigators involved in the project will decide"
msgstr "參與本計畫的其中一位計畫主持人將作出決定"

#: answer/c42196af-a4eb-4026-8a4a-8e46012ac47f/label
msgid "Library or archive staff will decide"
msgstr "將由圖書館或檔案館人員決定"

#: question/b51878eb-fdaf-4e3a-940e-8ecc98059d58/title
msgid "What will the decision whether or not to extend the renewal be based on?"
msgstr "是否延長典藏期限，會依據什麼做決定？"

#: choice/f6d68b58-7996-453f-a033-71272aa01204/label
msgid "It will be based on the actual use of the archived data"
msgstr "這將取決於典藏資料的實際使用情況"

#: choice/b84a59dd-73a3-48f9-9556-04ce3750df73/label
msgid "It will be based on the predicted use of the archived data"
msgstr "這將取決於典藏資料的預期使用情況"

#: choice/4071f707-d2c0-4102-9916-2dcab77c27a8/label
msgid "It will be based on available budget"
msgstr "這將取決於可用的預算"

#: question/553834d6-ff71-4b76-b4b4-b90d19a3f0a4/title
msgid "Will data formats of data in cold storage be upgraded if they become obsolete?"
msgstr "如果「冷儲存」中的資料格式變得過時，是否會更新為較新的格式？"

#: question/5a192c70-d824-49d2-965c-dca90deb04ac/title
msgid "Will data be migrated regularly to more modern storage media (e.g. newer tapes)?"
msgstr "資料是否會定期遷移到較新的儲存媒體（例如較新的磁帶）？"

#: reference/4edaeeb8-0e4d-4ae7-b1c6-2e324bebdfd6/description
msgid "Archival during the project"
msgstr "計畫期間的典藏"

#: question/de23bb94-b727-4907-9a5d-6f8c78c3e432/title
msgid "Will any of the repositories you use charge you for their services?"
msgstr "您使用的資料儲存庫是否會收取服務費？"

#: question/edc9b6d9-c121-4e00-ba83-710330c2e18d/title
msgid "How will you be paying for these services?"
msgstr "您將如何支付這些服務的費用？"

#: answer/f613d751-f6dd-406e-863c-cdce486a5fc0/label
msgid "We have budgeted for these costs in the project"
msgstr "我們已在計畫中為這些成本編列預算"

#: answer/9081d546-59d1-4ffb-987e-02f6ed002e73/label
msgid "These costs will be carried by (one of) the departments involved in the project"
msgstr "這些成本將由參與計畫的一個或多個部門承擔"

#: answer/aeafeb04-59e1-4e56-8c89-07d773474695/label
msgid "These costs will be carried by (one of) the institutes involved in the project"
msgstr "這些成本將由參與計畫的一個或多個機構承擔"

#: answer/6fb69263-d2cb-4d90-babe-523136c29bc4/label
msgid "We will pay for these costs by other means"
msgstr "我們會以其他方式支付這些成本"

#: question/6e0704a2-cea3-4ae7-8ab5-5eb6db163639/title
msgid "How will you pay for these costs?"
msgstr "您會如何支付這些費用？"

#: question/4baf405e-262e-4f1a-bfdc-fe72fc628650/title
msgid "Are there any other recurring fees to keep data or documents available?"
msgstr "是否還有其他為維持資料或文件可取用而定期支付的費用？"

#: question/4baf405e-262e-4f1a-bfdc-fe72fc628650/text
msgid "Are you using any commercially licensed products to keep data, software or documents available, for which a regular fee must be paid?"
msgstr "您是否使用任何需定期付費的商業授權產品，來確保資料、軟體或文件可供取用？"

#: answer/5951120f-af93-4f15-b15a-b2be9a89efff/advice
msgid "Make sure this will be kept running by the department or institute. It is best to also have a backup plan, being able to move data and documents to a different place if a service is discontinued. For this, you may need to arrange permission from all project partners beforehand."
msgstr "請確保此服務將持續由該部門或機構維運。最好也要預先準備備援方案，以便在某項服務停止提供時，仍能將資料與文件移轉至其他地方。為此，您可能需要事先取得所有計畫合作夥伴的同意。"

#: question/13a7eeae-09f5-42bf-8e62-b2c1fe1b86f7/title
msgid "Did you budget for the time and effort it will take to prepare the data for publication?"
msgstr "您是否已預估並編列資料出版前整理與準備所需的時間及人力？"

#: question/2a0cf686-63ed-44b6-ae74-38ddd39ac741/title
msgid "How much have you budgeted for making data or other research outputs FAIR?"
msgstr "您目前編列了多少相關經費使資料或其他研究成果符合 FAIR 原則？"

#: question/2a0cf686-63ed-44b6-ae74-38ddd39ac741/text
msgid "Specify an amount including the relevant"
msgstr "請指定金額，並包含相關項目"

#: question/92a10652-3675-48f2-8d50-180a29cec62e/title
msgid "Will you be making sure that blocks of data deposited in different repositories can be recognised as belonging to the same study?"
msgstr ""

#: answer/0e748d3d-fd83-470f-918a-0321b1fc9f11/label
msgid "Yes, all data sets will have links to the related data"
msgstr "是，所有資料集都會連結到相關資料"

#: answer/18ca5e47-464d-40c5-881b-c15e54bd2bff/label
msgid "Yes, all data sets will be linked from a single catalogue entry"
msgstr ""

#: answer/6445c352-5685-4e23-ac52-ebcabe353bd0/label
msgid "Yes, we have made other arrangements"
msgstr "是，我們已有其他安排"

#: question/588ad032-56ba-4d52-b29c-6a5b56aa6569/title
#: resourcePage/9aed3587-820d-44ff-b635-5ddfc7a48cae/title
msgid "Will reference data be created?"
msgstr "是否會建立參考資料？"

#: question/588ad032-56ba-4d52-b29c-6a5b56aa6569/text
msgid ""
"Will any of the data that you will be creating form a reference data set for future research (by others)?\n"
"\n"
"Much of todays data is used in comparison with reference data. You may be comparing your own data with a \"standard set\" which is maintained as a collection by someone else. Or you could be determining differences to a standard (for example in bioinformatics, a genome is often compared with a reference genome to identify genomic variants). Will you be creating any data that will be reference data for other researchers?"
msgstr ""
"您將建立的任何資料，是否會成為供未來研究（由其他人）使用的參考資料集？\n"
"\n"
"現今許多資料都會與參考資料進行比較。您可能會將自己的資料與他人維護的「標準資料集」進行比較；也可能會判定資料相對於某項標準的差異（例如在生物資訊學中，常會將基因組與參考基因組比較，以辨識基因組變異）。您是否會建立任何可供其他研究人員作為參考資料的資料？"

#: question/9f081091-0810-4f12-be7f-0a22ee928a14/title
msgid "Who will own the reference data? Who will be allowed to use it?"
msgstr "誰將擁有參考資料？誰可以使用它？"

#: question/9f081091-0810-4f12-be7f-0a22ee928a14/text
msgid ""
"It is important to think early about ownership and permissions. Who will have the authority to decide later about the use of the reference data? Will a single person or single organisation be responsible for this?\n"
"\n"
"Please note as well that many kinds of data can not be \"owned\"; you can only have copyrights on specific data collections, and those data base rights are not as universal as creative rights on other works."
msgstr ""
"及早思考所有權與權限問題是很重要的。日後誰將有權決定這些參考資料的使用方式？此事是否將由單一個人或單一組織負責？\n"
"\n"
"另請注意，許多類型的資料其實無法被「擁有」；您只能對特定的資料彙編享有著作權，而這類資料庫權利也不像其他作品上的創作權利那樣具有普遍適用性。"

#: question/27769a31-717b-4204-8468-175ac93b195a/title
#: resourcePage/d8306ea1-549e-4963-a934-7a6500df8fd2/title
msgid "How will you maintain it?"
msgstr "您會如何維護它？"

#: question/27769a31-717b-4204-8468-175ac93b195a/text
msgid "How will maintenance be paid for in the long run? Will you host it yourself or deposit it with a repository? How will you deal with requests for help? And with requests for adding data?"
msgstr "您會如何負擔長期維護的費用？您會自行託管，還是將資料寄存於資料儲存庫？您會如何處理求助請求？另外，若有人提出新增資料的要求，您會如何應對？"

#: question/2679736a-800e-4eaa-a70f-818070540c48/title
msgid "How will the release schedule be?"
msgstr "發布時程會如何安排？"

#: question/2679736a-800e-4eaa-a70f-818070540c48/text
msgid "Will you be updating the reference data at regular intervals?"
msgstr "您是否會定期更新參考資料？"

#: question/13af8c24-3e2d-452c-8e5e-e6ab972a43fd/title
msgid "Will the reference data be made available under a standard licence?"
msgstr ""

#: question/210d40f0-88c9-4982-80da-743ac9d93ee7/title
msgid "What will the conditions for use be?"
msgstr "使用條件會是什麼？"

#: question/210d40f0-88c9-4982-80da-743ac9d93ee7/text
msgid "Please either specify a link to the license that you have made for the data, or summarise the conditions here."
msgstr "請提供您為此資料制定的授權條款連結，或在此摘要說明使用條件。"

#: question/28712f2b-1775-4c81-8d87-4bf0b95c2a64/title
msgid "Which standard licence will you apply?"
msgstr ""

#: question/28712f2b-1775-4c81-8d87-4bf0b95c2a64/text
msgid "You will be presented with suggestions from [Wikidata](https://www.wikidata.org/), but you also have the option to manually enter the licence that is not listed there."
msgstr ""

#: reference/6c277217-8bc7-4768-94e2-be019571c94b/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on Data Licences"
msgstr ""

#: reference/dea35444-c8b4-4282-be9c-72e8092d01ed/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on Licensing"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的授權條款頁面"

#: question/8cd74016-3547-4cc2-8577-2894301e7334/title
msgid "Will the reference data be available from an existing repository?"
msgstr "參考資料是否可從既有資料儲存庫取得？"

#: question/b94df3e7-a32e-4e3b-81fe-93a039409b10/title
msgid "Where will you make it available?"
msgstr "您會在哪裡提供這些資料？"

#: question/b94df3e7-a32e-4e3b-81fe-93a039409b10/text
msgid "Preferably answer with a URL, alternatively explain."
msgstr "最好以網址回答；若無法提供，請另作說明。"

#: question/a41a57ef-ac45-4f82-96ec-bdb39f54d401/title
msgid "Which repository?"
msgstr "哪一個資料儲存庫？"

#: reference/75f0120d-b3a8-4042-8249-dfe2de83a3d5/description
msgid "Reuse of existing reference data"
msgstr "既有參考資料的再次使用"

#: chapter/6be88f7c-f868-460f-bba7-91e1c659adfd/title
msgid "Giving access to data"
msgstr "提供資料取用權限"

#: chapter/6be88f7c-f868-460f-bba7-91e1c659adfd/text
msgid "This chapter deals with the information needed by people who will re-use your data, and with the access conditions they will need to follow."
msgstr "本章說明日後想再次使用您資料的人所需的資訊，以及他們必須遵循的資料取用條件。"

#: question/6516eae1-98b2-48f2-9862-b5fb140cfad7/title
msgid "Will you be working with the philosophy 'as open as possible' for your data?"
msgstr "您是否會依循「盡可能開放 (as open as possible)」的原則來管理您的資料？"

#: question/6516eae1-98b2-48f2-9862-b5fb140cfad7/text
msgid ""
"The FAIR principles do not contain any direction towards \"Openness\". This is done on purpose, because there can be compelling reasons not to make data \"Open\", such as privacy, other sensitive data, or intellectual property protection.\n"
"\n"
"The true goal of funding agencies is to create the maximum value for society from their investments. They therefore often add \"As open as possible, as closed as necessary\" to the requirements for funding."
msgstr ""
"FAIR 原則本身並不要求資料一定要「開放」。這樣設計是有原因的：有時確實有充分理由不能開放資料，例如隱私、其他敏感資料或智慧財產保護。\n"
"\n"
"資助機構真正想達成的目標，是讓投入的資源為社會創造最大價值。因此，它們常會在補助要求中加入「盡可能都開放，視需要再保留」的原則。"

#: answer/ca5c002d-fb3f-4873-bede-a8f304a3934f/advice
msgid "You will need to explain!"
msgstr "您需要說明原因！"

#: question/3f3e9c5a-c112-41a6-9084-62c1c266fed6/title
msgid "Will the data be accessible through a free and standardised access protocol?"
msgstr ""

#: question/3fafdd1e-79b3-4c25-93f4-a031437d5fea/title
msgid "What specific protocols will be used to provide access to the data?"
msgstr "會使用哪些具體協定讓他人取用資料？"

#: question/a549d10b-aa46-4c0c-863f-30219ac5ecce/title
msgid "Can all of your data become completely open over time?"
msgstr "隨著時間推移，您的所有資料是否將會完全公開？"

#: question/a549d10b-aa46-4c0c-863f-30219ac5ecce/text
msgid "Some data may be subject to a temporary embargo, or need to stay closed for specific reasons. "
msgstr "有些資料可能設有暫時性的延後開放期限，或基於特定理由而保持不公開。 "

#: question/c010e830-bd89-460d-9498-cb41e7ffeb87/title
msgid "Are there legal reasons why (some of your) data can not be completely open?"
msgstr "是否因為法律因素，使您（部分）的資料無法完全公開？"

#: question/019db0b3-9067-4134-8bfd-76db3cfc572a/title
msgid "Are there privacy reasons why your data can not be open?"
msgstr "是否因隱私因素使您的資料無法公開？"

#: question/754148c2-6019-4318-8d44-d73becc989f4/title
msgid "Are there restrictions on where the data need to be stored?"
msgstr "資料的儲存位置是否有任何限制？"

#: answer/2f0e4c16-be62-4836-aa0e-b52fd9132ac7/label
msgid "Yes, they must stay in the EU"
msgstr "是，資料必須留在歐盟境內"

#: answer/00bddac1-2375-4554-bb3c-27b261cc22e7/label
msgid "Yes, they must stay in the same country"
msgstr "是，資料必須留在同一國家境內"

#: answer/f6adfe7d-45f5-41a4-ba48-e43cc131c824/label
msgid "Yes, they must stay in the same institute"
msgstr "是，資料必須留在同一機構內"

#: question/a25b30f4-2d0f-4132-9b8e-0950f0b0ed66/title
msgid "Could pseudonymisation be used to make the data more openly available?"
msgstr ""

#: question/a25b30f4-2d0f-4132-9b8e-0950f0b0ed66/text
msgid "Legally, pseudonymous data (which means that someone has the key to reverse the process) is still considered privacy sensitive information. However, the EU is working on special cases where the data can still be opened as long as the key availability is sufficiently limited."
msgstr "從法律上而言，擬匿名化資料（亦即仍有人持有可逆轉處理過程之金鑰的資料）仍被視為涉及隱私的敏感資訊。不過，歐盟目前正研議特殊情況：只要金鑰的可取得性受到充分限制，這類資料仍可公開提供。"

#: question/5db6bd58-5d1d-4d02-9497-972cbef64c16/title
msgid "Can you make use of an existing 'trusted third party' for pseudonymisation?"
msgstr ""

#: question/5db6bd58-5d1d-4d02-9497-972cbef64c16/text
msgid "Making use of the same pseudonymisation for different studies makes it possible to integrate information later. Obviously it also raises the risk of re-identification."
msgstr ""

#: question/15ee1921-1fea-4f22-b462-b3cf7cdd4646/title
msgid "Could anonymisation be used to make the data more openly available?"
msgstr ""

#: question/15ee1921-1fea-4f22-b462-b3cf7cdd4646/text
msgid "Different anonymization techniques exist. Disadvantage of anonymization is that data integration becomes virtually impossible, but it may be the only way to open up your data for other research."
msgstr "現行有多種匿名化的方式。雖然匿名化的缺點是使得資料幾乎無法整合，但可能是將資料開放給其他研究使用的唯一方式。"

#: question/69be6695-152b-48ba-a1fd-6662476e39b7/title
msgid "Could you use data aggregation to make the data openly available?"
msgstr "您是否可以透過資料聚合 (data aggregation)，使資料更容易公開提供？"

#: question/69be6695-152b-48ba-a1fd-6662476e39b7/text
msgid "Aggregated data, where typically at least 15 individuals are in any data point, are considered sufficiently anonymous. This is an alternative way of making data openly available for future research."
msgstr "聚合資料通常被視為已充分匿名化；這類資料的每個資料點通常至少包含 15 個個體。這也是讓資料可供未來研究使用的另一種公開方式。"

#: question/ecca7dd6-62f2-4714-a85a-8d79bbca402a/title
msgid "Describe the procedure for users to access private data"
msgstr "請描述使用者取用非公開資料的程序"

#: question/ecca7dd6-62f2-4714-a85a-8d79bbca402a/text
msgid "Explain the procedure for authorized users to access private (e.g., personal) data (who is allowed to access it, what is required from them, etc.)."
msgstr "請說明獲得授權的使用者取用非公開資料（例如個人資料）的程序（像是哪些人可取用、需符合哪些條件等）。"

#: question/a18d79d2-74b1-4524-a3c7-2c1a87b66a75/title
msgid "Are there intellectual property reasons why your data can not be open?"
msgstr ""

#: question/b4f9916a-c846-49ff-bfd2-f5d1346de553/title
msgid "Is it clear who owns data and documents?"
msgstr "是否清楚誰擁有資料與文件？"

#: question/c9ed4379-19e2-4ce3-8962-5c2fca69b6cd/title
msgid "Will someone be given decision power to move documents or data to a new place after the project has finished?"
msgstr "計畫結束後，是否會有人被賦予決定權，可將文件或資料移至新的位置？"

#: question/c9ed4379-19e2-4ce3-8962-5c2fca69b6cd/text
msgid "In one case in the past, all documents that had been assembled by a project in a documentation system had to be deleted because not a single person could decide to move them to a new platform when the documentation system was going off-line."
msgstr "過去曾發生過這樣一個案例，某個計畫在一套文件系統中彙整的所有文件，最後都得刪除，因為當該文件系統即將下線時，竟沒有任何一個人有權決定將這些文件移轉到新的平台。"

#: question/55f03a4a-034b-422a-adf6-757416b7650a/title
msgid "Will you be allowing authenticated access to the data?"
msgstr "您是否會允許通過身分驗證後取用資料？"

#: question/baed9cce-91ab-45d0-a272-92246b2e6c72/title
msgid "Where will the data be stored?"
msgstr "資料會儲存在哪裡？"

#: answer/09f8f08d-04ae-463a-bbe0-f5ce05595777/label
msgid "In a domain repository (like EBI's and CRG's EGA) that arranges restricted access"
msgstr "在提供受限取用的特定領域資料儲存庫中，例如 EBI 與 CRG 的 EGA"

#: answer/46a96e04-4d2a-41e8-90e7-b6afa3f318fd/label
msgid "In a national or institutional repository that arranges restricted access"
msgstr "在提供受限取用的國家或機構資料儲存庫中"

#: answer/00e67874-dbe8-41a4-b9fc-0a4429765fce/label
msgid "In a dedicated repository"
msgstr "在專用資料儲存庫中"

#: answer/00e67874-dbe8-41a4-b9fc-0a4429765fce/advice
msgid "make sure you can guarantee longevity of this repository!"
msgstr "請務必確認您能保障此資料儲存庫的長期存續！"

#: question/278a8218-eb9f-43b4-8dac-cd6a644537fa/title
msgid "Who will take care of authentication of potential users?"
msgstr "誰會負責潛在使用者的身分驗證？"

#: answer/dc4e23fd-5477-41c8-919d-74df342f2d33/label
msgid "We will use username/password authentication, possibly augmented with two-factor security"
msgstr "我們會使用使用者名稱／密碼身分驗證，並可能加上雙因素身分驗證"

#: answer/0c05f134-b694-4697-9d72-750374da423c/label
msgid "We will use a single sign-on system such as edugain"
msgstr "我們會使用單一登入系統，例如 edugain"

#: answer/109e8083-1eb6-4b69-b7ae-32dab8b6a5f6/label
#: answer/f57960de-3cfb-47da-a30b-da7c5d27a38e/label
msgid "We will make other arrangements"
msgstr "我們會另作安排"

#: question/23909308-55cf-4e94-a616-2a74c809aa48/title
msgid "Who will take care of authorisation of potential users?"
msgstr ""

#: answer/ed47c9b7-9c2b-48ab-bdf4-efd8913f673e/label
msgid "One of the project members will authorise"
msgstr ""

#: answer/ed47c9b7-9c2b-48ab-bdf4-efd8913f673e/advice
msgid "It is not a good idea to tie this to a person"
msgstr "不建議將這項責任綁定在某一個人身上"

#: answer/ca3b6db3-cd6c-4139-8d24-e5ded15c2796/label
msgid "We will set up a data access committee"
msgstr "我們會成立資料取用委員會"

#: answer/d010e09e-8ce8-47c6-a1f9-f281519ba936/label
msgid "We will make use of an existing data access committee"
msgstr "我們將透過現有的資料存取委員會 (Data Access Committee) 來管理資料存取"

#: question/0de7232f-802d-4e1f-a84c-2895d08901ce/title
msgid "Which existing Data Access Committee?"
msgstr "是哪一個既有的資料取用委員會？"

#: question/c534c029-cb42-46a9-a118-87abfe3b54da/title
msgid "Are the criteria for application to access the data openly available?"
msgstr "申請資料取用的審查條件是否是公開的？"

#: question/b7cb192b-349a-4966-b37d-b63903bf2204/title
msgid "Has auditing for the re-use been arranged?"
msgstr "是否已安排再利用 (re-use) 的稽核機制？"

#: reference/ff3b29fc-fa24-4799-aa2c-29fabc5fc584/label
msgid "RDMkit on Sharing Human Data"
msgstr "RDMkit 中的人體資料共享"

#: question/85a9d872-3d41-4560-82c4-b850a6e2d5ac/title
msgid "Are there business reasons why (some of your) data can not be completely open?"
msgstr "是否有商業因素，使您（部分）的資料無法完全公開？"

#: answer/1c377b4c-bd6f-457e-8e7e-06efcd1b6444/label
msgid "Yes, patents still need to be applied for"
msgstr "是，仍需先申請專利"

#: answer/0cfc22ec-5551-4a37-84ec-308c85440af5/label
msgid "Yes, other business reasons"
msgstr "是，還有其他商業原因"

#: question/43370b85-0ee0-4f0f-b7de-9b04a54a2480/title
msgid "What other business reasons are there not to open all data immediately?"
msgstr "還有哪些商業原因使您無法立即開放所有資料？"

#: question/c10f9098-5b1c-4abc-adaa-bdef2fb537ca/title
msgid "Are there other reasons why (some of your) data can not be completely open?"
msgstr "是否有其他原因使您（部分）的資料無法完全公開？"

#: answer/cb052963-c573-4567-a462-4a5444a87808/label
msgid "Yes, papers need to be submitted first"
msgstr "是，論文需要先投稿"

#: answer/2b755a90-8a43-41c0-9020-5e2b9ca8f88e/label
msgid "Yes, other reasons"
msgstr "是，還有其他原因"

#: question/b289fdcc-aedc-496e-8169-e0bbe2346d1f/title
msgid "What other reasons are there not to open all data immediately?"
msgstr "還有哪些原因使您無法立即開放所有資料？"

#: question/f5c12fcf-15d0-44ba-a53c-49ea9d7f620f/title
msgid "Will you use temporary restrictions on the reuse of the data (embargo)?"
msgstr "您是否會設定資料限制期 (embargo)，暫時限制他人再利用資料？"

#: answer/d7a60a9d-75f6-4d0a-8a3d-0661d30f9a93/label
msgid "No, all data will be opened immediately"
msgstr "不會，所有資料都會立即開放"

#: answer/3da39a55-18e5-4b0a-8da1-5b7fc5260ad1/label
msgid "No, unrestricted data will be open immediately, restricted data will be indefinitely limited"
msgstr "不會，不受限制的資料會立即開放；受限制的資料則會無限期維持限制"

#: answer/82f84d7e-338c-46bc-9785-42df560c01ed/label
msgid "No, all data will be opened as soon as legal restrictions are falling away"
msgstr "不會，法律限制解除後，所有資料都會立即開放"

#: answer/1b120967-803b-458b-b565-dbee6a785509/label
msgid "Yes, data without legal restrictions will be released openly after a fixed time period"
msgstr "會，不受法律限制的資料會在固定期限後開放"

#: question/99a48a1a-5c27-4e15-9da0-515da815b4b8/title
msgid "What embargo period are you using?"
msgstr "延後開放期限為多久？"

#: question/99a48a1a-5c27-4e15-9da0-515da815b4b8/text
msgid "After what period will restrictions on the reuse of data (except ethical and legal restrictions) fall away?"
msgstr "除倫理與法律限制外，資料再次使用限制會在多久後解除？"

#: question/12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a/title
msgid "Will metadata be available openly?"
msgstr "後設資料是否會公開提供？"

#: question/12baa8af-db59-43a5-8ec7-0941c58ff89a/text
msgid "Horizon Europe demands that metadata is completely open, e.g. provided under a CC0 license, and that any deviation from this is clarified."
msgstr "Horizon Europe 要求後設資料必須完全開放，例如以 CC0 公眾領域貢獻宣告提供；若有任何偏離此原則的情況，請加以說明。"

#: question/6b5a6334-fbb3-4c88-995a-6d899e30da1e/title
msgid "Please explain why the metadata will not be openly available"
msgstr "請說明後設資料不會公開提供的原因"

#: question/26b2afa6-99e8-4337-b380-5642bc807ad8/title
msgid "Will metadata contain instructions how to get access to the data?"
msgstr "後設資料是否會包含如何取得資料的說明？"

#: question/1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57/title
msgid "Will the metadata be available in a form that can be harvested and indexed?"
msgstr "後設資料是否可供自動擷取並建立索引？"

#: question/1270ea5a-92a2-46ce-b658-9bf2862b9b57/text
msgid "Repositories often allow search engines and catalogues to index the metadata in an automated way. Will this be the case for your data?"
msgstr "資料儲存庫通常會允許搜尋引擎與目錄系統以自動化方式為其中的後設資料建立索引。您的資料也會是這種情況嗎？"

#: answer/6833a1fa-62fe-46b1-bb81-a3e42ff9626d/label
msgid "Yes, by the repository / repositories"
msgstr "是，由資料儲存庫提供"

#: answer/90bd5ae9-087f-429d-8e2a-d322078f1d20/label
msgid "Yes, we will take care of that"
msgstr "是，我們會負責讓後設資料可被自動擷取並建立索引"

#: chapter/70cc627a-779b-432e-b928-fd263f1ab24f/title
msgid "Other outputs"
msgstr "其他成果"

#: chapter/70cc627a-779b-432e-b928-fd263f1ab24f/text
msgid ""
"Projects may produce valuable outputs beyond datasets, such as software, workflows, protocols, documentation, training materials, ontologies, or metadata schemas.\n"
"\n"
"Use this section to describe which additional outputs will be preserved or shared, who may reuse them, and where they will be made available."
msgstr ""

#: question/eb698404-004a-4cdf-a599-be01e0eb7fd2/title
msgid "How do you decide which additional research outputs should be retained?"
msgstr "您如何決定哪些額外的研究成果需要保留？"

#: question/eb698404-004a-4cdf-a599-be01e0eb7fd2/text
msgid "This question refers to research outputs beyond datasets, such as code, documentation, lab protocols, questionnaires, reference data, software, or workflows. Please explain how you decide which of these outputs are important to keep, for example, because they are necessary for reproducibility, reuse by others, legal compliance, or future reference. You can also describe any criteria, policies, or team practices used to make these decisions."
msgstr ""

#: question/426bdcb5-d012-4f1d-b99e-36dc3efe6e50/title
msgid "Are there any other outputs of your project that might be valuable to some other entities (researchers, researcher groups, institutes)?"
msgstr "您的計畫成果是否可能對其他對象有再利用的價值（如研究人員、研究團隊或研究機構）？"

#: question/426bdcb5-d012-4f1d-b99e-36dc3efe6e50/text
msgid "Consider outputs beyond datasets and publications, such as software, workflows, protocols, ontologies, training materials, documentation, models, or curated reference resources."
msgstr ""

#: question/8df5fdb2-e358-4c27-bbe8-efdca150702b/title
msgid "Are there any software packages you will be publishing?"
msgstr ""

#: question/8df5fdb2-e358-4c27-bbe8-efdca150702b/text
msgid "Include software, scripts, pipelines, notebooks, APIs, plugins, or analysis tools developed or substantially modified within the project."
msgstr ""

#: question/1ae8d7b0-4bcd-4914-aaea-fa389fc056f4/title
msgid "Specify a list of software packages you will be publishing"
msgstr "請列出您將發布的軟體套件"

#: question/1024bb15-aaf5-4696-9b49-42898b72a16d/title
msgid "Software package:"
msgstr "軟體套件："

#: question/1024bb15-aaf5-4696-9b49-42898b72a16d/text
msgid "Provide a title or a name for the software you will be publishing."
msgstr ""

#: question/36938ca8-e22d-47a6-8859-a52f536101c5/title
msgid "Will you be adding an open-source licence?"
msgstr ""

#: question/36938ca8-e22d-47a6-8859-a52f536101c5/text
msgid "Specify whether the software will be distributed under a recognised open-source licence to clarify conditions for reuse, modification, and redistribution. Open Source licenses give a series of permissions (and guarantees) to users of your software. There are a number of different open source licences to choose from."
msgstr ""

#: question/0184bfcc-69ab-48c8-9d62-e23ae73a60be/title
msgid "What is the licence?"
msgstr ""

#: question/0184bfcc-69ab-48c8-9d62-e23ae73a60be/text
msgid "Choose from the predefined list of licenses. If you cannot find the one you need, please fill it in manually."
msgstr "請從預先定義的授權清單中選擇。若找不到所需的授權，請自行手動填寫。"

#: reference/250662f3-6a33-4dbf-8fb4-abb91be3314b/label
msgid "FAIRCookbook on Software Licensing"
msgstr "FAIRCookbook 的軟體授權頁面"

#: question/87b45400-169d-424d-8e71-d2034618dab5/title
msgid "Where will the software package be available?"
msgstr "這個軟體套件將在哪裡提供？"

#: question/87b45400-169d-424d-8e71-d2034618dab5/text
msgid "Specify where the software will be hosted or distributed, for example GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket, institutional repositories, Zenodo, or domain-specific repositories."
msgstr ""

#: question/3effd452-f0ae-4c25-b971-2b5762889ca4/title
msgid "Will this software be listed in a catalogue?"
msgstr "這個軟體套件是否會列入目錄？"

#: question/3effd452-f0ae-4c25-b971-2b5762889ca4/text
msgid "Examples include [Software Heritage](https://www.softwareheritage.org/), [bio.tools](http://bio.tools), institutional catalogues, EOSC catalogues, or domain-specific software registries."
msgstr ""

#: question/ee81402b-aefa-4cb6-9743-bb5de655e76d/title
msgid "Are there any other outputs of your project, besides software, that could be valuable to other entities (such as researchers, research groups, or institutes)?"
msgstr "除了軟體之外，您的計畫產出是否還有可能對其他對象有再利用的價值（如研究人員、研究團隊或研究機構）？"

#: question/ee81402b-aefa-4cb6-9743-bb5de655e76d/text
msgid ""
"Are there any other outputs of your project, besides software, that could be valuable to other entities (such as researchers, research groups, or institutes)?  \n"
"Examples may include workflows, protocols, training materials, documentation, ontologies, metadata schemas, curated collections, benchmarks, questionnaires, educational resources, or policy recommendations."
msgstr ""

#: question/82359337-0a92-4446-a7bb-dcf1c01a350a/title
msgid "What other outputs are there besides software?"
msgstr "除了軟體之外，還有哪些其他成果？"

#: question/88a92e66-ae03-485e-90f4-5c9d67970cd9/title
msgid "What is the output?"
msgstr "這項成果是什麼？"

#: question/88a92e66-ae03-485e-90f4-5c9d67970cd9/text
msgid "Provide the name or type of the output, for example “metadata schema”, “training manual”, “workflow documentation”, or “benchmark dataset description”."
msgstr ""

#: question/e1b36d54-c7b1-40ba-be4f-c96798fc8187/title
msgid "Why is it valuable?"
msgstr "這項成果為什麼有再次使用價值？"

#: question/e1b36d54-c7b1-40ba-be4f-c96798fc8187/text
msgid "Explain how the output may support reproducibility, interoperability, education, validation, standardisation, future research, or reuse by others."
msgstr ""

#: question/349c806a-6527-4d58-933a-dd53a31d831f/title
msgid "By whom it might be reused?"
msgstr "哪些對象可能會再次使用這項成果？"

#: question/349c806a-6527-4d58-933a-dd53a31d831f/text
msgid "Identify potential reusers such as researchers in the same field, interdisciplinary researchers, clinicians, industry partners, educators, policy makers, or infrastructure providers."
msgstr ""

#: question/04b92f1a-2045-475f-b988-5d2d397fcbe3/title
msgid "Is this output available?"
msgstr "這項成果是否可以取得？"

#: question/04b92f1a-2045-475f-b988-5d2d397fcbe3/text
msgid "Indicate whether the output is already publicly accessible, restricted, embargoed, or still under development."
msgstr ""

#: question/5cf47d97-d32f-4cb4-8fb3-49f3717f0980/text
msgid "Possible reasons include ongoing development, embargo periods, intellectual property restrictions, privacy or security concerns, contractual obligations, or lack of resources for publication."
msgstr ""

#: question/ee3c29ee-1b93-42c7-b369-69c5efdd75b7/title
msgid "Where is this output available?"
msgstr "這項成果可以在哪裡取得？"

#: question/ee3c29ee-1b93-42c7-b369-69c5efdd75b7/text
msgid "Provide a repository name, catalogue, persistent identifier (PID/DOI), institutional webpage, or another stable access location where the output can be accessed."
msgstr ""

#: metric/8db30660-d4e5-4c0a-bf3e-553f3f0f997a/title
msgid "Findability"
msgstr ""

#: metric/8db30660-d4e5-4c0a-bf3e-553f3f0f997a/abbreviation
msgid "F"
msgstr ""

#: metric/8db30660-d4e5-4c0a-bf3e-553f3f0f997a/description
msgid "The Findability metric describes how easily data can be located. The score associated with an answer will be higher if it makes it easier for humans or for computers to locate your data set, e.g. if it ends up in an index or has a unique resolvable identifier."
msgstr ""

#: metric/0feac7e6-add4-4723-abae-be5ce7864c63/title
msgid "Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: metric/0feac7e6-add4-4723-abae-be5ce7864c63/abbreviation
msgid "A"
msgstr ""

#: metric/0feac7e6-add4-4723-abae-be5ce7864c63/description
msgid "The Accessibility metric describes how well the access to the database is described and how easy it is to implement. The score associated with an answer will be higher if it makes it easier for humans and computers to get to the data. This is determined by e.g. the protocol for accessing the data or for authenticating users, and also by the guaranteed longevity of the repository. Note that this is different from the Openness metric!"
msgstr ""

#: metric/a42bded3-a085-45f8-b384-32b4a77c8385/title
msgid "Interoperability"
msgstr ""

#: metric/a42bded3-a085-45f8-b384-32b4a77c8385/abbreviation
msgid "I"
msgstr ""

#: metric/a42bded3-a085-45f8-b384-32b4a77c8385/description
msgid "The Interoperability metric describes how well the data interoperates with other data. The score associated with an answer will be higher if it makes it easier for humans and computers to couple the data with other data and 'understand' relationships. This is influenced by the use of standard ontologies for different fields and proper descriptions of the relations. It is also influenced by proper standard metadata that is agreed by the community."
msgstr ""

#: metric/0bafe0c2-a8f2-4c74-80c8-dbf3a5b8e9b7/title
msgid "Reusability"
msgstr ""

#: metric/0bafe0c2-a8f2-4c74-80c8-dbf3a5b8e9b7/abbreviation
msgid "R"
msgstr ""

#: metric/0bafe0c2-a8f2-4c74-80c8-dbf3a5b8e9b7/description
msgid "The Reusability metric describes how well the data is suitable for reuse in other context. The score associated with an answer will be higher if it makes it easier for humans and computers to reuse the data. This is influenced largely by proper description of how the data was obtained, and also by the conditions that are put on the reuse (license and, for personally identifying information, consent)."
msgstr ""

#: metric/8845fe2b-79df-4138-baea-3a035bf5e249/title
msgid "Good DMP Practice"
msgstr ""

#: metric/8845fe2b-79df-4138-baea-3a035bf5e249/abbreviation
msgid "G"
msgstr ""

#: metric/8845fe2b-79df-4138-baea-3a035bf5e249/description
msgid "The Good DMP Practice metric describes how appreciated a process is among Data Stewards. A score associated with an answer will be high if a practice would be considered preferable over alternatives, generally a good idea."
msgstr ""

#: metric/cc02c5a0-9754-4432-a7e0-ce0f3cf7a0a0/title
msgid "Openness"
msgstr ""

#: metric/cc02c5a0-9754-4432-a7e0-ce0f3cf7a0a0/abbreviation
msgid "O"
msgstr ""

#: metric/cc02c5a0-9754-4432-a7e0-ce0f3cf7a0a0/description
msgid "The Openness metric describes how Open the data are available. Note that this is different from the Accessibility metric. A score associated with an answer will be high if the data will be as open as possible, and low if voluntary restrictions apply to access and re-use."
msgstr ""

#: phase/b101f2d0-2476-452d-aa8d-95a41a02b52c/title
msgid "Before Submitting the Proposal"
msgstr ""

#: phase/b101f2d0-2476-452d-aa8d-95a41a02b52c/description
msgid "Some data stewardship issues already need to be addressed during the creation of a proposal for a research project. For example these could be questions that can have a significant impact on the budget or timeline of a project. Only such questions are labeled as \"desirable\" in this phase.\n"
msgstr ""

#: phase/1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e/title
msgid "Before Submitting the DMP"
msgstr ""

#: phase/1796fa3c-9f53-475f-89ff-c66a0453c42e/description
msgid "In many research projects, the finished data management plan is one of the early deliverables. Questions that should be addressed in those early months of the project are highlighted as desirable when this phase is selected."
msgstr ""

#: phase/adc9133d-afcd-4616-9aea-db5f475898a2/title
msgid "Before Finishing the Project"
msgstr ""

#: phase/adc9133d-afcd-4616-9aea-db5f475898a2/description
msgid "When a project rounds up, this means that all data has found its final spots. In this phase, questions that document the final state of affairs will be labeled as desirable.\n"
msgstr ""

#: phase/1ace0fc6-a949-495f-a32e-e948f3f6bed1/title
msgid "After Finishing the Project"
msgstr ""

#: phase/1ace0fc6-a949-495f-a32e-e948f3f6bed1/description
msgid "After a project is finished, the team conducts a comprehensive project review to evaluate its overall success and identify areas for future improvement and followup. Relevant feedback is gathered from stakeholders, and the team is finalizing reports and archiving project documentation. Finally, lessons learned are being documented for future reference. Questions relevant for these processes will be labeled as desirable in this phase."
msgstr ""

